hadiths[600]{hadithnumber,text}:
"3001","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from Ayyub, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The believer eats in one intestine, while the disbeliever eats in seven intestines. No one narrated this hadith from Ayyub except Mamar."
"3002","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from Ayyub, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no shighar in Islam. No one narrated this hadith from Ayyub except Mamar."
"3003","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from Thabit and Aban, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no shighar in Islam; and shighar is that a man offers his sister to a man without dowry. So there is no shighar in Islam, no jalab and no janab. No one narrated this hadith from Thabit except Mamar."
"3004","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever swears and says: If Allah wills, has not broken his oath. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Tawus except Mamar."
"3005","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq informed us, he said: Mamar informed us, he said: Ibn Jurayj informed me, he said: Ata ibn al-Saib informed me that Abdullah ibn Habib informed him, from Ali, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said regarding: And give them from the wealth of Allah which He has given you: a quarter of the contract of manumission. No one raised this hadith from Ata ibn al-Saib except Ibn Jurayj; Abd al-Razzaq is alone in transmitting it; and Abdullah ibn Habib is Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami."
"3006","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from Ashath ibn Abdullah, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man may do the deeds of the people of goodness for seventy years, then when he bequeaths he is unjust in his bequest, so his end is sealed with an evil deed and he enters the Fire; and a man may do the deeds of the people of evil for seventy years, then acts justly in his bequest, so his end is sealed with a good deed and he enters Paradise. Then Abu Hurayrah would say: Recite if you wish: These are the limits of Allah, up to: and for him is a humiliating punishment. No one narrated this hadith from Shahr ibn Hawshab except Ashath ibn Abdullah, and it is not narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except through the hadith of Ashath ibn Abdullah."
"3007","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from Uthman al-Jazari, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ransomed the captives of Badr, the ransom of each being four thousand, and killed Uqbah ibn Abi Muayt, killing him before the ransom. Ali ibn Abi Talib stood to him and killed him while captive. He said: Who will care for the children, O Muhammad? He said: The Fire. No one narrated this hadith from Uthman al-Jazari except Mamar."
"3008","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Yasin al-Zayyat, from Hammad ibn Abi Sulayman, from Ribi ibn Hirash, from Jarir ibn Abdullah who said: I performed ablution for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he wiped over his leather socks after Surat al-Maidah was revealed. No one narrated this hadith from Hammad ibn Abi Sulayman, from Ribi, except Yasin al-Zayyat; Abd al-Razzaq is alone in transmitting it; and Shubah narrated it from Hammad, from Ibrahim, from Hammam ibn al-Harith, from Jarir."
"3009","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, he said: al-Ashath informed me, from al-Hasan, from Abdullah ibn Mughaffal who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let none of you urinate in his bathing place then perform ablution in it, for most whisperings (waswasah) come from it. No one narrated this hadith from Ashath ibn Abdullah except Mamar."
"3010","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Muhammad ibn Rashid, from Khalid - meaning al-Hadhdha - from Qays ibn Abbad who said: I came to Madinah and entered the mosque for Asr prayer, advanced to the first row, then a man came, took my shoulder, moved me back and stood in my place after the imam had said takbir and I had said takbir. When we finished the prayer he turned to me and said: I only moved you back because the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us that the Muhajirun and Ansar pray in the first row; I knew you were not among them so I moved you back. I said: Who is this? They said: Ubayy ibn Kab. No one narrated this hadith from Khalid al-Hadhdha except Muhammad ibn Rashid; Abd al-Razzaq is alone in transmitting it."
"3011","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Yahya ibn al-Ala, from Layth, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Abu Umamah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to the people of Quba: What is this purification with which you have been distinguished in this verse: Wherein are men who love to purify themselves, and Allah loves those who purify themselves? They said: O Messenger of Allah, none of us leaves the privy without washing his seat. This hadith is not narrated from Abu Umamah except with this chain; Abd al-Razzaq is alone in transmitting it."
"3012","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq informed us, he said: Bishr ibn Rafi informed me, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Peace (al-salam) is a name among Allah's names, so spread it among yourselves. No one narrated this hadith from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir except Bishr ibn Rafi; Abd al-Razzaq is alone in transmitting it."
"3013","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Mamar informed us, from Uthman al-Jazari, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas who said: Hamzah was killed on the day of Uhud, and with him a man of the Ansar was killed. Safiyyah bint Abd al-Muttalib came with two garments to shroud Hamzah with them, but there was no shroud for the Ansari, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cast lots between the two garments, then shrouded each of them in one garment. No one narrated this hadith from Uthman al-Jazari except Mamar."
"3014","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq informed us, he said: Mamar informed us, from Said al-Jurayri, from Abdullah ibn Buraydah al-Aslami, from Abu al-Aswad al-Duali, from Abu Dharr who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best you change white hair with is henna and katam. No one narrated this hadith from Said al-Jurayri except Mamar."
"3015","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Qattan al-Misri narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, he said: Abu Ghassan Muhammad ibn Mutarrif narrated to us, he said: Zayd ibn Aslam narrated to me, from his father, from Umar ibn al-Khattab who said: Captives were brought to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); a woman among the captives rushed about, and when she found a boy among the captives she took him, pressed him to her belly and nursed him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do you think this woman would throw her child into the Fire? We said: No, by Allah, while she is able not to throw him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah is more merciful to His servants than this woman to her child. No one narrated it from Zayd ibn Aslam except Abu Ghassan, nor narrated it from Abu Ghassan except Ibn Abi Maryam, and it is not narrated from Umar except with this chain."
"3016","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Qattan narrated to us, he said: Yusuf ibn Adi narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Zakariyya ibn Abi Zaidah narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Firas, from al-Shabi, from al-Bara ibn Azib; and Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from al-Shabi, from al-Bara ibn Azib - each mentioning what the other did not mention - who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood on the day of sacrifice and said: Whoever faces our qiblah, prays our prayer, and performs our sacrifice rite, let him not slaughter until he prays. A man stood and said: O Messenger of Allah, this is a day when meat is disliked, and I hastened my sacrifice to feed my family, my household and my neighbors. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Repeat another sacrifice. He said: I have a young milch she-goat dearer to me than two meat sheep. He said: Slaughter it, for it is the best of your rites, but no sacrifice will suffice for anyone after you. No one narrated it from Sufyan except Ibn Abi Zaidah, nor narrated it except Yusuf ibn Adi."
"3017","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Qattan narrated to us, he said: Hamid ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, he said: Shayban Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, from Layth, from Mujahid, from al-Aswad, from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The jet-black dog is a devil. Mujahid narrated nothing from al-Aswad, from Aishah, besides this; none narrated it from him except Layth, nor from Layth except Shayban."
"3018","Ishaq ibn Khalawayh al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Bahr narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: Mamar informed us, from Abu Ishaq, from Asim ibn Damrah, from Ali who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is pleased that Allah extend his life, expand his provision, and avert from him an evil death, let him fear Allah and maintain kinship ties."
"3019","Ishaq ibn Khalawayh al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Bahr narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: Mamar informed us, he said: Thabit and Sulayman al-Taymi informed me, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked toward Iraq, Syria and Yemen and said: O Allah, turn their hearts toward Your obedience, and protect those behind them. No one narrated it from Sulayman al-Taymi except Mamar, nor narrated it from Mamar except Hisham ibn Yusuf, nor narrated it from Hisham except Ali ibn Bahr."
"3020","Ishaq ibn Khalawayh narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Bahr narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: Mamar narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left neither gold nor silver, neither sheep nor camel, and left only half of barley; we ate from it for a time, then I measured it and wished I had not measured it. No one narrated it from Hisham ibn Urwah except Mamar, nor from Mamar except Hisham ibn Yusuf, nor from Hisham except Ali ibn Bahr."
"3021","Ishaq ibn Khalawayh narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj al-Sami narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Habib and Hisham and Humayd, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: If a fly falls into the vessel of one of you, immerse it in it, for one of its wings is disease and the other is cure. No one narrated it from Hammad ibn Salamah, from Humayd, except Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj al-Sami."
"3022","Ishaq ibn Hajib al-Marwazi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyabi narrated to us, he said: my father narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Dhib, from Ibn Shihab, from al-Harith ibn al-Hakam, from Abu Amr ibn Himas - who had companionship - that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Women have no right to the middle of the road. No one narrated it from al-Zuhri except Ibn Abi Dhib."
"3023","Ishaq ibn Hajib al-Marwazi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyabi narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Nafi narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Sad, from Muadh ibn Abdullah ibn Khubayb al-Juhani, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a boy knows his right from his left, command him to pray. This is not narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except with this chain, and none narrated it from Hisham ibn Sad except Abdullah ibn Nafi."
"3024","Ishaq ibn Marwan al-Dahhan al-Baghdadi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Ala ibn Hammad al-Narsi narrated to us, he said: Wuhayb ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Ayyub, from al-Zuhri, from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, from his mother Umm Kulthum bint Uqbah ibn Abi Muayt who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: He is not a liar who reconciles between people, saying good or conveying good."
"3025","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Abi Hassan al-Anmati narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, he said: Ghalib al-Qattan narrated to us, from Bakr ibn Abdullah al-Muzani, from Ibn Umar who said: We used to say of the killer of a believer when he died that he is in the Fire, and we would say of one who committed a major sin and died upon it that he is in the Fire, until Allah sent down this verse: Allah does not forgive that partners be associated with Him, but forgives what is less than that. No one narrated it from Bakr al-Muzani except Ghalib al-Qattan, nor narrated it from Ghalib except Umar ibn al-Mughirah."
"3026","Ishaq ibn Abi Hassan al-Anmati narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Masruq al-Kindi narrated to us, he said: al-Walid ibn Abdullah ibn Jumay narrated to us, from Abu al-Tufayl, from Said ibn Zayd, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever takes a handspan of land unjustly will have it hung around him on the Day of Resurrection from seven earths. No one narrated it from Abu al-Tufayl except al-Walid ibn Jumay, nor narrated it from al-Walid except Muhammad ibn Masruq al-Kindi, and his son Thabit ibn al-Walid."
"3027","Ishaq ibn Dawud al-Sawwaf al-Tustari narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Ghaylan narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Bazi narrated to us, he said: Rawh ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, he said: Malik ibn Anas narrated to me, from al-Zuhri, from Abd al-Rahman al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The odor of the fasting person's mouth is sweeter to Allah than the scent of musk. It is not narrated from Malik except by this route."
"3028","Ishaq ibn Dawud al-Sawwaf narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Ghaylan narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Bazi narrated to us, from Sadaqah ibn Abi Imran, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from al-Shabi, from Urwah ibn Mudarris al-Tai who said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was at the standing place at Muzdalifah, and said: O Messenger of Allah, I came from the mountain of Tayyi; I exhausted myself and tired my mount; by Allah, I left no rope (path) without standing upon it. Do I have a Hajj, O Messenger of Allah? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever prayed with us this prayer, having come to Arafah by night or day, has completed his rites and his Hajj is complete. No one narrated it from Sadaqah ibn Abi Imran except Abdullah ibn Bazi."
"3029","Ishaq ibn Dawud al-Sawwaf narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Ghaylan narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Bazi narrated to us, from Sufyan ibn Uyaynah, from Mansur ibn al-Mutamir, from Ibrahim, from Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa al-Aslami who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I cannot learn the Quran; teach me what suffices me in prayer to say. He said: Say: Glory be to Allah, praise be to Allah, there is no god but Allah, Allah is Greatest, and there is no power nor strength except through Allah. He said: O Messenger of Allah, this is for Allah; what shall I say for myself? He said: Say: O Allah, forgive me, have mercy on me, guide me, grant me health, and provide for me. When the man turned away, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This one has attained all good - or: learned all good - or something like this. No one narrated it from Sufyan ibn Uyaynah, from Mansur, except Abdullah ibn Bazi; and this Ibrahim is Ibrahim al-Saksaki; it is not narrated from the hadith of Mansur except by this route."
"3030","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Abi al-Wars al-Ghazzi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi al-Sari al-Asqalani narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Mamar informed us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Said al-Khudri who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever sees me in a dream has truly seen me, for Satan does not take my likeness, nor that of the Kabah. No one narrated it from Zayd ibn Aslam except Mamar."
"3031","Ishaq ibn Muhammad al-Tahhan al-Kufi narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Abi Abd al-Rahman al-Asbaghi narrated to us, he said: Musab ibn Sallam narrated to us, from al-Zibriqan al-Sarraj, from Habib ibn Yasar, from Zayd ibn Arqam who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever does not trim his mustache is not of us."
"3032","Ishaq ibn Muhammad al-Tahhan narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Abi Abd al-Rahman al-Asbaghi narrated to us, he said: Musab ibn Sallam narrated to us, from al-Zibriqan, from Musa ibn Abi al-Mukhtar, from Bilal ibn Yahya, from Hudhayfah who said: No dwellings after dwellings that were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - through whom Allah averts affliction as He averts it from these dwellings - meaning Kufa. No one narrated these two hadiths from al-Zibriqan except Musab ibn Sallam."
"3033","Ishaq ibn Muhammad al-Khuzai al-Makki narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Said ibn Salim al-Qaddah narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Majid ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Rawwad narrated to us, from his father, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: We, the company of prophets, were commanded with three: hastening the breaking of the fast, delaying the pre-dawn meal, and placing the right hand over the left in prayer. It is not narrated from Ibn Umar except by this route."
"3034","Ishaq ibn Jamil al-Asbahani narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr ibn al-Abbas al-Bahili narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Malik ibn Amr, Abu Amir, narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Budayl al-Khuzai, from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Do not sever ties, do not turn away from one another, do not hate one another; be servants of Allah as brothers. It is not lawful for a Muslim to forsake his brother for more than three days. Thus Abdullah ibn Budayl ibn Warqa narrated it from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah, from Ibn Abbas. The companions of al-Zuhri narrated it from al-Zuhri, from Ata ibn Yazid, from Abu Ayyub, and from al-Zuhri, from Anas ibn Malik; if Abdullah ibn Budayl preserved it, it is a strange hadith, and it is not narrated from Ibn Abbas except by this route."
"3035","Ishaq ibn Muhammad al-Asbahani narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Saghani narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Ubaydah ibn Abdullah, from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Have mercy on those on earth, and the One in heaven will have mercy on you. No one narrated this hadith from al-Amash except Hafs ibn Ghiyath, nor from Hafs except Musa ibn Dawud; al-Saghani is alone in transmitting it."
"3036","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Raja al-Dawsi al-Anbari narrated to us, he said: Wahb ibn Baqiyyah al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn Abdullah narrated to us, from Humayd al-Tawil, from Bakr ibn Abdullah al-Muzani, from Aishah, may Allah be pleased with her, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to touch intimately while fasting; and which of you can control his desire as the Messenger (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) could control?"
"3037","Idris ibn Abd al-Karim al-Haddad narrated to us, he said: Asim ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Qays ibn al-Rabi narrated to us, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The first to be called to Paradise are those who praise Allah much, who praise Allah in ease and hardship. No one narrated it from Habib ibn Abi Thabit except Qays ibn al-Rabi, and Shubah ibn al-Hajjaj from the hadith of Nasr ibn Hammad al-Warraq."
"3038","Idris ibn Abd al-Karim al-Haddad narrated to us, he said: Asim ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Qays ibn al-Rabi narrated to us, from Abu Husayn, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Amr ibn Luhayy ibn Qamaah ibn Khindif."
"3039","Idris ibn Jafar al-Attar narrated to us, he said: Uthman ibn Umar ibn Faris narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Hassan narrated to us, from Ali ibn al-Hakam, from Ibrahim al-Nakhai, from Abu Abdullah al-Jadali, from Khuzaymah ibn Thabit, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: For the traveler three days and their nights, and for the resident a day and a night."
"3040","Ayyub ibn Abi Sulayman al-Suri Abu Maymun narrated to us, he said: Atiyyah ibn Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, he said: my father narrated to me, he said: Muhammad ibn Ziyad narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu Umamah say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: I am the foremost of the Arabs to Paradise, Suhayb is the foremost of the Romans to Paradise, Bilal is the foremost of the Ethiopians to Paradise, and Salman is the foremost of the Persians to Paradise."
"3041","Anas ibn Salm Abu Aqil al-Khawlani narrated to us, he said: Makhlad ibn Malik al-Harrani narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Ubaydullah, from Thumamah ibn Uqbah, from al-Harith ibn Suwayd, that he heard Abdullah ibn Masud say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whenever a man is among a people committing sins, more numerous and mightier than him, and they flatter him in his affair, Allah will punish them all. No one narrated this hadith from al-Harith ibn Suwayd except Thumamah ibn Uqbah, nor from Thumamah except Abd al-Aziz ibn Ubaydullah."
"3042","Anas ibn Salm al-Khawlani narrated to us, he said: Muallal ibn Nufayl al-Harrani narrated to us, he said: Attab ibn Bashir narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq, from his father, from al-Harith, from Ali who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he returned from a journey would pray two rakahs. This hadith is not narrated from Ali except with this chain; Muallal ibn Nufayl is alone in transmitting it."
"3043","Anas ibn Salm al-Khawlani narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Asbagh Abd al-Aziz ibn Yahya al-Harrani narrated to us, he said: Makhlad ibn Yazid narrated to us, from Aidh ibn Shurayh, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that when he said takbir he would raise his hands until level with his ears, saying: Glory be to You, O Allah, and with Your praise; blessed is Your name, exalted is Your grandeur, and there is no god besides You. This hadith is not narrated from Anas except with this chain; Makhlad ibn Yazid is alone in transmitting it."
"3044","Aban ibn Makhlad al-Asbahani narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Imran al-Asbahani narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Abd al-Rahman and Qurrah ibn Khalid and Harun ibn Ibrahim all narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us in one of the afternoon prayers - Zuhr or Asr - and gave salutation after two rakahs. The hasty people left, saying: The prayer has been shortened, the prayer has been shortened. Among the people were Abu Bakr and Umar, but they were too awed to speak to him. He stood to a piece of wood in the mosque upon which he used to place his hand, and a man called Dhu al-Yadayn, long of hands - the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to call him Dhu al-Yadayn - said to him: O Messenger of Allah, has the prayer been shortened or did you forget? He said: I did not forget nor was it shortened. He asked the people, and they said: Dhu al-Yadayn spoke the truth. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned and prayed two rakahs like his bowing or longer, then prostrated twice. No one narrated this hadith from Qurrah and Said brother of Abu Hurrah and Harun ibn Ibrahim except Abu Dawud, nor narrated it from Abu Dawud except Abdullah ibn Imran."
"3045","Aslam ibn Sahl al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Said ibn Bashir, from Aban ibn Taghlib, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever performs ablution after the ritual bath is not of us. No one narrated it from Aban ibn Taghlib except Said ibn Bashir, nor from Said except al-Walid; Sulayman ibn Ahmad is alone in transmitting it."
"3046","Aslam ibn Sahl narrated to us, he said: al-Qasim ibn Isa al-Ta'i narrated to us, he said: Rahmah ibn Mus'ab narrated to us, from Azrah ibn Thabit, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, who said: I saw Umar ibn al-Khattab kissing the Stone and saying: By Allah, I know well that you are a stone that neither harms nor benefits, and were it not that I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kissing you, I would not have kissed you."
"3047","Aslam ibn Sahl al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: al-Qasim ibn Isa narrated to us, he said: Rahmah ibn Mus'ab narrated to us, from Azrah ibn Thabit, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every Prophet has a supplication with which he supplicated and Allah answered him, and I have deferred my supplication as intercession for my ummah."
"3048","Aslam ibn Sahl narrated to us, he said: al-Qasim ibn Isa al-Ta'i narrated to us, he said: Rahmah ibn Mus'ab narrated to us, from Azrah ibn Thabit, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The people of Paradise will miss people whom they knew in this world, so they will come to the Prophets and mention them, and they will intercede for them and their intercession will be accepted, and it will be said to them: the freed ones; and all of them are freed ones; the water of life will be poured over them. No one narrated these three hadiths from Azrah ibn Thabit except Rahmah ibn Mus'ab; al-Qasim ibn Isa al-Ta'i is alone in transmitting them."
"3049","Aslam ibn Sahl al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Aban al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Ata narrated to us, from Hurayth ibn Abi Matar, from al-Sha'bi, from Ibn Abi al-Sanabil, from Fatimah bint Qays, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade wearing gold and stringing it, so a woman threw down a gold bracelet, and it remained in the mosque for days with no one taking it. No one narrated this hadith from al-Sha'bi except Hurayth, and no one narrated it from Hurayth except Yazid ibn Ata."
"3050","Aslam ibn Sahl al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Abu Kurayb narrated to us, he said: Waki' narrated to us, from al-Ala ibn Abd al-Karim, from al-Sha'bi, from Samurah ibn Jundub, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed, and when he finished he said: Is there anyone here from Banu Fulan? No one answered him. Then he said: Is there anyone here from Banu Fulan? No one answered him. Then he said: Is there anyone here from Banu Fulan? A man said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah, here is Fulan. He said: Your companion is detained at the gate of Paradise because of a debt upon him. A man said: His debt is upon me, O Messenger of Allah. No one narrated this hadith from al-Ala ibn Abd al-Karim except Waki', and no one narrated it from Waki' except Abu Kurayb, and we only wrote it from Aslam."
"3051","Aslam ibn Sahl narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Dawud ibn Thabit narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn Amr al-Umawi narrated to us, he said: Bassam al-Sayrafi narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sam, from Musa ibn Talhah, from Abu Dharr, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to fast the thirteenth, the fourteenth and the fifteenth of the month. No one narrated this hadith from Bassam except Khalid ibn Amr; Sulayman ibn Dawud ibn Thabit is alone in transmitting it."
"3052","Aslam ibn Sahl al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Muqaddam ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Ata narrated to us, he said: my uncle al-Qasim ibn Yahya narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from al-Zuhri, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a drink while a Bedouin was on his right and Abu Bakr was on his left, so he drank, and Umar said to him: O Messenger of Allah, give it to Abu Bakr, but he gave it to the Bedouin and said: Those on the right first. No one narrated this hadith from Ubaydullah ibn Umar except al-Qasim ibn Yahya; Muqaddam ibn Muhammad is alone in transmitting it."
"3053","Aslam ibn Sahl narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Sa'id ibn Yazid al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Rawh ibn Musafir narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from al-Sha'bi, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three will be given their reward on the Day of Resurrection twice: a man who had a slave woman and disciplined her well, then freed her and married her, so his reward is doubled; and an owned slave who fulfills the right of Allah and the right of his master, so his reward is doubled; and a man who believed in his Prophet, then met the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and believed in him and followed him, so his reward is doubled. No one narrated this hadith from al-A'mash except Rawh ibn Musafir; Ishaq ibn Sa'id is alone in transmitting it."
"3054","Aslam ibn Sahl al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ali al-Shaybani al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Hakam ibn Mansur narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from al-Hasan, from Abu Bakrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: This son of mine is a chief, and Allah will bring reconciliation through him between two factions of the Muslims, meaning al-Hasan ibn Ali. No one transmitted this hadith well from Dawud ibn Abi Hind except Abd al-Hakam ibn Mansur."
"3055","Al-Ahwas ibn al-Mufaddal ibn Ghassan al-Ghallabi narrated to us, he said: my father narrated to us, he said: Rawh ibn Aslam narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Bakr al-Muzani narrated to us, he said: Humayd ibn Hilal narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn al-Samit narrated to me, from Abu Dharr, who said: I prayed three years before I heard of Islam. I said: O Abu Dharr, in which direction did you turn? He said: I turned wherever Allah directed me; I would pray from the beginning of the night, and when the end of the night came I would fall down as if I were a lifeless heap until the sun rose over me. He said: Ghifar violated the sacred month, so I set out with my brother Unays and we believed, and we stayed with a maternal uncle of ours. Our uncle heard that my brother visited his household, and he mentioned that, so I said: We have no staying with you. So we departed, and he kept covering his head and weeping in grief over us. We camped near Makkah, and my brother challenged a poet over his flock: whichever of them was the better poet would take the other's flock. We went to a soothsayer, and the soothsayer said to Unays: I have judged for you before judging for you, so he took the poet's flock. He camped near Makkah and said to Abu Dharr: Guard my need and I will guard your flock. When he came to Makkah he heard of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and what they said about him, so he fulfilled his need and returned to his brother and said: O my brother, I saw a man in Makkah calling to the God you worship. Abu Dharr said: O my brother, what do the people say? He said: They say: madman, and they say: poet, and they say: soothsayer. I compared his words to the measures of the poets, and by Allah he is no poet, and I heard the words of the soothsayers, and by Allah he is no soothsayer, nor by Allah is he mad. I said: O my brother, what do you say? He said: I say he is truthful and they are liars. He said: I said: I wish to meet him. He said: O my brother, the people are hostile to him and have turned harsh against him; when you arrive, ask about the Sabian. When I arrived in Makkah I saw a man whom my eye overlooked, and I said: Where is this Sabian? He called out: A Sabian, a Sabian. People came out from every valley and pelted me with every stone and clod until they left me like a red heap. They dispersed from me, and I came to Zamzam, washed the blood off me, and entered between the Ka'bah and its curtains. I stayed thirty days and nights with no food except the water of Zamzam, until Allah sealed the ears of the people of Makkah so that I saw no one circumambulating the House except two women, who passed by me saying: Isaf and Na'ilah. I said: Marry one of them to the other with a phallus of wood. He said: O son of my brother, and he mentioned a word, so they turned away saying: The Sabian is between the Ka'bah and its curtains; by Allah, if only one of our men were here. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and Abu Bakr entered and they met them, and they said: What is this noise? They said: The Sabian is between the Ka'bah and its curtains. They said: What does he say? They said: He says a word that fills our mouths. They came, touched the Stone, circumambulated seven times, then prayed two rak'ahs. He said: I recognized Islam, and I recognized the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) by Abu Bakr putting him forward. I came to them and said: Peace be upon you, O Messenger of Allah, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. He said: And upon you, and the mercy of Allah; and upon you, and the mercy of Allah; and upon you, and the mercy of Allah, three times. Then he said: From where are you? I said: I am from Ghifar. He placed his hand on his forehead. I went to take it, and Abu Bakr said: Do not be hasty. Then he raised his head to me and said: How long have you been here? I said: For thirty days and nights. He said: What is your food? I said: I have no food except the water of Zamzam, and the folds of my belly have cracked, and I have found no faintness of hunger upon my liver. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is blessed; it is nourishing food; it is blessed; it is nourishing food; it is blessed; it is nourishing food. Abu Bakr said: O Messenger of Allah, permit me to present him a gift tonight. He permitted him, and he went to a house, entered it, opened a door, and scooped for us handfuls of Ta'ifi raisins. That was the first food I ate in Makkah until I left it. He said to me: I have been commanded to emigrate to a land of palm trees, and I do not think it is but Yathrib; so go, for you are the messenger of the Messenger of Allah to your people. When I came to my brother he said: O my brother, what have you brought us? I said: I met him, accepted Islam, pledged allegiance, and I invite my brother to Islam. He said: And I have accepted Islam and pledged allegiance. We came to our mother and invited her to Islam, and she said: I have no aversion to your religion, and I have accepted Islam and pledged allegiance. Then we departed and came to our people and invited them to Islam; half of them accepted, and their chief Ima ibn Rahadah accepted, and he led them in prayer. The remaining half said: Leave us until the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passes by us. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by them, and the remaining half accepted. Aslam said: We accept Islam upon what Ghifar accepted. So they accepted, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Aslam, may Allah grant it peace, and Ghifar, may Allah forgive it. No one narrated this hadith from Abdullah ibn Bakr ibn Abdullah al-Muzani except Rawh ibn Aslam, and no one narrated it from Rawh ibn Aslam except al-Mufaddal ibn Ghassan al-Ghallabi and Hajjaj ibn al-Sha'ir."
"3056","Azhar ibn Zufar al-Misri narrated to us, he said: Abu Aslam Muhammad ibn Makhlad al-Ru'ayni narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Abi Karimah narrated to us, from Makhul, from Qaza'ah ibn Yahya, from Habib ibn Maslamah al-Fihri, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Visit occasionally and love will increase. No one narrated this hadith from Makhul except Sulayman ibn Abi Karimah, and no one narrated it from Sulayman except Muhammad ibn Makhlad; Azhar ibn Zufar is alone in transmitting it."
"3057","Azhar ibn Zufar narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Makhlad al-Ru'ayni Abu Aslam narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Zayd ibn Aslam narrated to us, from his father, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about the companions of the Heights, and he said: A people killed in the path of Allah while disobedient to their parents; martyrdom prevented them from entering the Fire, and disobedience prevented them from entering Paradise, so they stand upon a wall between Paradise and Hell until their fat melts and their flesh withers, until Allah finishes the reckoning of creation; and when He finishes the reckoning of creation He enfolds them in mercy from Him and they are admitted to Paradise. No one narrated this hadith from Zayd ibn Aslam except his son Abd al-Rahman, and no one narrated it from Abd al-Rahman except Muhammad ibn Makhlad, and it is not narrated from Abu Sa'id except with this chain."
"3058","Al-Aswad ibn Marwan al-Maqaddi narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Dimashqi narrated to us, he said: Sa'dan ibn Yahya narrated to us, from Sadaqah ibn Abi Imran, from Sulayman al-Kahili, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The imam is a guarantor and the muezzin is trusted. O Allah, guide the imams and forgive the muezzins."
"3059","Al-Aswad ibn Marwan narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, he said: Sa'dan ibn Yahya narrated to us, from Sadaqah ibn Abi Imran, from Abu Ya'fur, from Mus'ab ibn Sa'd, who said: I prayed and joined my hands together, and my father forbade me and said: We used to do it, then we were commanded to place the hands on the knees. No one narrated these two hadiths from Sadaqah ibn Abi Imran except Sa'dan ibn Yahya; Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman is alone in transmitting them."
"3060","Usamah ibn Ahmad al-Tujibi al-Misri narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Tahir ibn al-Sarh narrated to us, he said: Bakr ibn Sulaym narrated to us, from Abu Hazim, from Sahl ibn Sa'd al-Sa'idi, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Islam began as something strange and will return as something strange as it began, so glad tidings to the strangers. It was said: And who are the strangers? He said: Those who set things right when people have become corrupt."
"3061","Bishr ibn Musa ibn Salih ibn Shaykh ibn Umayrah al-Asadi narrated to us, he said: Mansur ibn Suqayr narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn A'yan narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man may be among the people of prayer, zakah, hajj, umrah and jihad, until he mentioned the arrows of good, yet on the Day of Resurrection he will only be recompensed according to his intellect. No one narrated this hadith from Ubaydullah ibn Umar except Musa ibn A'yan; Mansur ibn Suqayr is alone in transmitting it."
"3062","Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Khallad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him not harm his neighbor; and whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him speak good or remain silent; and whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him honor his guest. They said: O Messenger of Allah, what is honoring him? He said: His due hospitality is three nights; whatever is beyond that is charity. No one narrated this hadith from Zayd ibn Aslam except Hisham ibn Sa'd; Khallad ibn Yahya is alone in transmitting it."
"3063","Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Ishaq al-Saylahini narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Abdullah ibn Rabah, from Abu Qatadah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Abu Bakr: When do you pray witr? He said: I pray witr at the beginning of the night. And he said to Umar: When do you pray witr? He said: I pray witr at the end of the night. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Abu Bakr has taken the cautious course, and he said to Umar: He has taken the strong course. No one transmitted this hadith well from Hammad ibn Salamah except Yahya ibn Ishaq."
"3064","Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Samad ibn Hassan al-Marrudhi narrated to us, he said: Kharijah ibn Mus'ab narrated to us, from Mansur, from Rib'i ibn Hirash, from al-Ma'rur ibn Suwayd, from Abu Dharr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah Almighty says: Son of Adam, if you do nearly the earth full of sins and do not associate anything with Me, I will grant you nearly the earth full of forgiveness. No one narrated it from Kharijah except Abd al-Samad ibn Hassan."
"3065","Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Samad ibn Hassan narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Hamzah, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, that he said: Seeking permission is part of announcing death, and announcing death is from the affair of Jahiliyyah. No one transmitted it well from Sufyan except Abd al-Samad."
"3066","Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Ishaq al-Saylahini narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us, from Asim, from Abu Abd al-Rahman, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, in a raised report, that he said: The best of you is he who reads the Qur'an and teaches it. No one narrated it from Asim except Sharik."
"3067","Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Hubayrah, from Hassan ibn Kurayb, that a boy of theirs died and his father grieved intensely over him, so a man from the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called Hawshab said: Shall I not tell you of a like case I witnessed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: There was a man who used to come to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with his son, then he stayed away from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for days. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What has happened to Fulan? They said: His son who used to come with him has died. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) met him and said: O Fulan, would it please you that your son be with you as the most active of lads in vigor? Would it please you, O Fulan, that your son be an elder like the best of elders? Or that it be said to you: Enter Paradise as reward for what was taken from you? Hawshab ascribed no hadith from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) other than this."
"3068","Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Ishaq al-Saylahini narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Wasil, the freedman of Abu Uyaynah, from Yahya ibn Ubayd, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would withdraw for urination as he would withdraw for lodging. No one narrated this hadith from Wasil, the freedman of Abu Uyaynah, except Sa'id ibn Zayd; and Yahya is Yahya ibn Ubayd ibn Dujayy; Ubayd ibn Dujayy ascribed from Abu Hurayrah no hadith except this one."
"3069","Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Dawud al-Dabbi narrated to us, he said: Uqbah ibn Abdullah al-Rifa'i narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Buraydah, from his father, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not go out on the day of Fitr until he ate, and he would not eat on the day of sacrifice until he returned and ate from his slaughtered animal. No one narrated this hadith from Abdullah ibn Buraydah except Uqbah ibn Abdullah and Thawwab ibn Utbah al-Mahri."
"3070","Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Dawud narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn al-Mu'ammal narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from A'ishah, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: O A'ishah, the swiftest of people to perish are your people. I said: From Taym, may Allah make me your ransom? He said: No, but this clan of Quraysh; deaths will consume them swiftly, and people will envy them. I said: What will remain of people after them? He said: They are the backbone of people; when they perish, people perish. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Abi Mulaykah except Abdullah ibn al-Mu'ammal."
"3071","Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hussam ibn Misakk narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Qasim, from Zayd ibn Arqam, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered the mosque of Quba and saw them praying Duha, and said: This is the prayer of the oft-returning. He said: And they used to pray it when the young camels felt the heat of the sun. No one narrated this hadith from Hussam ibn Misakk except Musa ibn Dawud."
"3072","Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Ishaq al-Saylahini narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us, from Mikhwal, from Muslim al-Batin, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray witr with three rak'ahs: reciting in the first Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High, in the second Say, O disbelievers, and in the third Say, He is Allah, the One. No one narrated this hadith from Mikhwal except Sharik."
"3073","Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri narrated to us, he said: I heard Ibn Awn narrating from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: It was forbidden, or he was forbidden, that a man urinate in standing or stagnant water and then perform ablution from it or bathe from it. No one transmitted it well from Ibn Awn except al-Muqri."
"3074","Bishr ibn Ali ibn Bishr al-Ijli al-Ammi al-Antaki narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Nasr al-Antaki narrated to us: Ishaq ibn Isa ibn al-Tabba' narrated to us, from Malik ibn Anas, from Ziyad ibn Mikhraq, from Mu'awiyah ibn Qurrah, from his father, who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, I slaughter a sheep while I pity it. He said: And for the sheep, if you show it mercy, Allah will show you mercy. No one narrated this hadith from Malik except Ishaq ibn Isa; Abdullah ibn Nasr is alone in transmitting it."
"3075","Bishr ibn Ali ibn Bishr al-Ijli narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Sallam al-Manbiji narrated to us, he said: al-Waddah ibn Abbad al-Kufi narrated to us, from Asim al-Ahwal, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: I went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on one of the nights, carrying his purification water, when he heard a caller. He said: O Anas, pour it out. He said: O Allah, help me in what will save me from what You have frightened me of. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If only he would say its sister. It was as if the man understood what the Messenger of Allah intended, so he said: And grant me the longing of the truthful for what You have made them long for. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Quick, O Anas, put down the purification water and go to this caller and tell him to supplicate for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that He help him in what He sent him with, and to supplicate for his ummah that they take what their Prophet brought them in truth. I came to him and said: Supplicate for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that Allah help him in what He sent him with, and supplicate for his ummah that they take what their Prophet brought them in truth. He said: And who sent you? I disliked telling him, and I had not sought permission from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so I said: What harm is it to you, may Allah have mercy on you, in what I asked of you? He said: Will you not tell me who sent you? So I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and told him what he said. He said: Tell him: I am the messenger of the Messenger of Allah. He said to me: Welcome to the Messenger of Allah, and welcome to his messenger; I was more deserving of coming to him. Convey peace to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from me, and tell him: Al-Khadir conveys peace to you, and says to you: Allah has favored you over the Prophets as He favored the month of Ramadan over the rest of the months, and He favored your ummah over the nations as He favored Friday over the rest of the days. When I turned away from him, I heard him saying: O Allah, make me of this ummah, the shown mercy, the guided, the oft-repented upon. No one narrated this hadith from Anas except Asim al-Ahwal, and no one narrated it from Asim except al-Waddah ibn Abbad; Muhammad ibn Sallam is alone in transmitting it."
"3076","Bishr ibn Musa al-Ghazzi narrated to us, he said: Ayyub ibn Ali ibn al-Haysam narrated to us, he said: Ziyad ibn Sayyar narrated to us, from Azzah bint Iyad, from Abu Qirsafah, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: May Allah brighten a servant who hears my words, grasps them and preserves them; for many a carrier of knowledge conveys it to one more knowledgeable than he. Three things over which the heart harbors no malice: sincerity of deed for Allah, sincere advice to the rulers, and adherence to the community."
"3077","Bakr ibn Sahl al-Dimyati narrated to us, he said: Shu'ayb ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, from Amr ibn al-Harith, from Mujammi' ibn Ka'b, from Maslamah ibn Mukhallad, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Leave women without adornment and they will keep to the seclusion of chambers. No one narrated it from Amr ibn al-Harith except Yahya ibn Ayyub, and no one narrated it from Yahya except Shu'ayb ibn Yahya, and it is not narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except with this chain."
"3078","Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Hashim narrated to us, he said: Hiql narrated to us, from al-Awza'i, he said: Amr ibn Qays narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever among you comes to Friday prayer, let him bathe. No one narrated it from al-Awza'i except Hiql, and no one narrated it from Hiql except Amr ibn Hashim; Bakr ibn Sahl is alone in transmitting it."
"3079","Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Hashim narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Awza'i narrating from Hassan ibn Atiyyah, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever swears an oath and makes an exception, then breaks it afterwards, there is no expiation upon him. No one narrated it from al-Awza'i except Amr ibn Hashim."
"3080","Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Uqayl ibn Khalid, from Ibn Shihab, that Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Bakr informed him, that Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman informed him, that Abu Dharr informed him, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The Hour will not come until Luka' ibn Luka' prevails over the world, and the best of people is a believer between two noble ones. No one narrated it from al-Zuhri except Uqayl, and no one narrated it from Uqayl except Ibn Lahi'ah; Abdullah ibn Yusuf is alone in transmitting it, and it is not narrated from Abu Dharr except from this route."
"3081","Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, he said: Shu'ayb ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Jabbar ibn Umar narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about a mouse that fell into ghee, and he said: Throw it away with what is around it and eat it, if it is solid. They said: O Messenger of Allah, what if it is liquid? He said: Make use of it. Thus Abd al-Jabbar ibn Umar narrated it from Ibn Jurayj, from Ibn Shihab, from Salim, from his father; and Ma'mar narrated it from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab, from Abu Hurayrah; and the companions of al-Zuhri narrated it from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah, from Ibn Abbas."
"3082","Bakr ibn Sahl al-Dimyati narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Shurayh Abu Shurayh al-Ma'afiri narrated to us, that he heard Sahl ibn Abi Umamah ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf narrating from his father, from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not be harsh upon yourselves, for those before you perished only through their harshness upon themselves, and you will find their remnants in monasteries and cloisters."
"3083","Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: Abu Shurayh Abd al-Rahman ibn Shurayh narrated to us, that he heard Sahl ibn Abi Umamah ibn Sahl narrating from his father, from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever asks Allah for martyrdom truthfully from his heart, Allah will raise him to the ranks of the martyrs even if he dies on his bed. These two hadiths are not narrated from Sahl ibn Hunayf except with this chain."
"3084","Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, he said: Shu'ayb ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: al-Layth ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Hurmuz al-A'raj, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: If his neighbor asks him to fix a plank of wood in his wall, let him not refuse him. Thus Shu'ayb ibn Yahya narrated it from al-Layth."
"3085","Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, he said: Mahdi ibn Ja'far al-Ramli narrated to us, he said: al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, he said: Abd al-A'la ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Farwah narrated to us, from Ishaq ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Talhah, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a newly built dome of a man of the Ansar and said: What is this? He said: A dome. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every building, and he gestured with his hand thus over his head, larger than this, is a calamity upon its owner on the Day of Resurrection. No one narrated this hadith from Ishaq ibn Abdullah except Abd al-A'la ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Farwah; al-Walid is alone in transmitting it."
"3086","Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Abi al-Fayyad al-Barqi narrated to us, he said: Ashhab ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, from Ibn Lahi'ah, from Mishrah ibn Ha'an, from Uqbah ibn Amir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever acts with deliberation hits the mark, or nearly does, and whoever hastens errs, or nearly does. No one narrated this hadith from Uqbah ibn Amir except Mishrah, and no one narrated it from Mishrah except Ibn Lahi'ah, and no one narrated it from Ibn Lahi'ah except Ashhab; Ibrahim ibn Abi al-Fayyad is alone in transmitting it."
"3087","Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: al-Haytham ibn Humayd narrated to us, he said: al-Nu'man ibn al-Mundhir informed us, from Makhul, from Anbasah ibn Abi Sufyan, from Umm Habibah, that she informed him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever guards four rak'ahs before the midday prayer and four after it, Allah will forbid him to the Fire. No one narrated this hadith from al-Nu'man ibn al-Mundhir except al-Haytham ibn Humayd and Yahya ibn Hamzah."
"3088","Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: al-Haytham ibn Humayd narrated to us, from al-Ala ibn al-Harith, from Makhul, from Anbasah ibn Abi Sufyan, from Umm Habibah, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever touches his private part, let him perform ablution. No one narrated this hadith from Makhul except al-Ala ibn al-Harith, and it is not narrated from Umm Habibah except with this chain."
"3089","Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: al-Haytham ibn Humayd narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'id informed me, from Sulayman ibn Musa, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was shrouded in three white Sahuli garments. No one narrated this hadith from Nafi' except Sulayman ibn Musa, and no one narrated it from Sulayman except Abu Mu'id."
"3090","Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: al-Layth ibn Sa'd narrated to me, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Abi Ja'far narrated to me, from Abu al-Aswad, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Amrah, from A'ishah, that she said concerning the meats of the sacrifices: We used to preserve some of it, and people would come with it to Madinah, and they would eat it only for three days; it was not a binding command, but he intended that they eat of it. No one narrated it from Yahya ibn Sa'id except Hisham ibn Urwah, and no one narrated it from al-Layth ibn Sa'd except Abdullah ibn Salih."
"3091","Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi al-Sari narrated to us, he said: Ata ibn Muslim al-Khaffaf narrated to us, from Ja'far ibn Burqan, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, from al-Fadl ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said in the illness in which he died: Bind my head; perhaps I may go out to the mosque. So I bound his head with a yellow band, then he went out to the mosque supported between two men. No one narrated this hadith from Ja'far except Ata."
"3092","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi al-Sari narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Ma'mar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Good is tied to the forelocks of horses until the Day of Resurrection, and the one who spends on horses is like one who stretches his hand with spending and does not withhold it. No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except Ma'mar; Abd al-Razzaq is alone in transmitting it."
"3093","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Sulayman ibn Yusuf al-Abdi narrated to us, he said: Layth ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Abu al-Khayr, from Uqbah ibn Amir al-Juhani, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When I was taken up to the lowest heaven I entered the Garden of Eden, and an apple fell into my hand; when I placed it in my hands it split open upon a wide-eyed houri, pleasing, the lashes of her eye like the front feathers of eagles' wings. I said to her: Who are you? She said: I am for the caliph after you. No one narrated this hadith from al-Layth except Abdullah."
"3094","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Mahdi ibn Ja'far al-Ramli narrated to us, he said: Rawwad ibn al-Jarrah narrated to us, from Abu al-Hasan al-Hanzali, from Bukayr ibn Shihab al-Damaghanai, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to us saying: Seek refuge with Allah from the pit of sorrow. They said: O Messenger of Allah, what is the pit of sorrow? He said: A pit in a valley in the bottom of Hell, from which Hell itself seeks refuge every day four hundred times; Allah has prepared it for the reciters who show off with their deeds, and the most hateful of creation to Allah Almighty is a reciter who visits the officials. Bukayr ibn Shihab narrated from Ibn Sirin no hadith except this one."
"3095","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Hashim al-Bayruti narrated to us, he said: Abdah ibn Sulayman al-Kilabi narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Abi Arubah, from Amir ibn Abd al-Wahid al-Ahwal, from Makhul, from Abdullah ibn Muhayriz, from Abu Mahdhurah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) taught me the adhan as nineteen phrases and the iqamah as seventeen phrases. No one narrated this hadith from Sa'id except Abdah; Amr is alone in transmitting it."
"3096","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Mahdi ibn Ja'far al-Ramli narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Yazid al-Iskandarani narrated to us, from Haywah ibn Shurayh, from Abu Sakhr, from Yazid ibn Abdullah ibn Qusayt, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no one who sends peace upon me except that Allah returns my soul to me so that I return peace upon him. No one narrated this hadith from Yazid except Abu Sakhr, and no one narrated it from Abu Sakhr except Haywah; Abdullah ibn Yazid is alone in transmitting it."
"3097","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi al-Sari al-Asqalani narrated to us, he said: Rishdin ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Umar, the freedman of Ghufrah, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli, from Abdullah ibn Amr, who said: They said: O Messenger of Allah, the muezzins excel us. He said: Say as the muezzin says, and when you finish, ask and you will be given. No one narrated this hadith from Umar, the freedman of Ghufrah, except Rishdin."
"3098","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Hashim al-Bayruti narrated to us, from al-Awza'i, he said: Sulayman ibn Habib al-Muharibi narrated to me, from Abu Umamah al-Bahili, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three things: whoever has one of them is under Allah's guarantee: whoever goes out in the path of Allah is under Allah's guarantee; if He takes his soul He admits him to Paradise, and if He returns him to his family it is with what he obtained of reward and booty; and a man who is in the mosque is under guarantee; if He takes his soul He admits him to Paradise, and if He returns him to his family it is with what he obtained of reward and booty; and a man who enters his house to sleep is under Allah's guarantee. No one narrated this hadith from Sulayman ibn Habib except al-Awza'i."
"3099","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Hashim al-Bayruti narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Sulayman ibn Abi al-Jawn al-Ansi narrated to us, from Abbad ibn Kathir al-Basri, from Abu Ubaydah, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever prays the prayer at its time, performs its ablution fully, completes its standing, humility, bowing and prostration, it goes forth white and radiant, saying: May Allah preserve you as you preserved me; and whoever prays the prayer outside its time, does not perform its ablution fully, nor complete its humility, bowing or prostration, it goes forth black and dark, saying: May Allah waste you as you wasted me, until when it is where Allah wills it is folded as a worn garment is folded, then his face is struck with it. No one narrated this hadith from Humayd al-Tawil, from Anas, except Abbad ibn Kathir; Abd al-Rahman ibn Sulayman is alone in transmitting it; and Abu Ubaydah is Humayd al-Tawil."
"3100","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Hashim narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Shu'ayb ibn Shabur narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn al-Harith al-Dhimari narrated to me, from Ali ibn Yazid, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah al-Bahili, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever says in the morning three times: O Allah, to You is praise; there is no god but You; You are my Lord and I am Your servant; I have believed in You devoting my religion to You; I enter the morning upon Your covenant and Your promise as much as I can; I repent to You from the evil of my deed, and I seek Your forgiveness for my sins which none forgives but You; then if he dies that day he enters Paradise; and if he says in the evening three times: O Allah, to You is praise; there is no god but You; You are my Lord and I am Your servant; I enter the evening upon Your covenant and Your promise as much as I can; I repent to You from the evil of my deed, and I seek Your forgiveness for my sins which none forgives but You; and dies that night, he enters Paradise. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would swear what he would not swear over other than it, saying: By Allah, no servant says it in a day in the morning and dies that day except that he enters Paradise, and if he says it in the evening and dies that night he enters Paradise. No one narrated this hadith from Yahya ibn al-Harith except Muhammad ibn Shu'ayb; Amr ibn Hashim is alone in transmitting it."
"3101","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, he said: Hilal ibn Amir narrated to us, from his father, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressing the people at Mina upon a mule, wearing a green cloak, with a man of the people of Badr before him expressing from him; I came until I put my hand between his feet and his sandal straps, and I kept marveling at its coolness. Amir Abu Hilal narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) no hadith other than this."
"3102","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from Hajjaj ibn Artah, from al-Hakam ibn Utaybah, from Yahya ibn al-Jazzar, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed in an open space with nothing before him. No one narrated this hadith from al-Hakam, from Yahya ibn al-Jazzar, except al-Hajjaj. And Huraym ibn Sufyan narrated it from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas; and Isma'il ibn Muslim narrated it from al-Hakam, from Mujahid."
"3103","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: Abu Bahriyyah narrated to us, from Abu Bakr al-Hudhali, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Tamim al-Dari, who said: They said: O Messenger of Allah, people love the humps of camels and the tails of sheep while they are alive? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whatever is cut from an animal while it is alive is carrion. It is not narrated from Tamim except with this chain; Abu Bakr is alone in transmitting it."
"3104","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Shu'ayb ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: al-Layth ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Hurmuz, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: If his neighbor asks him to fix a plank of wood in his wall, let him not refuse him. No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except al-Layth, and no one narrated it from al-Layth except Shu'ayb."
"3105","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Sulayman al-Misri narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad al-Rassasi narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Khumayr, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a girl is born, Allah Almighty sends an angel to her who ushers blessing in, saying: A weak one has come forth from a weak one; the one who maintains her is aided until the Day of Resurrection. And when a boy is born, Allah sends an angel to him from heaven who kisses between his eyes and says: Allah conveys peace to you. No one narrated this hadith from Shu'bah except Abd al-Rahman; Abdullah is alone in transmitting it."
"3106","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn al-Bara ibn al-Nadr ibn Anas ibn Malik narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to us, from al-Hakam ibn Utaybah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Abu al-Darda, who said: I was sitting before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he mentioned well-being and the great reward Allah has prepared for its companion if he is grateful, and he mentioned tribulation and the great reward Allah has prepared for its companion if he is patient. I said: By my father and mother, O Messenger of Allah, to be granted well-being and be grateful is dearer to me than to be afflicted and be patient. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: And the Messenger of Allah loves well-being along with you. No one narrated this hadith from Shu'bah except Ibrahim; Bakr is alone in transmitting it."
"3107","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn al-Bara ibn al-Nadr ibn Anas narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Mas'ud al-Ansari, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah Almighty has servants whom He gives life in well-being, causes to die in well-being, resurrects in well-being, and admits to Paradise in well-being. No one narrated this hadith from al-A'mash except Hammad, and it is not narrated from Abu Mas'ud except with this chain; and nothing is preserved for Hammad ibn Salamah from al-A'mash except this hadith, though Hammad ibn Salamah narrated from al-Hajjaj ibn Artah, from al-A'mash; and it is not denied that he heard from al-A'mash, for he narrated from a group of Kufans, among them Salamah ibn Kuhayl, Hammad ibn Abi Sulayman, Asim ibn Bahdalah, Abu Hamzah al-A'war and others."
"3108","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Abu Ata Bilal ibn Amr narrated to us, from Salih ibn Abi Salih, from Umar ibn Rashid, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Harmalah, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three whose testimony that there is no god but Allah is not accepted: the male rider and the ridden, the female rider and the ridden, and the unjust imam. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Harmalah except Umar ibn Rashid, and no one narrated it from Umar except Salih ibn Abi Salih; Abu Ata is alone in transmitting it."
"3109","Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: al-Layth ibn Sa'd narrated to me, he said: Khalid ibn Yazid narrated to me, from Sa'id ibn Abi Hilal, from Muhammad ibn Ka'b al-Qurazi, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: Abu Talhah came to Umm Sulaym, who is the mother of Anas ibn Malik, while Abu Talhah was his stepfather, and said: Do you have anything, O Umm Sulaym? For I passed by the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was teaching the people of the Suffah Surah al-Nisa, with a stone tied on his belly from hunger. She said: I had some barley which I ground, then she sent me to the markets, and the markets were walled gardens of theirs, and I brought them some firewood, and I made a round loaf from it. Then he said: Do you have any condiment? She said: I had a skin with ghee in it, and I do not know if anything remains in it, so I brought it to him and squeezed it. He said: The squeezing of two is more effective than the squeezing of one, so they squeezed together and produced about a date's worth, and she greased the loaf with it. Then she called me and said: O Anas, seek out the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). I said: Yes. He said: I left him with the people of the Suffah teaching them; invite him and do not invite anyone else with him; take care not to disgrace me. I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and when he saw me he said: Perhaps your father sent you to us? I said: Yes. He said to the people: Go forth. They went forth that day, eighty men. He took my hand, and when I drew near the house I pulled my hand from his hand. Abu Talhah kept seeking me in the house, pelting me with stones, saying: You have disgraced me before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Then he went out to him and told him the news. He said: It will not harm you. He ordered them and they sat, then he entered and we brought him the loaf. He said: Is there any condiment? Umm Sulaym said: O Messenger of Allah, we had a skin, and Abu Talhah and I squeezed it. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Bring it, for the squeezing of three is more effective than the squeezing of two. It was brought to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) squeezed it with them, and they produced about a date's worth, and they wiped the loaf with it. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wiped it with his hand, then supplicated for blessing in it, then said: Call ten for me. I called ten, and they ate until they belched with fullness. They kept entering ten by ten until they were full. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sat and we sat with him, and we ate until there was leftover. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Ka'b except Sa'id, and no one narrated it from Sa'id except Khalid; al-Layth is alone in transmitting it."
"3110","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Shu'ayb ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: al-Layth ibn Sa'd narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Ansari narrated to us, from Sa'd ibn Ibrahim, from Nafi' ibn Jubayr, from Urwah ibn al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, from his father al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, from the Messenger (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he went out to relieve himself, and al-Mughirah followed him with a water skin containing water; he brought his hands out from under a fur garment, performed ablution and wiped over his leather socks. No one narrated this hadith from Yahya except al-Layth and Muhammad ibn Ishaq."
"3111","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi al-Sari al-Asqalani narrated to us, he said: al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, he said: Mu'awiyah ibn Sa'id al-Tujibi narrated to us, from Abu Qabil, from Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever dies on Friday or Friday night is shielded from the trial of the grave. No one narrated this hadith from Mu'awiyah except al-Walid."
"3112","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'awiyah Muhammad ibn Khazim narrated to us, he said: Abu Ishaq al-Shaybani narrated to us, from Adi ibn Thabit, from al-Bara ibn Azib, who said: The Messenger (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Hassan, lampoon the polytheists, and Jibril is with you. No one narrated this hadith from al-Shaybani except Abu Mu'awiyah."
"3113","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Ja'far al-Dimyati narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Majid ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Rawwad narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None of you will die until he completes his provision, so do not deem provision slow; fear Allah and seek gracefully; take what is lawful and leave what is unlawful. No one narrated this hadith from Abu al-Zubayr except Ibn Jurayj, and it is not narrated from Jabir except with this chain."
"3114","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi al-Sari al-Asqalani narrated to us, he said: Adam ibn Abi Iyas narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Dinar al-Shami, from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) let his forelock hang down as the People of the Book let theirs hang, then parted it afterwards as the Arabs part; and when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was in doubt about a matter done by the polytheists and the People of the Book, concerning which no revelation had come, he acted according to the practice of the People of the Book. No one narrated this hadith from Abdullah ibn Dinar al-Bahrani except Isma'il, and no one narrated it from Isma'il except Adam; Muhammad is alone in transmitting it."
"3115","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Aswad narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A previously married woman is to be consulted concerning herself; if she remains silent that is her permission, and if she refuses there is no validity imposed upon her."
"3116","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Malik, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: My pulpit is upon a canal of the canals of Paradise, and what is between the pulpit and the house of A'ishah is a meadow of the meadows of Paradise. No one narrated this hadith from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah except Muhammad ibn Abdullah; Ibn Lahi'ah is alone in transmitting it."
"3117","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Yusuf and Shu'ayb narrated to us, they said: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Abi Ja'far, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Hold to the siwak, for it is pleasing to the Lord and sweetens the mouth."
"3118","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Musa ibn Wardan, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: May Allah curse the people of predestination who deny one decree and affirm another decree. No one narrated this hadith from Musa except Ibn Lahi'ah."
"3119","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Abi Habib and Yunus narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, from Urwah, from A'ishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would say takbir on Fitr and Adha, seven in the first rak'ah and five in the second before the recitation. No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except Yunus, Yazid ibn Abi Habib and Khalid ibn Yazid; Ibn Lahi'ah is alone in transmitting it."
"3120","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, he said: al-Harith ibn Yazid narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu al-Ward saying: I heard Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr saying: The tashahhud of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is: In the name of Allah, and by Allah, the best of names; greetings belong to Allah, the good things, the prayers; I bear witness that there is no god but Allah alone without partner, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger; He sent him with the truth as a bearer of glad tidings and a warner; and that the Hour is coming without doubt; peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings; peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah; O Allah, forgive me and guide me. This is in the first two rak'ahs. It is not narrated from Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr except with this chain; Ibn Lahi'ah is alone in transmitting it."
"3121","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Yusuf and Shu'ayb ibn Yahya narrated to us, they said: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated to us, from Sa'id al-Maqburi, from his father, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said in the year of Banu Lihyan: Let one man from every two of you go out, and let the warrior leave behind one to care for his family and wealth, and he will have half his reward. It is not narrated from Abu Sa'id except with this chain; Ibn Lahi'ah is alone in transmitting it."
"3122","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Yusuf and Shu'ayb ibn Yahya narrated to us, they said: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, he said: Zabban ibn Fa'id narrated to us, from Lahi'ah ibn Uqbah, from Amr ibn Rabi'ah al-Hadrami, who said: I heard Salamah ibn Qaysar saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever fasts a day seeking the face of Allah, Allah will distance him from Hell the distance of a crow that flew as a chick until it died of old age. It is not narrated from Salamah ibn Qaysar except with this chain; Ibn Lahi'ah is alone in transmitting it."
"3123","And with the same chain: Zabban ibn Fa'id narrated to us, from Sahl ibn Mu'adh ibn Anas, from his father, from Abu al-Darda, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Headache and fever do not leave the believer, though his sins be like Uhud, without leaving upon him sins weighing a mustard seed. It is not narrated from Abu al-Darda except with this chain; Ibn Lahi'ah is alone in transmitting it."
"3124","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn Yazid ibn Subayh al-Murri narrated to us, he said: Yunus ibn Maysarah ibn Halbas narrated to us, from Umm al-Darda, from Abu al-Darda, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Allah Almighty has settled for every servant five things of His creation: his deed, his lifespan, his provision, his trace, and his resting place. It is not narrated from Abu al-Darda except with this chain; Khalid is alone in transmitting it."
"3125","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn Yazid ibn Subayh narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Abi Ablah, from Utbah ibn Ghazwan, of the Banu Mazin ibn Sa'sa'ah, who was of the Companions, that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: After you are days of patience; one who holds fast therein to what you are upon will have the reward of fifty of you. They said: O Prophet of Allah, or of them? He said: No, rather of you. They said: O Prophet of Allah, or of them? He said: No, rather of you, three times or four. This hadith is not narrated from Utbah except with this chain; Ibrahim ibn Abi Ablah is alone in transmitting it."
"3126","And with the same chain: Ibrahim ibn Abi Ablah narrated to us, that Marwan ibn al-Hakam asked Abu Hurayrah: Did you hear anything from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) concerning prayer over the funeral? He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: O Allah, You created him, You guided him to Islam, You took his soul, and You know best his secret and his open; we have come to You as intercessors, so forgive him and have mercy on him. No one narrated this hadith from Ibrahim except Khalid ibn Yazid and Irak ibn Khalid ibn Yazid."
"3127","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Shu'ayb ibn Yahya narrated to us, from Nafi' ibn Yazid: Mu'awiyah ibn Yazid ibn Shurahbil informed me, that Abdullah ibn al-Walid ibn al-Mughirah narrated to him, that he heard Abdullah ibn Abi Zakariyya narrating from Shurahbil ibn al-Simt, that he saw Salman al-Farisi while he was stationed at the coast of Hims, and said: What is this? He said: Standing guard. Salman said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Guarding for a day in the path of Allah is like fasting a month and standing its nights; and whoever dies while guarding, the reward of the deeds he used to do continues for him, he is safe from the tempter, and he is raised on the Day of Resurrection as a martyr. No one narrated this hadith from Abdullah ibn Abi Zakariyya except Abdullah ibn al-Walid, and no one narrated it from Abdullah except Mu'awiyah ibn Yazid; Nafi' ibn Yazid is alone in transmitting it."
"3128","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Shu'ayb ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Harb ibn Qays, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Taymi, from Abu Umamah ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf and Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurayrah and Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: When a man bathes on Friday, applies perfume, listens attentively and does not engage in idle talk until the imam finishes his sermon, and prays what occurs to him, he is forgiven what is between one Friday and the next, plus three days more. No one narrated this hadith from Harb except Yazid; Ibn Lahi'ah is alone in transmitting it."
"3129","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Shu'ayb ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Nafi' ibn Kaysan, who informed him that his father Kaysan informed him that he used to trade in wine in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); he came from Syria with wine in skins intending trade, and came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have brought a fine drink. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It has been forbidden after you. Kaysan said: Should I go and sell it, O Prophet of Allah? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It has been forbidden, and its price has been forbidden. So Kaysan went to the skins, seized them by their legs, then poured them all out. It is not narrated from Kaysan except with this chain; Ibn Lahi'ah is alone in transmitting it."
"3130","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Shu'ayb ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from al-Harith ibn Yazid, from Ulayy ibn Rabah, who said: I heard Abdullah ibn Amr saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The Muslim attains the rank of the fasting, night-praying one through good character."
"3131","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: al-Layth ibn Sa'd narrated to me, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Abi Ja'far narrated to me, from Abu al-Aswad, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Amrah bint Abd al-Rahman, from A'ishah, that she said concerning the meats of the sacrifices: We used to preserve some of it, and people would come with it to Madinah, and they would eat it only for three days; it was not a binding command, but he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) intended that they eat of it. No one narrated this hadith from Yahya except Hisham, and no one narrated it from Hisham except Abu al-Aswad, and no one narrated it from Abu al-Aswad except Ubaydullah ibn Abi Ja'far; al-Layth is alone in transmitting it."
"3132","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Nu'aym ibn Hammad al-Marwazi narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, from Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im, who said: It reached Mu'awiyah that Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As was narrating that there will be a king from Qahtan, so he became angry and said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: This authority will remain among Quraysh; none opposes them but Allah will throw him on his face into the Fire. No one narrated this hadith from Ma'mar except Abdullah."
"3133","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Salih ibn Musa al-Talhi narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Musa ibn Talhah, who said: It reached A'ishah that Ibn Umar says: Sudden death is wrath upon the believers. She said: May Allah forgive Ibn Umar; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) only said: Sudden death is relief for the believers and wrath upon the disbelievers. No one narrated this hadith from Abd al-Malik except Salih."
"3134","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi al-Sari al-Asqalani narrated to us, he said: al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, from Atiyyah ibn Qays al-Kilabi, who said: Mu'awiyah ibn Abi Sufyan proposed to Umm al-Darda after the death of Abu al-Darda, and Umm al-Darda said: I heard Abu al-Darda saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Any woman whose husband dies and she marries after him belongs to the last of her husbands; and I would not prefer you over Abu al-Darda. Mu'awiyah wrote to her: Then fast, for it is a cutter of desire. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Maryam except al-Walid."
"3135","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Shu'ayb ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, from Isa ibn Musa ibn Humayd al-Qurazi, from Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Sa'sa'ah, from his father, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, that he advised a man who stayed in the desert: When you call the adhan for prayer, raise your voice with the call, for no jinn, human, tree or anything hears your voice but will bear witness for you on the Day of Resurrection; I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying that. No one narrated this hadith from Isa ibn Musa except Yahya."
"3136","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Mahdi ibn Ja'far al-Ramli narrated to us, he said: Suwayd ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, from Humayd al-Tawil, from Anas, who said: A woman came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) seeking something, and he said: Sit on any of the roads of Madinah you wish until I sit with you. No one narrated this hadith from Suwayd except Mahdi."
"3137","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Shu'ayb ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: al-Layth narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ajlan narrated to me, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man who had never done any good removed a branch of thorns from the road, whether it was on a tree and he cut it, or it was lying and he removed it, so Allah Almighty thanked him and admitted him to Paradise. No one narrated this hadith from Zayd except Muhammad."
"3138","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Abd al-Karim Abu Umayyah, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Ibn Abbas, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Wine is the mother of obscenities and the greatest of major sins; whoever drinks it commits incest with his mother, his maternal aunt and his paternal aunt. No one narrated this hadith from Ata except Abd al-Karim."
"3139","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn al-Mughirah al-Missisi narrated to us, he said: Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every intoxicant is forbidden. No one narrated this hadith from Umar ibn al-Mughirah except Abdullah ibn Yusuf."
"3140","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, he said: Salim ibn Ghaylan narrated to us, from al-Walid ibn Qays, from Abu al-Haytham, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Keep company only with a believer, and let none eat your food but a God-fearing one. It is not narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except with this chain; Salim is alone in transmitting it."
"3141","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Nu'aym ibn Hammad narrated to us, he said: Rishdin ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Amr ibn al-Harith, from Darraj Abu al-Samh, from Abu al-Haytham, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), concerning His saying: Like molten brass; he said: Like the dregs of oil; when it is brought near him the skin of his face falls off from it. No one narrated this hadith from Amr except Rishdin."
"3142","Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Hamzah narrated to us, he said: Thawr ibn Yazid narrated to me, from Ali ibn Abi Talhah, from Abd al-Malik, from Abu Dharr, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fasted continuously two days and a night, and Jibril came to him and said: Allah has accepted your continuous fast, and it is not lawful for anyone after you; that is because Allah, blessed and exalted, says: Then complete the fast until the night, so there is no fasting after the night; and He commanded me to pray witr after dawn. No one narrated this hadith from Thawr except Yahya, and it is not narrated from Abu Dharr except with this chain."
"3143","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Nu'aym ibn Hammad narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr ibn Nafi', the freedman of Ibn Umar, narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm saying: I heard Amrah bint Abd al-Rahman saying: A'ishah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Overlook the slips of people of rank, so long as it is not a prescribed punishment. It is not narrated from A'ishah except from the hadith of Abu Bakr ibn Muhammad, from Amrah."
"3144","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Nu'aym ibn Hammad narrated to us, he said: al-Wazir ibn Subayh narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Maysarah ibn Halbas, from Umm al-Darda, from Abu al-Darda, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), concerning: Every day He is in a matter; he said: Of His matter is that He forgives a sin, relieves a distress, raises a people and lowers others. No one narrated this hadith from Umm al-Darda except Yunus."
"3145","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Hashim al-Bayruti narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Abi Karimah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Hassan, from al-Hasan, from his mother, from Umm Salamah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, inform me about the saying of Allah Almighty: And houris, wide-eyed. He said: Houris: fair; wide-eyed: large-eyed; the eyelash of the houri is like the wing of the eagle. I said: O Messenger of Allah, inform me about the saying of Allah Almighty: As if they were rubies and coral. He said: Their clarity is like the clarity of pearls in shells untouched by hands. I said: O Messenger of Allah, inform me about His saying: In them are good, beautiful ones. He said: Good in character, beautiful in faces. I said: O Messenger of Allah, inform me about His saying: As if they were sheltered eggs. He said: Their delicacy is like the delicacy of the skin inside the egg next to the shell, which is the thin membrane. I said: O Messenger of Allah, inform me about His saying: Loving, of equal age. He said: They are those who were taken in the abode of this world as aged, bleary, gray-haired old women; Allah created them after old age and made them virgins. He said: Loving: beloved, affectionate; of equal age: of one birth. I said: O Messenger of Allah, are the women of this world better, or the wide-eyed houris? He said: Rather the women of this world are better than the wide-eyed houris, as the outer garment is better than the lining. I said: O Messenger of Allah, and for what is that? He said: For their prayer, their fasting and their worship of Allah Almighty; Allah Almighty has clothed their faces with light and their bodies with silk, fair in color, green in garments, yellow in jewelry; their censers are pearls and their combs are gold; they say: Are we not the everlasting who never die; are we not the blissful who never suffer misery; are we not the residents who never depart; are we not the content who never anger; glad tidings to him for whom we are and who is for us. I said: A woman of us marries two, three or four husbands, then dies and enters Paradise and they enter with her; which of them will be her husband? He said: O Umm Salamah, she is given choice and chooses the best of them in character, saying: O Lord, he was the best of them with me in character in the abode of this world, so marry me to him. O Umm Salamah, good character has taken the good of this world and the Hereafter. No one narrated this hadith from Hisham ibn Hassan except Sulayman ibn Abi Karimah; Amr ibn Hashim is alone in transmitting it."
"3146","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Fulayh ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Gold for gold, silver for silver; do not take excess of one over the other. No one narrated this hadith from Fulayh except Sa'id."
"3147","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: al-Haytham ibn Humayd narrated to us, he said: Zayd ibn Waqid narrated to me, from Sulayman ibn Musa, from Kathir ibn Murrah, from Tamim al-Dari, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever reads a hundred verses in a night, a night's devotion is recorded for him."
"3148","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Ansari, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A hajj for one who has not performed hajj is better than ten expeditions, and an expedition for one who has performed hajj is better than ten hajjs, and an expedition by sea is better than ten expeditions by land; and whoever crosses the sea, it is as if he crossed all the valleys; and the seasick therein is like one rolling in his blood. No one narrated this hadith from Yahya ibn Sa'id except Yahya ibn Ayyub."
"3149","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Shu'ayb ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he walked, it was as if he leaned forward. No one narrated this hadith from Humayd except Yahya."
"3150","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Hashim narrated to us, he said: al-Hiql ibn Ziyad narrated to us, from al-Awza'i, from Uthman ibn Abi Sawdah, from Abu Shu'ayb al-Hadrami, from Abu Ayyub al-Ansari, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you defecates, let him wipe with three stones, for that suffices him. No one narrated this hadith from al-Awza'i in raised form except al-Hiql; Amr is alone in transmitting it."
"3151","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Shu'ayb ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Ansari, from Amrah, from A'ishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would pray witr with three rak'ahs, reciting in the first rak'ah Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High, in the second Say, O disbelievers, and in the third Say, He is Allah, the One, and Say, I seek refuge with the Lord of the daybreak, and Say, I seek refuge with the Lord of mankind. No one narrated this hadith from Sa'id except Yahya ibn Ayyub."
"3152","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Shu'ayb ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, from Humayd, that he heard Anas ibn Malik saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If a woman of the women of Paradise were to look down to the earth, she would fill what is between them with fragrance, and she would illuminate what is between them, and her crown upon her head would be better than the world and what is in it."
"3153","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Shu'ayb ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Khalid ibn Yazid, from Sa'id ibn Abi Hilal, from Ali ibn Yahya, from Abu Umamah al-Bahili, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: All of you are in Paradise except one who strays from Allah Almighty as a camel strays from its people. It is not narrated from Abu Umamah except with this chain; Ibn Lahi'ah is alone in transmitting it."
"3154","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: al-Layth ibn Sa'd narrated to me, he said: Ibrahim ibn A'yan narrated to me, from Kharijah ibn Mus'ab, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No child can repay his father unless he finds him enslaved and frees him. No one narrated this hadith from Kharijah except Ibrahim; al-Layth is alone in transmitting it."
"3155","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Shu'ayb ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abdullah ibn al-Had, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from his father, from Bilal, who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he wiped over the leather socks. No one narrated from Ibn al-Had except Yahya and al-Layth ibn Sa'd."
"3156","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: al-Layth ibn Sa'd narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Abdullah ibn al-Had narrated to me, from Mu'awiyah ibn Abi Muzarrid, from Yazid ibn Ruman, from Urwah, from A'ishah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The womb is a branch from the Most Merciful; whoever joins it, I join him, and whoever cuts it, I cut him. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn al-Had except al-Layth."
"3157","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Maysarah, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Nothing like marriage has been seen for two who love one another. No one narrated this hadith from Tawus except Ibrahim, and no one narrated it from Ibrahim except Muhammad and Sufyan al-Thawri; Mu'ammal ibn Isma'il is alone in transmitting it from al-Thawri."
"3158","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Hamzah narrated to us, he said: Thawr ibn Yazid narrated to me, from Khalid ibn Ma'dan, who narrated to him, he said: Rabi'ah ibn al-Ghaz narrated to me, that he asked A'ishah about the fasting of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and she said: He used to fast all of Sha'ban until joining it with Ramadan, and he used to seek to fast Mondays and Thursdays. No one narrated this hadith from Thawr except Yahya."
"3159","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Shu'ayb ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, from Humayd al-Tawil, that he heard Anas ibn Malik saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever loves the meeting with Allah, Allah loves meeting him; and whoever hates the meeting with Allah, Allah hates meeting him. They said: O Messenger of Allah, there is none of us but hates death. He said: It is not that; when the bearer of glad tidings from Allah comes to the believer, he loves the meeting with Allah, and Allah loves meeting him even more; and when what he hates comes to the disbeliever, he hates the meeting with Allah, and Allah Almighty hates meeting him even more."
"3160","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to me, from Ibn Jurayj, from Amr ibn Dinar and Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, who said: We sacrificed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a camel on behalf of seven persons. It was said to Jabir: And the cow? He said: It is like it. He said: And Jabir witnessed al-Hudaybiyyah. He said: And we sacrificed that day seventy camels. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Jurayj except Yahya."
"3161","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Ulayy ibn Rabah narrated to us, from his father, from Suraqah ibn Malik ibn Ju'shum, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Shall I not tell you of the people of Paradise and the people of Hell? I said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: As for the people of Hell, every harsh, arrogant, proud one; and as for the people of Paradise, the weak, the overpowered. It is not narrated from Suraqah except with this chain; Musa is alone in transmitting it."
"3162","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Ishaq, from Harithah ibn Mudarrib, who said: Abdullah ibn Mas'ud said to Ibn al-Nawwahah: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Were it not that you are an envoy I would kill you; but today you are no envoy. Rise, O Kharashah, and strike his neck. He rose to him and struck his neck. No one narrated this hadith from al-A'mash except Abu Mu'awiyah."
"3163","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Ishkab al-Saffar al-Kufi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Fudayl narrated to us, from Abu Mansur, from Zayd ibn Wahb, from Abu Dharr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Abu Dharr, which mountain is this? I said: Uhud. He said: By the One in whose hand is my soul, it would not please me that it were gold in pieces which I spend in the path of Allah, leaving of it a qirat. I said: A qintar, O Messenger of Allah? He said: A qirat. I said: A qintar, O Messenger of Allah? He said: A qirat. Then he said to me the third time: O Abu Dharr, I only say what is less, and I do not say what is more. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Mansur except Muhammad."
"3164","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Shu'ayb ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Abi Ja'far, from Safwan ibn Sulaym, from Salman al-Agharr, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered a detachment to go out, and they said: O Messenger of Allah, shall we go out tonight or stay until morning? He said: Would you not love to spend the night in a garden of the gardens of Paradise? No one narrated this hadith from Safwan except Ibn Lahi'ah."
"3165","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'awiyah al-Darir narrated to us, he said: Abu Hanifah al-Nu'man ibn Thabit narrated to us, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from A'ishah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said in the illness in which he died: It lightens death for me that I was shown you as my wife in Paradise. No one narrated this hadith from Hammad except Abu Hanifah and Mis'ar; Abu Mu'awiyah is alone in transmitting it."
"3166","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: al-Haytham ibn Humayd and Yahya ibn Hamzah narrated to us, they said: al-Nu'man ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us, from Makhul, from Anbasah ibn Abi Sufyan, from Umm Habibah, that she informed him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever guards four rak'ahs before the midday prayer and four after it, Allah will forbid him to Hell. No one narrated this hadith from al-Nu'man except al-Haytham and Yahya ibn Hamzah."
"3167","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Shu'ayb ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ali al-Qurazi, from Mu'awiyah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he heard the muezzin would say as he says. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Ali except Ibn Lahi'ah."
"3168","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Shu'ayb ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Abu Ali al-Hamdani, from Fadalah ibn Ubayd, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Level your graves."
"3169","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Shu'ayb ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman, from al-Qasim Abu Abd al-Rahman, from Shurahbil ibn al-Simt, from Amr ibn Abasah, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever grows a gray hair in the path of Allah, it is light for him on the Day of Resurrection; and whoever shoots the enemy with an arrow, whether he misses or hits, it is like freeing a neck; and whoever frees a Muslim neck, it is his ransom from the Fire, every limb for a limb. No one narrated this hadith from Sulayman except Ibn Lahi'ah."
"3170","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Shu'ayb ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Khalid ibn Abi Imran, from al-Qasim Abu Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Umamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever wipes the head of an orphan, for every hair is a good deed. No one narrated this hadith from Khalid except Ibn Lahi'ah."
"3171","And with the same chain, from Khalid ibn Abi Imran, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli, that Abu Sa'id al-Khudri narrated to him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took his hand and said: O Abu Sa'id. I said: At your service, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Three things: whoever has them, Paradise is incumbent for him. I said: And what are they, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Whoever is pleased with Allah as Lord, with Islam as religion, and with Muhammad as Messenger. He said: And the fourth, O Abu Sa'id, has such merit as a hundred degrees between heaven and earth, and it is jihad. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Abd al-Rahman except Khalid; Ibn Lahi'ah is alone in transmitting it."
"3172","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Shu'ayb ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman, from al-Qasim Abu Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Umamah, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him not wear silk or gold. No one narrated this hadith from Sulayman except Ibn Lahi'ah."
"3173","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Shu'ayb ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Ali Abu Dinar al-Hudhali, from Nu'aym ibn Hammar, that a man called the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, who are the martyrs? He said: The martyrs are those who fight in the first rank and do not turn their faces until they are killed; those meet in the highest chambers of Paradise; your Lord laughs to them; when Allah Almighty laughs to His believing servant there is no reckoning upon him. No one narrated this hadith from Ali Abu Dinar except Ibn Lahi'ah."
"3174","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Shu'ayb ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Abu al-Khayr, from Abdullah ibn Amr, that a man asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Which Muslims are best, O Messenger of Allah? He said: He from whose tongue and hand people are safe."
"3175","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Hashim al-Bayruti narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Abi Karimah narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: No servant glorifies Allah with a glorification, praises Him with a praise, or magnifies Him with a magnification, but Allah Almighty plants for him thereby a tree in Paradise, its root of gold, its top of jewel, crowned with pearls and rubies, its fruits like the breasts of virgins, softer than butter and sweeter than honey; whenever he picks anything of it, its place returns. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited this verse: Neither cut off nor withheld. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Jurayj except Sulayman; Amr ibn Hashim is alone in transmitting it."
"3176","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Sulayman al-Khurasani narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, he said: Ma'mar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim ibn Abdullah ibn Umar, from his father, who said: When Umar ibn al-Khattab was stabbed and appointed the council, his daughter Hafsah entered upon him and said: O father, the people say these men whom you placed in the council are not acceptable? He said: Prop me up. They propped him up while he was in his condition, and said: What might they say about Uthman? I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: On the day Uthman dies, the angels of heaven will pray over him. I said: For Uthman particularly, or for people generally? He said: Rather for Uthman particularly. He said: And what might they say about Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf? I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) suffering severe hunger, and Abd al-Rahman came with two loaves with melted fat between them and placed them before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: May Allah suffice you the affair of your world; as for the Hereafter, I am its guarantor. What might they say about Talhah? I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) whose saddle had fallen on a very cold night, and said: Who will straighten my saddle, and Paradise is his? Talhah hastened to the saddle and straightened it. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Paradise is yours upon me, O Talhah, tomorrow. What might they say about al-Zubayr? I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sleeping, and al-Zubayr kept fanning the Prophet's (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) face until he awoke. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Have you not ceased, O Abu Abdullah? He said: I have not ceased, may my father and mother be your ransom. He said: This is Jibril conveying peace to you, and saying to you: It is upon me to ward off the sparks of Hell from your face on the Day of Resurrection. What might they say about Ali? I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: O Ali, your hand is with my hand on the Day of Resurrection; you enter with me wherever I enter. No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except Ma'mar, and no one narrated it from Ma'mar except Ibn al-Mubarak; Abdullah ibn Yahya is alone in transmitting it."
"3177","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: Kathir ibn Sulaym al-Yashkuri narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I am a man sharp of tongue, mostly against my family. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Where are you in regard to seeking forgiveness? I seek Allah's forgiveness a hundred times in a day and night."
"3178","And with the same chain, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Good comes more swiftly to a house that is frequented than a knife to the hump of a camel."
"3179","And with the same chain, he said: No roasted meat was ever lifted from before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except that a carpet was carried with it."
"3180","And with the same chain, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: On the night I was taken, I did not pass any company of angels but they said: Command your ummah to cup."
"3181","And with the same chain, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the Almighty takes the two precious ones of a servant, his reward for them is Paradise."
"3182","And with the same chain, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he prayed and finished his prayer, would wipe his head with his right hand and say: In the name of Allah, besides whom there is no god, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate; O Allah, remove from me worry and grief."
"3183","And with the same chain, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said one day to his companions: Take your shield. They said: By our father and mother, O Messenger of Allah, has an enemy come? He said: Take your shield from the Fire; say: Glory be to Allah, praise be to Allah, there is no god but Allah, Allah is greatest, and there is no power nor strength except with Allah; for they are the preceders, they turn aside evil, they follow after, and they are the lasting righteous deeds."
"3184","And with the same chain, that a man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I see dreams that sicken me. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: The good dream is from Allah, and the bad is from Satan; when one of you sees that, let him spit to his left three times and seek refuge from its evil, for it will not harm him."
"3185","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Salim al-Himsi narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Abi Ablah narrated to us, he said: I was sitting at Ariha, and Wathilah ibn al-Asqa' passed by me leaning on Abdullah ibn al-Daylami; he seated him, then came to me and said: How strange what the shaykh narrated to me, meaning Wathilah. I said: What did he narrate to you? He said: We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the expedition of Tabuk, and a group of Banu Sulaym came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, our companion has made it incumbent. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Free a neck on his behalf; Allah will free with every limb of it a limb of him from the Fire."
"3186","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Aswad narrated to us, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Asma bint Abi Bakr, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The believer sits in his grave when those who witnessed him turn away from him, and it is said: What of a man called Muhammad, what is he? If he is a believer he says: He is the servant of Allah and His Messenger. It is said to him: Sleep; may your eyes sleep. And if he is not a believer he says: By Allah, I do not know; I heard people saying, so I said, and they delved, so I delved. It is said: May your eyes not sleep. No one narrated this hadith from Abu al-Aswad except Ibn Lahi'ah."
"3187","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Shu'ayb ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: al-Layth ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Usamah ibn Zayd, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when people came to him in the Farewell Pilgrimage; one of them said: I shaved before slaughtering. He said: No harm. And he said: I slaughtered before stoning. He said: No harm. He said: And all of Arafah is a standing place, and all of Muzdalifah is a standing place, and all the passes of Makkah are a road and a place of slaughter."
"3188","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Ulayy ibn Rabah al-Lakhmi narrated to me, from his father, from Uqbah ibn Amir al-Juhani, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us to pray in three hours, or to bury our dead in them: when the sun rises shining until it is high, when the noon stander stands until it declines, and when the sun turns to setting until it sets."
"3189","And with the same chain, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The day of Arafah, the day of sacrifice, and the days of tashriq are our festival, O people of Islam, and they are days of eating and drinking."
"3190","And with the same chain, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to us while we were in the Suffah and said: Which of you would love to go each morning to Buthan or al-Aqiq and take two large humped, bright she-camels without sin or severing kinship? They said: All of us, O Messenger of Allah, would love that. He said: Then for one of you to go each morning to the mosque and learn two verses of the Book of Allah is better for him than two she-camels, and than three, and than their numbers of camels."
"3191","With the same chain: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Learn the Book of Allah, keep to it constantly, acquire it, and chant it melodiously, for by the One in Whose Hand is my soul, it escapes from the chests of men more violently than young she-camels escape from their hobbles."
"3192","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Ulayy narrated to us, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do you know who the Muslim is? They said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: The one from whose hand and tongue the Muslims are safe. They said: Then who is the believer? He said: The one whom the believers trust with their lives and their wealth. They said: Then who is the emigrant? He said: The one who abandons evil and keeps away from it."
"3193","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Abdullah narrated to us, he said: Musa narrated to me, from his father, from Amr ibn al-As, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent for me and said: Take your sword and your weapons. So I took my sword and my weapons, then I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and found him performing ablution; he looked me up and down, then lowered his gaze, then said: O Amr, I intend to send you at the head of an army; Allah will grant you booty and keep you safe, and I shall allot you a good share of wealth. He said: By Allah, O Messenger of Allah, I did not accept Islam for wealth; rather I accepted Islam out of desire for Islam and to be with you. He said: O Amr, how excellent is righteous wealth for a righteous man."
"3194","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: al-Layth ibn Sad narrated to us, he said: Ibn al-Had narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, from Busr ibn Said, from Abu Qays, the freedman of Amr ibn al-As, from Amr ibn al-As, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When the judge exercises ijtihad and then is correct, he has two rewards, and when he judges and exercises ijtihad and then errs, he has one reward. So I narrated it to Abu Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm, and he said: Thus did Abu Salamah narrate to me, from Abu Hurayrah. This hadith is not narrated from Amr ibn al-As except with this chain; Yazid ibn al-Had alone transmitted it."
"3195","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: Bakr ibn Mudar narrated to us, from Amr ibn al-Harith, from Bukayr ibn Abdullah ibn al-Ashajj, that Muadh ibn Abdullah al-Juhani narrated to him that Uqbah ibn Amir said: We sacrificed young sheep with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"3196","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: Bakr ibn Mudar narrated to me, from Abu Zuraah Amr ibn Jabir, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, that he heard him say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever fasts Ramadan and six days of Shawwal, it is as if he fasted a year."
"3197","And with the same chain: that he heard Jabir ibn Abdullah narrating that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioned the plague and said: The one who flees from it is like the one who flees from the battlefield, and the one who endures it patiently has the reward of a martyr."
"3198","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Abdullah narrated to us, he said: Bakr ibn Mudar narrated to me, from Ayyash ibn Uqbah al-Hadrami, from Yahya ibn Maymun, he said: Sahl ibn Sad al-Saidi passed by me while I was sitting in the mosque, and said: Shall I not narrate to you a hadith I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? I said: Yes indeed. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever is in the mosque waiting for the prayer is engaged in prayer."
"3199","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: Bakr ibn Mudar narrated to me, from Amr ibn al-Harith, from Bukayr ibn Abdullah al-Ashajj, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: A woman is not to be married together with her paternal aunt nor together with her maternal aunt."
"3200","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Abi Ja'far, from Aban ibn Salih, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Supplication is the marrow of worship. This hadith was not narrated from Aban except by Ubaydullah; Ibn Lahi'ah alone transmitted it."
"3201","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahi'ah informed us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Shimasah al-Mahri, that he heard Uqbah ibn Amir al-Juhani say: We prayed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he prolonged the standing with us, though when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed he would shorten his standing; and during that we heard him saying: O Lord, and I among them? Then he reached out with his right hand to take something, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) bowed, then hastened thereafter. When he finished with the salutation he sat and we sat around him, and he said: I knew that my long standing alarmed you. We said: Yes; we heard you saying: O Lord, and I among them? He said: By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, nothing of what you have been promised in the Hereafter but was displayed to me in this station of mine, until the Fire was displayed to me; a portion of it advanced toward me until it reached my spot, and I feared it would engulf you, so I said: O Lord, and I among them? So Allah turned it away from you, and it came in pieces as though they were carpets. And I glanced into it a glance, and there was Amr ibn Hidthan, the brother of Banu Ghifar, reclining upon his bow in Hell, and there was the Himyari woman, the owner of the cat, who had tied it up and neither fed it nor gave it water nor set it free to seek what it eats, until it died in that state. This hadith was not narrated from Ibn Shimasah except by Yazid ibn Abi Habib."
"3202","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Shu'ayb ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: al-Layth informed us, from Yahya ibn Ayyub, from Abu Ghallab, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever strangles himself in this world and kills himself will strangle himself in the Fire, and whoever stabs himself will stab himself in the Fire, and whoever plunges himself down will plunge into the Fire."
"3203","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Abu al-Aswad, from Urwah, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The changed breath of the fasting person's mouth is sweeter in Allah's sight than the scent of musk. This hadith was not narrated from Abu al-Aswad except by Ibn Lahi'ah."
"3204","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Sad narrated to me, from Salih ibn Kaysan, from Ibn Shihab, from Muhammad ibn Abi Sufyan al-Thaqafi, from Yusuf ibn al-Hakam, the father of al-Hajjaj ibn Yusuf, from Muhammad ibn Sad, from Sad ibn Abi Waqqas, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever intends the humiliation of Quraysh, Allah, mighty and majestic, will humiliate him. This hadith was not narrated from al-Zuhri except by Salih; Ibrahim alone transmitted it."
"3205","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the price of the dog and the cat. This hadith was not narrated from al-A'mash except by Isa and Abthar ibn al-Qasim."
"3206","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Nu'aym ibn Hammad narrated to us, he said: Uqbah ibn Khalid al-Sakuni narrated to us, from Musa ibn Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, from his father, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you eat food, take off your sandals, for that is more restful for your feet. This hadith is not narrated from Anas except with this chain; Uqbah alone transmitted it."
"3207","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: Bakr ibn Mudar narrated to us, from Ja'far ibn Rabi'ah, that he heard Abu al-Khayr reporting from Abd al-Rahman ibn Wa'lah that he asked Ibn Abbas, saying: We raid this West, and they are people of religion, and they have waterskins in which there is milk and water? So Ibn Abbas said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Tanning is purification."
"3208","And with the same chain: Ja'far ibn Rabi'ah narrated to us, from Abu Marzuq al-Tujibi, from Hanash al-San'ani, from Ruwayfi' ibn Thabit al-Ansari, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: It is not lawful for anyone who believes in Allah and the Last Day to give his water to drink to another man's child."
"3209","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Hamzah narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid ibn Jabir narrated to me, he said: Zayd ibn Artah narrated to me, he said: I heard Jubayr ibn Nufayr narrating from Abu al-Darda, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The encampment of the Muslims on the day of the great battle will be beside a city called Damascus, among the best cities of Sham. This hadith was not narrated from Zayd ibn Artah except by Ibn Jabir."
"3210","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Ishkib al-Saffar al-Kufi narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Abis narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he retired to his bed, would say: My Lord, shield me from Your punishment on the day You resurrect Your servants. This hadith was not narrated from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, except by Ali ibn Abis; Isra'il and others narrated it from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Ubaydah."
"3211","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn al-Mughirah al-Massisi narrated to us, he said: Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every intoxicant is unlawful. This hadith was not narrated from Umar ibn al-Mughirah except by Abdullah ibn Yusuf."
"3212","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, from Atiyyah ibn Qays, from Qaza'ah ibn Yahya, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he said: Allah hears the one who praises Him, would say: O Allah, our Lord, to You belongs praise, filling the heavens and filling the earth, and filling whatever else You will after that; O Possessor of praise and glory, the truest thing the servant has said, and we are all Your servants; none can withhold what You give, and the fortune of the fortunate avails him nothing against You. This hadith was not narrated from Abu Sa'id except through the hadith of Qaza'ah ibn Yahya."
"3213","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Hashim al-Bayruti narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Awza'i narrating from Isma'il ibn Ubaydullah al-Makhzumi, from Ali ibn Abdullah ibn al-Abbas, from his father, he said: There was displayed to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) what would be opened up for his community after him, region after region, and he was delighted by that, so Allah, mighty and majestic, sent down: And your Lord will surely give you, and you will be pleased. He said: So Allah gave him in Paradise a thousand palaces, in every palace what befits him of youths and servants. This hadith was not narrated from Isma'il ibn Ubaydullah except by al-Awza'i, and it was not narrated from al-Awza'i except by Amr ibn Hashim and Sufyan al-Thawri; Yahya ibn Yaman alone transmitted it from Sufyan."
"3214","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Hashim al-Bayruti narrated to us, he said: Idris ibn Ziyad al-Alhani narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ziyad al-Alhani narrated to us, from Abu Umamah, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Allah, mighty and majestic, has made the salutation of peace the greeting of my community and a security for our dhimmis. This hadith was not narrated from Muhammad ibn Ziyad except by Idris ibn Ziyad; Amr ibn Hashim alone transmitted it."
"3215","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: Bakr ibn Mudar narrated to me, from Sakhr ibn Abdullah ibn Harmalah, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to his wives: Your affair after me weighs upon me, and none but the steadfast will endure with you. Then she said: May Allah give your father to drink from Salsabil; and he had gifted the wives of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forty thousand. This hadith was not narrated from Sakhr ibn Abdullah except by Bakr ibn Mudar."
"3216","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: Bakr narrated to me, from Ja'far ibn Rabi'ah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Hurmuz al-A'raj, from Abdullah ibn Malik ibn Buhaynah, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prostrated, he kept his upper arms away from his body until the whiteness of his armpits could be seen. This hadith is not narrated from Abdullah ibn Buhaynah except with this chain; Bakr ibn Mudar alone transmitted it."
"3217","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Yusuf and Shu'ayb ibn Yahya narrated to us, they said: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Abi Ja'far, from Abdullah ibn Abi Qatadah, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever sits upon the bed of an absent woman, a serpent will be appointed for him on the Day of Resurrection."
"3218","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi al-Sari al-Asqalani narrated to us, he said: Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Layth, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Shurayh ibn Hani, from Bilal, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would wipe over the leather socks and the head-cover. This hadith was not narrated from Habib except by al-Layth; Mu'tamir alone transmitted it."
"3219","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Shu'ayb ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Ayyub informed us, from Ibn Jurayj, that Abu al-Zubayr informed him that he heard Jabir ibn Abdullah say: In the days of Khaybar we ate horses and wild donkeys, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us the domestic donkey. This hadith was not narrated from Ibn Jurayj except by Yahya ibn Ayyub."
"3220","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Shu'ayb ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Jabbar ibn Umar informed us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not turn around when he walked; his cloak would sometimes catch on a tree or something and he would not turn until they lifted it off, for they would joke and laugh, and they felt secure from his turning, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"3221","Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Hashim al-Bayruti narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Darraj, from Abdullah ibn Hubayrah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Hujayrah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah has forgiven a man who removed a branch of thorns from the path of the Muslims, with what preceded of his sin. This hadith was not narrated from Ibn Hujayrah except by Ibn Hubayrah; Ibn Lahi'ah alone transmitted it."
"3222","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Nu'aym ibn Hammad narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Usamah ibn Zayd, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Jibril commanded me to give precedence to the eldest, or he said: to give precedence in the takbir. This hadith was not narrated from Nafi' except by Usamah; Ibn al-Mubarak alone transmitted it."
"3223","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Abi al-Fayyad al-Barqi narrated to us, he said: Ashhab ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Mishrah ibn Ha'an, from Uqbah ibn Amir, from Hudhayfah ibn al-Yaman, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: My companions will have a slip after me, which Allah will forgive them on account of their companionship, but people after them will take them as precedent, and Allah will cast them down on their nostrils into the Fire."
"3224","And with the same chain: from Ibn Lahi'ah, from Mishrah ibn Ha'an, from Uqbah ibn Amir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever acts with deliberation hits the mark, or nearly, and whoever hastens errs, or nearly. These two hadiths were not narrated from Mishrah except by Ibn Lahi'ah, nor from Ibn Lahi'ah except by Ashhab; Ibrahim alone transmitted them."
"3225","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Hashim al-Bayruti narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Hayyan Abu Khalid al-Ahmar narrated to us, from Humayd al-Tawil, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have been commanded to fight people until they say: There is no god but Allah; when they say it, they have protected their blood and their wealth from me, except by its right. It was said: And what is its right? He said: Adultery after chastity, or disbelief after Islam, or the killing of a soul, for which he is killed. This concluding wording of the hadith was not narrated from Humayd except by Abu Khalid al-Ahmar; Amr ibn Hashim alone transmitted it."
"3226","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Amr narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Husayn narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, mighty and majestic, does not take away knowledge by snatching it from people; rather He takes it by taking the scholars, until, when He leaves no scholar, people take ignorant leaders; they are asked and give fatwa without knowledge, so they go astray and lead astray. This hadith was not narrated from Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Husayn except by Amr ibn Hashim."
"3227","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Hamzah narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz, that Nafi' narrated to him that Ibn Umar, when he combined Maghrib and Isha, said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) hastening likewise, and he prayed them once, then I never saw him pray them before that nor after it. This hadith was not narrated from Abd al-Aziz except by Yahya ibn Hamzah."
"3228","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Abdullah narrated to us, he said: Yahya narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid ibn Jabir, that Isma'il ibn Ubaydullah narrated to him, from Umm al-Darda, from Abu al-Darda, he said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on one of his journeys on a hot day, and a man would place his hand upon his head because of the intense heat; none of us was fasting except the Prophet of Allah and Ibn Rawahah."
"3229","And with the same chain: Yahya narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Waqid, that Abu al-Munib al-Jurashi narrated to him, he said: Abu Hurayrah narrated to me, he said: My close friend Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) enjoined upon me three things which I guard: the forenoon supererogatory prayer, never to abandon it whether traveling or resident; fasting three days of every month; and not to sleep except upon witr, completing the lifetime with that. This hadith was not narrated from Abu al-Munib except by Zayd, nor was it narrated from Zayd except by Yahya and Sadaqah ibn Khalid."
"3230","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from Uqbah ibn Ubayd al-Ta'i, from Bushayr ibn Yasar, he said: I said to Anas: What have you disapproved of in our condition compared with the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: You do not straighten the rows completely. This hadith was not narrated from Bushayr ibn Yasar except by Uqbah ibn Ubayd."
"3231","And with the same chain: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from Asim al-Ahwal, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever deliberately lies about me, let him take his seat in the Fire. This hadith was not narrated from Asim, from Anas, except by Abu Mu'awiyah; and Abu Isma'il al-Mu'addib narrated it from Asim, from Umar ibn Bashir, from Anas."
"3232","Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, he said: Ishaq narrated to us, from Isa al-Iskandarani, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When Allah loves a people He puts them to trial. This hadith was not narrated from Anas except by Isa, nor from Isa except by Ishaq al-Azraq al-Basri, who is not the Wasiti one; Ibn Lahi'ah alone transmitted it."
"3233","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Nu'aym ibn Hammad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Talhah al-Taymi narrated to us, from Abu Suhayl Nafi' ibn Malik, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Sad ibn Abi Waqqas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out preparing an expedition, and al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib appeared, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This is the uncle of your Prophet, the most generous of Quraysh in hand, and the most joining of kinship, and sometimes he said: and the most tender."
"3234","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Hamzah narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Maryam, that Qaza'ah narrated to him, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever eats of this tree, let him not come near our mosque. This hadith was not narrated from Qaza'ah except by Yazid."
"3235","And with his chain: from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioned the day of Ashura, and magnified it, then said to those around him: Whoever among you has not eaten, let him fast this day of his; and whoever among you has already eaten, let him fast the remainder of his day. This hadith was not narrated from Qaza'ah except by Yazid."
"3236","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Nu'aym ibn Hammad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Thawr narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Isma'il ibn Umayyah, from Abdullah ibn Rafi', the freedman of Umm Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took my hand and said: Allah, mighty and majestic, created the soil on Saturday, and created therein the mountains on Sunday, and the trees on Monday, and the hateful things on Tuesday, and light on Wednesday, and spread therein beasts on Thursday, and counted as women count, and created Adam after Asr on Friday, in the last hour of the daytime, between Asr and night. This hadith was not narrated from Abdullah except by Isma'il; Ibn Jurayj alone transmitted it."
"3237","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Abu al-Khayr, from Uqbah ibn Amir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no deed of day and night but is sealed; so when the believer falls ill, the angels say: Our Lord, such-and-such a servant of Yours, You have confined him; so He says: Seal for him upon his deed until he recovers or dies. This hadith was not narrated from Yazid except by Ibn Lahi'ah."
"3238","And with the same chain: Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated to us, from Sad ibn Mas'ud, that he heard Abd al-Rahman ibn Jubayr ibn Nufayr narrating from his father, that he heard Abu al-Darda reporting that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I am the first for whom permission will be given to raise his head; so I shall raise my head and recognize my community, on my right and on my left. So it was said to him: How will you recognize them, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Radiant with marks of prostration, and their offspring with their light before them. This hadith is not narrated from Abu al-Darda except with this chain; Ibn Lahi'ah alone transmitted it."
"3239","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: Mu'awiyah ibn Salih narrated to me, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Khalid ibn Ma'dan, from Kathir ibn Murrah, from Uqbah ibn Amir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The one who recites the Quran secretly is like the one who gives charity secretly, and the one who recites the Quran aloud is like the one who gives charity aloud. This hadith was not narrated from Khalid except by Yahya; Mu'awiyah ibn Salih alone transmitted it."
"3240","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Hashim al-Bayruti narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to me, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Pray over your dead by night and day, the young and the old, male and female, four takbirs. This hadith was not narrated from Abu al-Zubayr except by Ibn Lahi'ah; Amr ibn Hashim alone transmitted it."
"3241","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Shu'ayb ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: al-Layth ibn Sad narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Sad, from Muhammad ibn Zayd ibn al-Muhajir ibn Qunfudh, from Abu Umamah al-Bahili, from Abdullah ibn Unays al-Juhani, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Among the gravest of grave sins are associating partners with Allah, disobedience to parents, and the engulfing oath; and no swearer swears by Allah a restraint oath in which he inserts even the like of a gnat's wing but it becomes a black spot upon his heart on the Day of Resurrection. This hadith is not narrated from Abdullah ibn Unays except with this chain; al-Layth alone transmitted it."
"3242","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Ulayy ibn Rabah narrated to me, from his father, from Abu Qays, the freedman of Amr ibn al-As, from Amr ibn al-As, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The difference between our fasting and the fasting of the People of the Book is the predawn meal. This hadith was not narrated from Amr except with this chain; Musa ibn Ulayy alone transmitted it."
"3243","And with the same chain: from Abu Qays, the freedman of Amr ibn al-As, he said: Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As sent me to Umm Salamah, the wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: Ask her: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kiss while fasting? If she says: No, then say: But Aishah reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would kiss while fasting. So Abu Qays said: I came to her, and she said: Free or slave? I said: Slave. She said: Come near. So I drew near and said: Abdullah ibn Amr has sent me to you to ask you: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kiss while fasting? She said: No. So I said: Aishah reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would kiss while fasting? She said: Perhaps he would kiss her, for he could not restrain himself out of love for her. This hadith is not narrated from Abdullah ibn Amr, from Aishah, except with this chain; Musa alone transmitted it."
"3244","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: Attaf ibn Khalid al-Makhzumi narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Abi Humayd narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir narrated to me, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, that he prepared food for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his companions and invited them; when they entered and the food was set down, a man among the people said: I am fasting. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Your brother invited you and went to trouble for you, then you say: I am fasting? Break your fast, then fast a day in its place if you wish. This hadith is not narrated from Abu Sa'id except with this chain; Hammad ibn Abi Humayd alone transmitted it, and he is Muhammad ibn Abi Humayd; the people of Madinah say: Hammad ibn Abi Humayd."
"3245","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Hashim al-Bayruti narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Abi Karimah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever asks about me, or it pleases him to look at me, let him look at Ash'ath, disheveled, rolled-up, who never laid a brick upon a brick nor a reed upon a reed; a banner was raised for him and he hastened toward it; today is the training ground, and tomorrow the race, and the goal is Paradise and Hell. This hadith was not narrated from Hisham except by Sulayman; Amr alone transmitted it."
"3246","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Walid al-Zubaydi narrated to me, from al-Zuhri, he said: Anbasah ibn Sa'id ibn al-As informed me, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent Aban ibn Sa'id ibn al-As to Madinah in a detachment toward Najd; Abu Hurayrah said: They came to us after we had conquered Khaybar before we distributed, and the halters of their horses were of palm fiber; Aban ibn Sa'id said: O Messenger of Allah, allot to us. So I said: O Messenger of Allah, do not allot to them. Aban said: You, O hyrax, come down from the mountaintop; but he did not allot them anything of the booty. This hadith was not narrated from al-Zuhri except by Muhammad ibn al-Walid al-Zubaydi."
"3247","Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: al-Layth narrated to me, he said: Hisham ibn Sad narrated to me, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever fasts a day in the path of Allah, Allah will distance him from the Fire by seventy autumns. This hadith was not narrated from Zayd ibn Aslam except by Hisham; al-Layth alone transmitted it."
"3248","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: al-Layth ibn Sad narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Abdullah ibn al-Had narrated to me, from Musa ibn Sarjis, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Aishah, she said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was dying, and with him was a cup in which there was water; he would put his hand into the cup, then wipe his face with the water, then say: O Allah, help me against the throes of death. This hadith was not narrated from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad except by Musa, nor from Musa except by Ibn al-Had; al-Layth alone transmitted it."
"3249","And with the same chain: Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Hamzah narrated to us, from al-Nu'man ibn al-Mundhir, that he asked Ata ibn Abi Rabah: Was concession granted to women to pray upon mounts? He said: They were granted no concession in that, neither in hardship nor in ease. This hadith was not narrated from al-Nu'man except by Yahya."
"3250","And with the same chain: Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Hamzah narrated to us, from al-Nu'man ibn al-Mundhir, from Makhul, he said: Huwaytib ibn Abd al-Uzza was with Abdullah ibn Umar on a journey, and Abdullah began praying upon his mount, nodding with his head toward whichever direction he was traveling; Huwaytib said to him: Did you hear this, O Abu Abd al-Rahman, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? Abdullah laughed and said: Yes, I heard it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"3251","And with the same chain: Yahya ibn Hamzah narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Thabit ibn Thawban narrated to us, that his father informed him that he asked Makhul about the fear prayer. He said: Abdullah ibn Umar would narrate that he prayed it with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pronounced the takbir, and a group of us lined up behind him, while another group faced the enemy; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) bowed with them one rak'ah and prostrated two prostrations, like half the dawn prayer; then they withdrew and faced the enemy, and the other group came and prayed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he did likewise; then he gave the salutation, and every man of the two groups stood and bowed for himself one rak'ah and two prostrations. This hadith was not narrated from Makhul except by Ibn Thawban; Yahya ibn Hamzah alone transmitted it."
"3252","And with the same chain: Yahya ibn Hamzah narrated to us, from al-Zubaydi, that al-Zuhri narrated to him, from Safwan ibn Abdullah ibn Safwan, from Umm al-Darda, from Ka'b ibn Asim al-Ash'ari, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fasting while traveling is not part of righteousness. This hadith was not narrated from al-Zubaydi except by Yahya."
"3253","And with the same chain: Yahya narrated to us, from al-Nu'man ibn al-Mundhir, from Makhul, he said: Amr ibn Abasah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever fasts a day in the path of Allah, the Fire will be distanced from him by a journey of a hundred years. This hadith was not narrated from al-Nu'man except by Yahya."
"3254","And with the same chain: Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to me, he said: Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated to us, from Umarah ibn Ghaziyyah, from Ibn Shihab, from Ibn Ka'b ibn Malik, from his father, and he was one of the three men whom Allah forgave, he said: Mu'adh ibn Jabal had taken on debt in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) until it encompassed his wealth; and Mu'adh was among the righteous companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So Mu'adh said: O Messenger of Allah, when I accepted Islam I did not intend to withhold from Islam any wealth I owned; I spent my wealth in the cause of Islam, and that left upon me a great debt; so call my creditors and ask them to be lenient with me; if they are lenient with me, that is the way of it, and if they refuse, then strip me of my wealth for them. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called his creditors and offered them to be lenient with him, but they said: We love our wealth. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) handed over all of Mu'adh's wealth to them; then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent Mu'adh to part of Yemen to compensate him, and Mu'adh obtained in Yemen from the perquisites of governorship wealth; then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed away while Mu'adh was in Yemen; part of the people of Yemen apostatized, and Mu'adh fought them, along with commanders whom the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had appointed over Yemen, until they entered Islam; then he came in the caliphate of Abu Bakr al-Siddiq with great wealth, and Umar ibn al-Khattab came to him and said: You have come with great wealth, and I think you should go to Abu Bakr and seek his sanction; if he sanctions it for you it is wholesome for you, otherwise hand it to him. So Mu'adh said: You know, O Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me only to compensate me when he handed my wealth to my creditors; I shall not hand to Abu Bakr anything of what I have brought unless he asks me; if he asks me I shall hand it to him, and if he does not take I shall keep it. Umar said to him: I intend for you and myself nothing but good. Then Umar stood and left; when he turned away he called him back, and he returned, and said: I shall obey you; but for a dream I saw I would not have obeyed you: I saw myself in sleep drowning in deep water, and I saw you take my hand and rescue me from it; so let us go to Abu Bakr. So they went until they entered upon him, and Mu'adh mentioned to him much as he had spoken with Umar concerning his creditors and what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) intended of compensating him; then he informed him of the wealth he had brought, until he said: And even this whip of mine is of what I have brought; take whatever you see fit, and sanction whatever you see fit. Abu Bakr said to him: It is all yours, O Mu'adh. Umar turned to Mu'adh and said: O Mu'adh, now it is wholesome for you. So Mu'adh became among the wealthiest of the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and Mu'adh was the first man to obtain wealth from the perquisites of governorship. Ibn Shihab said: So the practice continued concerning Mu'adh that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stripped him of his wealth and did not order it to be sold, and in the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) there is a good example. This hadith was not narrated from al-Zuhri in this completeness except by Yazid ibn Abi Habib and Umarah ibn Ghaziyyah; Ibn Lahi'ah alone transmitted it."
"3255","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: Mu'awiyah ibn Salih narrated to me, that Azhar ibn Sa'id narrated to him, from Abu Kabshah, the companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: While the Messenger of Allah was sitting, a woman passed by him, so he went to his family; then he came out to us with his head dripping water, and we said: O Messenger of Allah, as though something happened? He said: Yes; so-and-so woman passed by me, and desire for women fell into my soul, so I went to one of my wives; do likewise, for approaching the lawful is among the best of your deeds. This hadith is not narrated from Abu Kabshah except with this chain; Mu'awiyah ibn Salih alone transmitted it."
"3256","And with the same chain: Mu'awiyah ibn Salih narrated to us, from Abu Halbas Yazid ibn Maysarah, he said: I heard Umm al-Darda say: I heard Abu al-Darda say: I heard Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) — I never heard him use his kunyah before that nor after it — say: Allah, mighty and majestic, said: O Isa, I shall send after you a community: if what they love befalls them they praise and thank, and if what they hate befalls them they reckon reward and endure, with neither forbearance nor knowledge. He said: O Lord, how can this be, with neither knowledge nor forbearance? He said: I shall give them of My forbearance and My knowledge. This hadith was not narrated from Umm al-Darda except by Yazid ibn Maysarah; Mu'awiyah ibn Salih alone transmitted it."
"3257","And with the same chain: Mu'awiyah ibn Salih narrated to me, from Rabi'ah ibn Yazid, from Abu Idris al-Khawlani, from Abu Umamah al-Bahili, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Hold to night prayer, for it is the practice of the righteous before you, and a means of nearness to your Lord, and an expiation for evil deeds. This hadith was not narrated from Abu Umamah except by Abu Idris, nor from Abu Idris except by Rabi'ah; Mu'awiyah ibn Salih alone transmitted it."
"3258","And with the same chain: Mu'awiyah ibn Salih narrated to me, from Rashid ibn Sad, from Abu Umamah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Beware the discernment of the believer, for he looks with the light of Allah. This hadith is not narrated from Abu Umamah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), except with this chain; Mu'awiyah alone transmitted it."
"3259","And with the same chain: Mu'awiyah narrated to me, from Sa'id ibn Hani, from al-Irbad ibn Sariyah al-Sulami, he said: I sold a young camel to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then I came demanding payment, and said: O Messenger of Allah, pay me the price of my young camel. So he paid him an aged camel, and he said: O Messenger of Allah, this is better than my young camel. He said: It is better for you; the best of people are the best in repayment. This hadith is not narrated from al-Irbad except with this chain."
"3260","And with the same chain: Mu'awiyah narrated to me, he said: al-Ala ibn al-Harith narrated to me, from Makhul, from Ziyad ibn Jariyah, from Habib ibn Maslamah: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would grant an extra share on campaign of a quarter after the fifth, and would grant when returning a third after the fifth. This hadith was not narrated from al-Ala except by Mu'awiyah."
"3261","And with the same chain: Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Jubayr ibn Nufayr, from his father, from Awf ibn Malik al-Ashja'i, he said: We would treat with ruqyah in the pre-Islamic period, so we said: O Messenger of Allah, how should we treat in that? He said: Present your ruqyahs to me. He said: There is no harm in ruqyahs so long as there is no shirk. This hadith is not narrated from Awf except with this chain; Mu'awiyah alone transmitted it."
"3262","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Abi Talhah, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Before the Hour there will be deceitful years, in which the trustworthy will be accused and the accused will be trusted, and the Ruwaybidah will speak. They said: And what is the Ruwaybidah? He said: The fool who speaks concerning public affairs."
"3263","And with the same chain: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Abu al-Aswad, from Urwah, from Ali ibn Abi Talib, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever builds a mosque for Allah, Allah will build for him a house in Paradise. This hadith is not narrated from Ali except with this chain; Ibn Lahi'ah alone transmitted it."
"3264","And with the same chain: from Abu al-Aswad, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from his brother Abdullah ibn Muhammad, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Were it not that your people are fresh from disbelief, I would demolish the Ka'bah and make for it two doors, and include in it what Quraysh left out, being unable to do it. This hadith was not narrated from al-Qasim, from his brother, except by Abu al-Aswad; Ibn Lahi'ah alone transmitted it."
"3265","Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, he said: Mahdi ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Marzuq ibn Abi al-Hudhayl, from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah, from Ibn Abbas, from Umar ibn al-Khattab, that he entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he had withdrawn from his wives, and there he was upon a bed of woven cords; I looked and saw nothing in the house to catch the eye except tanned ox hides whose smell had spread. So I said: You are the Messenger of Allah and His chosen one, while Chosroes and Caesar live in brocade and silk? He said: Are you in doubt, O son of al-Khattab? Those are a people whose reckoning is theirs. This hadith was not narrated from Marzuq except by al-Walid ibn Muslim."
"3266","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: al-Haytham ibn Humayd narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn al-Harith narrated to me, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah al-Bahili, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever walks to a prescribed prayer while purified, his reward is like the reward of the pilgrim in ihram; and whoever walks to the forenoon glorification, his reward is like the reward of the one performing umrah; and a prayer upon a prayer with no idle talk between them is a record in Illiyyun. This hadith was not narrated from Yahya ibn al-Harith in this completeness except by al-Haytham ibn Humayd."
"3267","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Ishkib al-Saffar al-Kufi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Layth ibn Abi Sulaym, from Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Ata, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever among you sleeps with traces of grease on him before washing his hand, and something befalls him, let him blame none but himself. This hadith was not narrated from Muhammad ibn Amr except by Layth; Muhammad alone transmitted it."
"3268","And with the same chain: Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Sumay', from al-Hasan, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: Evil is the food, the food of the wedding feast to which the rich are invited and the poor are left out; and whoever is invited to a feast and does not answer has disobeyed Allah and His Messenger. I did not say it. This hadith was not narrated from Isma'il except by Muhammad ibn Fudayl."
"3269","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi al-Sari al-Asqalani narrated to us, he said: Abu Isam Rawwad ibn al-Jarrah narrated to us, from Sharik ibn Abdullah, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What has become of so-and-so, an orphan girl who was with her? I said: We have sent her to her husband. He said: Did you not send with her a slave girl to beat the tambourine and sing? She said: Saying what? He said, saying: The grain. This hadith was not narrated from Hisham ibn Urwah except by Sharik, nor from Sharik except by Rawwad; Muhammad ibn Abi al-Sari alone transmitted it."
"3270","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Ghani ibn Sa'id al-Thaqafi narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Abd al-Rahman al-San'ani narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three are obligatory upon me and voluntary for you: witr, the toothstick, and night prayer. This hadith was not narrated from Hisham except by Musa; Abd al-Ghani ibn Sa'id alone transmitted it."
"3271","Bakr narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Ishkib al-Saffar narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Bayan ibn Bishr, from al-Sha'bi, from Adi ibn Hatim, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, we hunt with these dogs. He said: When you release your trained dog and mention Allah's name over it, then what it holds for you is yours, even if it kills, unless it eats; if it eats then do not eat, for I fear it held it only for itself; and if other dogs join them, do not eat. This hadith was not narrated from Bayan except by Muhammad ibn Fudayl."
"3272","And with the same chain: Muhammad ibn Fudayl ibn Ghazwan narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The household of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never ate their fill of wheat bread until he passed away, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"3273","And from Abu Hurayrah, he said: I saw seventy of the people of the Bench, not one of them having a cloak; either a sheet or a wrap which they had tied around their necks; some of it reaching half the shin, and some reaching the ankles, and he gathers it with his hand for fear his nakedness would show."
"3274","And from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The distance between the disbeliever's shoulders in the Fire is a three-day journey for the swift rider."
"3275","And from Abu Hurayrah, he said: Severe hunger struck me, so I came to Umar and asked him to open for me a verse of Allah's Book; he entered his house, then opened it to me; I went a short distance, then fell upon my face from hunger, and there was the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) standing over my head. He said: Abu Hurayrah. I said: At your service, O Messenger of Allah, and glad tidings to you. So I informed him of my state, and he recognized what was in me; he went to his dwelling and ordered for me a large cup of milk; I drank from it, then he said: Return, O Abu Hurayrah. So I returned and drank until my back straightened and became like an arrow; then I met Umar and mentioned to him what had happened to me, and I said to him: Allah undertook that through one more deserving of it than you; I had asked you to recite the verse to me though I read it better than you. Umar said: By Allah, I would have loved to have admitted you more than red camels."
"3276","And from Abu Hurayrah, he said: A man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) seeking hospitality, but he had nothing with which to host him. So he said: Is there no man to host this one, may Allah have mercy on him? Then a man of the Ansar came and took him to his dwelling, and said to his wife: Honor the guest of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). She said: By Allah, we have nothing but the children's food. He said to her: Put the children to sleep, light the lamp, bring it near to the guest of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, show him as though we eat with him, extinguish the lamp, and leave it for the guest of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. So she did. He said: And Abu Talhah came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the next morning, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah has indeed marveled — or: laughed — at so-and-so and so-and-so, meaning Abu Talhah and his wife; and He sent down concerning them this verse: And they prefer others over themselves, even though they are in need. None narrated these hadiths from Fudayl ibn Ghazwan except Muhammad ibn Fudayl."
"3277","And with the same chain: Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Umarah ibn al-Qa'qa', from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The first group to enter Paradise of my community will be upon the image of the moon on the night of full moon; and those who follow them upon the light of the brightest star in the sky; they neither urinate nor defecate, neither spit nor blow their noses; their combs are of gold, their sweat is musk, their censers are aloeswood, their spouses are wide-eyed maidens, their character upon the character of a single man, upon the image of their father Adam, sixty cubits. This hadith was not narrated from Umarah except by Muhammad ibn Fudayl."
"3278","And with the same chain: Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Sad al-Ansari narrated to us, from Habib ibn Salim, he said: Abu Hurayrah narrated to us, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: My likeness and the likeness of the prophets is as the likeness of a man who built a house and completed and beautified it, but there remained from one of its corners the place of a brick; people began circling his building, marveling and saying: Why did he not place a brick here to complete his building? So I am that; I am the seal of the prophets, there is no prophet after me."
"3279","And with his chain: Abu Hurayrah narrated to us, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: My likeness and yours is as the likeness of a man who kindled a fire, and these beasts and moths began falling into it, while he drives them away from it, but they plunge into it; I am holding your waists: Come away from the Fire, come away from the Fire, but you overcome me and plunge into it. These two hadiths were not narrated from Habib ibn Salim except by Muhammad ibn Sad; Muhammad ibn Fudayl alone transmitted them."
"3280","And with the same chain: Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Abd al-Wahid ibn Ayman, from his father, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, he said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) dug the Trench, severe hardship struck the Muslims, until the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) bound a rock upon his belly from hunger, as did his companions. So I slaughtered a young she-goat, ordered my family, and they baked some barley they had and cooked the young goat; then I invited the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him of what I had prepared. He said: Go and prepare what you have until I come to you. So I went and prepared what we had; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came with the whole army. I said: O Messenger of Allah, it is but a young she-goat which I prepared for you and a few of your companions. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Bring a bowl. So I brought him a bowl; then he said: Put stew in it. Then he invoked blessing upon it, then said: In the name of Allah. Then he said: Admit ten men. So I did; when they ate and were full they went out, and I admitted another ten, until the whole army was covered, while the food remained as it was. This hadith was not narrated from Abd al-Wahid ibn Ayman except by Muhammad ibn Fudayl."
"3281","Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, he said: Darraj narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Hujayrah, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will come upon my community a time when reciters increase and jurists decrease, knowledge is taken away, and harj increases. They said: And what is harj? He said: Killing among you. Then after that will come a time when men recite the Quran and it does not pass their throats; then will come a time when the hypocrite and the polytheist dispute with the believer. This hadith was not narrated from Ibn Hujayrah except by Darraj; Ibn Lahi'ah alone transmitted it."
"3282","And with the same chain: Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj ibn Artah, from Qatadah, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sacrificed two horned black-and-white rams; he brought one near and said: In the name of Allah, from You and to You; this is on behalf of Muhammad and his household. Then he brought the other near and said: In the name of Allah, from You and to You; this is on behalf of whoever professes Your oneness of my community. This hadith was not narrated from al-Hajjaj except by Abu Mu'awiyah."
"3283","And with the same chain: from al-Hajjaj ibn Artah, from al-Zuhri, from Hakim ibn Bashir, from Abu Ayyub al-Ansari, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best charity is upon the hostile kindred. This hadith was not narrated from al-Zuhri except by Hajjaj ibn Artah."
"3284","And with the same chain: from al-Hajjaj, from Qatadah, from Anas, that Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf married a woman for the weight of a date pit of gold. This hadith was not narrated from al-Hajjaj except by Abu Mu'awiyah."
"3285","And with the same chain: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from Khalid ibn Ilyas, from Salih, the freedman of al-Taw'amah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would rise in prayer upon the fronts of his feet. This hadith was not narrated from Salih except by Khalid ibn Ilyas; Abu Mu'awiyah alone transmitted it."
"3286","And with the same chain: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Muslim, from al-Zuhri, from Anas, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Here I am, for Hajj and Umrah together. This hadith was not narrated from al-Zuhri except by Isma'il."
"3287","And with the same chain: Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Amir ibn Yahya, from Hanash al-San'ani, from Ibn Abbas, that some men of Himyar came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asking him, and a man among them said: I love women, and I love to approach my wife from behind; what do you think? So Allah the Exalted sent down: Your women are a tilth for you, so come to your tilth as you will. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Approach her from the front and from behind, so long as that is in the private part. This hadith was not narrated from Yazid ibn Abi Habib except by Ibn Lahi'ah."
"3288","Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Abu al-Aswad, from Abdullah ibn Rafi', from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is overtaken by Ramadan while another Ramadan is still due upon him which he did not make up, it will not be accepted from him. This hadith is not narrated from Abu Hurayrah except with this chain; Ibn Lahi'ah alone transmitted it."
"3289","And with the same chain: from Ibn Lahi'ah, from Bakr ibn Sawadah, from Ziyad ibn Nu'aym, from Wafa ibn Shurayh, from Ruwayfi' ibn Thabit, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever invokes blessing upon Muhammad and says: O Allah, settle him in the near station with You on the Day of Resurrection, my intercession becomes due for him. This hadith is not narrated from Ruwayfi' except with this chain; Ibn Lahi'ah alone transmitted it."
"3290","And with the same chain: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Abu al-Aswad, from Urwah, from Aishah, that she asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the bathhouse, and he said: After me there will be bathhouses, and there is no good in bathhouses for women. She said: O Messenger of Allah, what if she enters it with a waist wrap? He said: No; even if she enters it with a wrap, a bodice, and a headscarf; there is no woman who removes her headscarf outside her husband's house but she has lifted the veil between her and her Lord. This hadith was not narrated from Urwah except by Abu al-Aswad; Ibn Lahi'ah alone transmitted it."
"3291","And with the same chain: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Bukayr ibn Abdullah ibn al-Ashajj, from Abu Bakr ibn al-Munkadir, from Amr ibn Sulaym al-Zuraqi, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Sa'id al-Khudri, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Bathing on Friday is incumbent upon every pubescent one, and that he touch perfume, even if from his household's perfume. This hadith was not narrated from Amr ibn Sulaym except by Abu Bakr ibn al-Munkadir; Bukayr ibn Abdullah alone transmitted it."
"3292","And with the same chain: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Abbad ibn Salim, from Salim ibn Abdullah, from his father, from Umar ibn al-Khattab, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whomever Allah intends good for, He gives him understanding in religion. This hadith was not narrated from Salim except by Abbad, nor from Abbad except by Ibn Lahi'ah and Amr ibn al-Harith."
"3293","And with the same chain: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, that Abd al-Rahman ibn Shimasah narrated to him, from Tabi' al-Hijri, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Udays al-Balawi, he said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: People will emerge who pass out of religion as the arrow passes out of the game, killed at Mount Lebanon or at Mount Galilee. Ibn Lahi'ah said: So Ibn Udays was killed at Mount Lebanon or at Mount Galilee. This hadith is not narrated from Abd al-Rahman ibn Udays except with this chain."
"3294","And with the same chain: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, he said: Abu Zura'ah Amr ibn Jabir narrated to us, he said: I heard Sahl ibn Sad al-Sa'idi say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not revile Tubba', for he had accepted Islam. This hadith is not narrated from Sahl ibn Sad except with this chain; Ibn Lahi'ah alone transmitted it."
"3295","And with the same chain: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Bukayr ibn Abdullah ibn al-Ashajj, from al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn Abi Rafi', that he narrated to him that his father narrated to him that Abu Rafi' narrated to him that he was the keeper of the foreleg. He said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: Hand me the foreleg. So I handed it to him; then he said: Hand me the foreleg. So I handed it to him; then he said: Hand me the foreleg. So I said: O Prophet of Allah, does a sheep have other than two forelegs? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Had you kept handing me, you would have kept handing me. This hadith was not narrated from al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn Abi Rafi' except by Bukayr ibn Abdullah ibn al-Ashajj."
"3296","And with the same chain: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Khalid ibn Yazid, from Sa'id ibn Abi Hilal, from Utbah ibn Abi Utbah, who narrated to him from Nafi' ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im, from Ibn Abbas, he said: It was said to Umar ibn al-Khattab: Narrate to us about the course of the hour of hardship. So Umar said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to Tabuk in severe heat; we alighted at a stop where thirst struck us and we thought our necks would break; a man would go seeking water and return thinking his neck would break; a man would slaughter his camel, squeeze its dung and drink it, and place what remained upon his liver. So Abu Bakr said: O Messenger of Allah, Allah has accustomed you to good in supplication, so supplicate for us. He said: Do you wish that? He said: Yes. He said: So he raised his hands and did not lower them until the clouds gathered and rained, then settled, and they filled what they had. This hadith was not narrated from Nafi' ibn Jubayr except by Utbah; Sa'id ibn Abi Hilal alone transmitted it."
"3297","And with the same chain: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Malik ibn Marwan al-Madani narrated to us, that Musa ibn Amr ibn Qudamah ibn Maz'un narrated to him, from Salim ibn Abdullah, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when someone died, would say: Advance him before our forerunner Uthman ibn Maz'un; what an excellent forerunner. This hadith was not narrated from Salim except by Musa ibn Amr ibn Qudamah."
"3298","Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: Mu'awiyah ibn Salih narrated to me, from Azhar ibn Sa'id, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Sa'ib al-Hilali, and he is the nephew of Maymunah, the wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Maymunah said: O son of my brother, come that I may treat you with the ruqyah of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So she said: In the name of Allah I treat you, and Allah heals you from every ailment in you; remove the harm, O Lord of people; heal, there is no healer but You. This hadith is not narrated from Maymunah except with this chain; Mu'awiyah ibn Salih alone transmitted it."
"3299","And with the same chain: Mu'awiyah ibn Salih narrated to us, that Abd al-Rahman ibn Jubayr ibn Nufayr narrated to him, from his father, from Ka'b ibn Iyad, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Every community has a trial, and the trial of my community is wealth. This hadith is not narrated from Ka'b ibn Iyad except with this chain; Mu'awiyah ibn Salih alone transmitted it."
"3300","And with the same chain: Mu'awiyah ibn Salih narrated to me, from Kathir ibn al-Harith, from al-Qasim Abu Abd al-Rahman, from Adi ibn Hatim, that he said: O Messenger of Allah, which charity is best? He said: The service of a servant in the path of Allah, or the shade of a tent, or the loan of a fecund she-camel. This hadith is not narrated from Adi ibn Hatim except with this chain; Mu'awiyah alone transmitted it."
"3301","And with the same chain: Mu'awiyah narrated to me, from Damrah ibn Habib, from Anbasah ibn Abi Sufyan, that he heard Umm Habibah, the wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), say: I and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would pray in a single garment, and therein was what was. She said: I pray in it and he prays in it, meaning the garment in which he has intercourse. This hadith was not narrated from Anbasah except by Damrah; Mu'awiyah alone transmitted it."
"3302","And with the same chain: Mu'awiyah narrated to me, that Abd al-Rahman ibn Jubayr ibn Nufayr narrated to him, from his father, from Amr ibn al-Hamiq, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When Allah intends good for a servant, He sweetens him. He said: And do you know what His sweetening him is? They said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: He opens for him a righteous deed before his death, until his Beloved and those around him are pleased with him. This hadith is not narrated from Amr except with this chain; Mu'awiyah alone transmitted it."
"3303","Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Ja'far al-Dimyati narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Majid ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Rawwad narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The martyr is forgiven with the first gush of his blood, and is married to two wide-eyed maidens, and intercedes for seventy of his family; and the frontier guard, when he dies at his post, Allah records for him the reward of his deed until the Day of Resurrection, he is supplied with his provision morning and evening, he is married to seventy maidens, and it is said to him: Stand and intercede until the reckoning is finished. This hadith was not narrated from Ibn Jurayj except by Ibn Abi Rawwad; Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Ja'far alone transmitted it."
"3304","Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi al-Sari al-Asqalani narrated to us, he said: Shu'ayb ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from al-Hasan ibn al-Salt, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever has intercourse with his wife while she is menstruating, and a child is decreed between them and leprosy afflicts him, let him blame none but himself. This hadith was not narrated from al-Zuhri except by al-Hasan ibn al-Salt, a Shaykh of the people of Sham; Ibn Abi al-Sari alone transmitted it."
"3305","Bakr ibn Ahmad ibn Muqbil al-Basri narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Ibrahim, the companion of al-Qusi, narrated to us, he said: I heard my father say: Suwayd Abu Hatim narrated to us, he said: Matar al-Warraq narrated to us, from Hassan ibn Bilal, from Hakim ibn Hizam, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he sent him to Yemen, said: Do not touch the Quran unless you are pure. This hadith was not narrated from Matar al-Warraq except by Suwayd Abu Hatim, and it is not narrated from Hakim ibn Hizam except with this chain."
"3306","Bakr ibn Ahmad ibn Muqbil narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Malik ibn Hawdhah ibn Khalifah al-Bakrawi narrated to us, he said: My uncle Amr ibn Khalifah narrated to us, from Ibn Awn, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abidah, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Keep to the Quran, for it escapes from the chests of men more violently than roaming birds to their homes. This hadith was not narrated from Ibn Awn except by Amr ibn Khalifah; Abd al-Malik ibn Hawdhah alone transmitted it."
"3307","Bakr ibn Muhammad al-Qazzaz al-Basri narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Mu'awiyah al-Jumahi narrated to us, he said: Wuhayb ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would sit after giving the salutation until he said: O Allah, You are Peace and from You is peace; blessed are You, O Possessor of majesty and honor. This hadith was not narrated from Hisham except by Wuhayb, nor from Wuhayb except by Abdullah ibn Mu'awiyah."
"3308","Bakr ibn Ahmad ibn Sadawayh al-Basri narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, he said: Qaza'ah ibn Suwayd narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from al-Qasim ibn Ghannam, from some of his mothers, from Umm Farwah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The most beloved deeds to Allah are prayer at the beginning of its time. None narrated it from Ubaydullah ibn Umar except Qaza'ah ibn Suwayd."
"3309","Those named Bishran: Bishran ibn Abd al-Malik al-Mawsili narrated to us, he said: Ghassan ibn al-Rabi' narrated to us, he said: Thabit ibn Yazid narrated to us, from Burd ibn Sinan, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, that he would lease his land until Rafi' ibn Khadij narrated to him that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade leasing land, so he abandoned that. None narrated it from Burd ibn Sinan except Thabit ibn Yazid; Ghassan ibn al-Rabi' alone transmitted it."
"3310","Bishran narrated to us, he said: Ghassan narrated to us, he said: Thabit narrated to us, from al-Hasan ibn Abi Ja'far, from Muhammad ibn Ziyad, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Does not he who raises his head before the imam fear that Allah will turn his head into a donkey's head?"
"3311","Those named Bujayr: Bujayr ibn Muhammad ibn Jabir al-Muharibi narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: Yahya ibn Ya'la ibn al-Harith al-Muharibi narrated to us, from his father, from Ghaylan ibn Jami' al-Muharibi, from Mansur, from Rib'i ibn Hirash, from Tariq ibn Abdullah al-Muharibi, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you pray, do not spit before you nor to your right, but spit to your left if it is empty, or beneath your foot. This hadith was not narrated from Ghaylan except by Ya'la."
"3312","And with the same chain: from Ghaylan ibn Jami', from Firas ibn Yahya, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Bara ibn Azib: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade a man to slaughter his sacrifice before he prays."
"3313","And with the same chain: Yahya ibn Ya'la narrated to us, from his father, from Bakr ibn Wa'il, from Sa'id ibn Abi Arubah, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None should precede with fasting a day or two before Ramadan, unless it be a fast one of you habitually fasts. None narrated it from Bakr except Ya'la."
"3314","Those named Babawayh: Babawayh ibn Khalid ibn Babawayh al-Ayli narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Yahya al-Ayli narrated to us, he said: Mu'awiyah ibn Abd al-Karim al-Dall narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Sirin narrated to us, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us in one of the two afternoon prayers, Zuhr or Asr, and stood after the two rak'ahs; a man called Dhu al-Yadayn stood up to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, have you forgotten or has the prayer been shortened? He said: Rather I forgot. So he stood and prayed the two rak'ahs, then prostrated two prostrations while sitting, then gave the salutation."
"3315","And with the same chain: Mu'awiyah al-Dall narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Sirin narrated to us, from his sister, from Umm Atiyyah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us wearing gold and silver-plating cups; the women spoke to him about wearing gold, but he refused us, and permitted us silver-plating cups. These two hadiths were not narrated from Mu'awiyah except by Umar ibn Yahya, and we heard them only from this shaykh."
"3316","Those named Buhlul: Buhlul ibn Ishaq ibn Buhlul al-Anbari narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Jud'ani narrated to me, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, bless my community in its early mornings. This hadith was not narrated from Ubaydullah except by Muhammad; Ibn Abi Uways alone transmitted it."
"3317","Those named al-Bakhtari: al-Bakhtari ibn Muhammad ibn al-Bakhtari al-Lakhmi al-Baghdadi, Abu Salih, narrated to us, he said: Kamil ibn Talhah al-Jahdari narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Mughirah, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Aishah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) applied perfume before entering ihram. This hadith was not narrated from Abu Awanah except by Kamil ibn Talhah."
"3318","Al-Bakhtari narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Sama'ah narrated to us, he said: Abu Yusuf the judge narrated to us, from Abu Hanifah, from Abu al-Hudhayl, from Ibn Umar: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted women to go out for the dawn prayer and the night prayer."
"3319","Al-Bakhtari narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn al-Ja'd narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Iyad narrated to us, from Abu Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm, from Amrah, from Aishah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Sacrifice is the day you sacrifice, and breaking fast is the day you break fast."
"3320","Those named Badr: Badr ibn al-Haytham, the Kufan judge, narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Jarrah al-Jawzajani narrated to us, he said: Mu'alla ibn Asad al-Ammi narrated to us, he said: Wuhayb ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Sa'id, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The sons of Adam are upon various levels: among them one born a believer, living a believer, dying a believer; among them one born a disbeliever, living a disbeliever, dying a disbeliever; among them one born a believer, living a believer, dying a disbeliever; and among them one born a disbeliever, living a disbeliever, dying a believer. This hadith was not narrated from Dawud ibn Abi Hind except by Wuhayb, nor from Wuhayb except by Mu'alla; Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Jarrah alone transmitted it."
"3321","Those named Bulbul: Bulbul ibn Ishaq ibn Bulbul al-Khallal al-Basri narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, he said: Mu'adh ibn Hisham narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Samurah, he said: The companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would trade in the sanctuary to Sham."
"3322","The chapter of Ta, those named Tamim: Tamim ibn Muhammad al-Farisi narrated to me, he said: Ya'qub ibn Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Rashid al-Madini, the freedman of Abd al-Rahman ibn Aban ibn Uthman, narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ajlan narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, she said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) missed a youth who used to sit with him, and said: Why do I miss so-and-so? They said: He was seized suddenly, and they called fever sudden seizure. He said: Come with us to visit him. When he entered upon him, the boy wept, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Do not weep, for Jibril, peace be upon him, informed me that fever is my community's share of Hell."
"3323","The chapter of Tha, those named Thabit: Abu Ma'n Thabit ibn Nu'aym al-Huji narrated to us, he said: Adam ibn Abi Iyas al-Asqalani narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Dawud, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Mahmud ibn Labid, from Rafi' ibn Khadij, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Pray dawn in full light, for it is greater in reward. None narrated it from Shu'bah except Adam and Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid, except that Baqiyyah narrated it from Shu'bah, from Dawud al-Basri, and it has been said he is Dawud ibn Abi Hind."
"3324","Thabit Abu Ma'n narrated to us, he said: Adam narrated to us, he said: Qays ibn al-Rabi' narrated to us, from Abu Husayn, from Ibrahim al-Taymi, from his father, from Abu Dharr, he said: Mut'ah was only for the companions of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) exclusively. None narrated it from Abu Husayn except Qays ibn al-Rabi'."
"3325","And with the same chain: Adam narrated to us, he said: Abu Ja'far al-Razi narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Bushayr ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The womb is a branch of the Most Merciful, suspended upon the loins of the Most Merciful, saying: O Allah, join whoever joins me, and cut whoever cuts me. This hadith was not narrated from Abdullah ibn Dinar except by Abu Ja'far al-Razi, nor was it narrated from Abu Ja'far except by Adam and Abu al-Nadr Hashim ibn al-Qasim."
"3326","Thabit narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi al-Sari narrated to us, he said: Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from his father, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is asked about knowledge and conceals it will be bridled on the Day of Resurrection with a bridle of fire. This hadith was not narrated from Sulayman al-Taymi except by his son; Ibn Abi al-Sari alone transmitted it."
"3327","The chapter of Jim, those named Ja'far: Ja'far ibn Muhammad al-Qalanisi al-Ramli narrated to us, he said: Adam ibn Abi Iyas narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us, from Khusayf, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to them: I ask you no wage for it except that you love me for my kinship among you, and preserve toward me the kinship between me and you, and do not harm me."
"3328","Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Abd al-Wahhab al-Hajabi narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Amr ibn Salih, from al-Hasan, from Sa'sa'ah ibn Mu'awiyah, from Abu Dharr, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There are no two Muslims whose three children die before reaching puberty but they are forgiven by virtue of His mercy to them. I said: Increase me, may Allah have mercy on you. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There is no Muslim who spends two pairs of his wealth in the path of Allah but the keepers of Paradise receive him, each of them calling him to what is with them."
"3329","And with the same chain: from Amr ibn Salih, from Humayd ibn Hilal, from Abdullah ibn al-Samit, from Abu Dharr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The donkey, the woman, and the black dog cut off prayer. These two hadiths were not narrated from Amr except by Hammad, nor from Hammad except by al-Hajabi."
"3330","Ja'far ibn Sulayman al-Nawfali al-Madini narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Abdullah al-Uwaysi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Sakhr al-Ayli narrated to me, he said: Abu Ubaydah ibn Muhammad ibn Ammar ibn Yasir narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is pleased to read the Quran fresh as it was revealed, let him read it upon the reading of Ibn Umm Abd. This hadith is not narrated from Ammar except with this chain; al-Uwaysi alone transmitted it."
"3331","Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir al-Hizami narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Dawud al-Mikhraqi narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Sad, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): People are but like a hundred camels, among which you hardly find a single riding camel. This hadith was not narrated from Zayd ibn Aslam except by Hisham ibn Sad; Isma'il alone transmitted it."
"3332","Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Abi Bakr al-Mawsili narrated to us, he said: Zakariyya ibn Isa al-Sha'bi narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, from Abu Salamah, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This is Jibril, and he conveys salam to you. So I said: And upon you be peace and Allah's mercy and blessings. This hadith was not narrated from Zakariyya except by Umar ibn Abi Bakr."
"3333","Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Umar narrated to us, he said: Zakariyya narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married al-Kilabiyyah; when she entered upon him, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) drew near her, and she said: I seek refuge in Allah from you. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You have sought refuge in a Mighty One; join your family. This hadith was not narrated from Zakariyya except by Umar."
"3334","Ja'far ibn Ilyas ibn Sadaqah al-Kabbash al-Misri narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: Ibn Wahb narrated to me, from Malik ibn Anas, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah has placed truth upon the tongue of Umar and his heart. This hadith was not narrated from Malik except by Ibn Wahb, nor from Ibn Wahb except by Ibn Salih."
"3335","Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Nu'aym ibn Hammad narrated to us, he said: Nuh ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, from al-Suddi, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever deliberately lies about me, let him take his seat in the Fire. This hadith was not narrated from al-Suddi except by Nuh; Nu'aym alone transmitted it."
"3336","Jafar narrated to us, he said: Nuaym narrated to us, he said: Nuh narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Said, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked: Who are the family of Muhammad? He said: Every God-fearing person. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited: {Their allies are none but the God-fearing}. No one narrated this hadith from Yahya except Nuh; Nuaym is alone in transmitting it."
"3337","Jafar ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Bahr al-Hujaymi narrated to us, he said: Sulaym ibn Muslim al-Khashshab narrated to us, he said: al-Nadr ibn Arabi narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The one who drinks from vessels of gold and silver only gulps the Fire of Hell into his belly. No one narrated this hadith from al-Nadr except Sulaym; Muhammad ibn Bahr is alone in transmitting it."
"3338","Jafar narrated to us, he said: Abu Jafar al-Nufayli narrated to us, he said: Yunus ibn Rashid narrated to us, from Awn ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hanafiyyah, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Use ithmid (antimony), for it grows the hair, removes impurities, and clears the sight."
"3339","Jafar narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Yahya al-Marwazi narrated to us, he said: Ziyad ibn Abdillah al-Bakkai narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Sulayman, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you wakes from his sleep and wants to perform ablution, let him not put his hand into the vessel until he has washed it, for he does not know where his hand spent the night. No one narrated it from Abd al-Malik except Ziyad; Musa is alone in transmitting it, and it is not narrated from Jabir except with this chain."
"3340","Jafar narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Ibrahim al-Sulami narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Salih narrated to us, from al-Ajlah, from al-Shabi, from Alqamah, from Abdillah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of people are my generation, then the second, then the third, then there will come a people in whom there is no good. No one narrated it from al-Hasan ibn Salih except Yahya, and it is not narrated from Alqamah except through this channel."
"3341","Jafar narrated to us, he said: al-Haytham ibn Ayyub al-Talqani narrated to us, he said: al-Nadr ibn Shumayl narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr al-Ansari who said: My father narrated to me, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to have cupping done and did not wrong the cupper regarding his fee. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad except al-Nadr."
"3342","Jafar ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Yaqub al-Talqani narrated to us, he said: Abdillah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Muslim al-Makki, from Abu Yazid al-Madini, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Keep to the first row, keep to the right side, and beware of (praying in) the row between the pillars. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Yazid except Ismail; Ibn al-Mubarak is alone in transmitting it."
"3343","Jafar narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Yazid al-Bakri al-Juzajani narrated to us, he said: Abu Muti al-Hakam ibn Abdillah al-Sulami narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Zibyan, from Jarir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever does not show mercy to people, Allah will not show mercy to him. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, blessed and exalted, wrote in the Mother of the Book before creating the heavens and the earth: I am Allah, the Most Merciful, the Compassionate; I created the womb (rahim) and derived for it a name from My name; whoever joins it I shall join him, and whoever cuts it I shall cut him off. No one narrated this hadith from Shubah except Abu Muti; Muhammad ibn Yazid is alone in transmitting it."
"3344","Jafar narrated to us, he said: Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Abu Muti narrated to us, from Said ibn Abi Arubah, from Qatadah, from Abdillah ibn al-Harith, from Muadh ibn Jabal who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Beware of wrongdoing, for wrongdoing is darknesses on the Day of Resurrection, and beware of miserliness, for it destroyed those before you; it commanded them to sever ties so they severed their kinship, and commanded them to shed blood so they shed their blood. A man stood and said: O Messenger of Allah, which Islam is best? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best Islam is that the Muslims are safe from his tongue and his hand. No one narrated this hadith from Qatadah except Said; Abu Muti is alone in transmitting it; it is not narrated from Muadh except with this chain."
"3345","Jafar narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Hakim al-Samarqandi narrated to us, he said: Hashim ibn Makhlad narrated to us, from al-Salt ibn Dinar, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Umm Atiyyah who said: We were forbidden from following funeral processions, but it was not made binding on us; and we were commanded to go out on the day of Fitr and the day of Adha, and that the veiled women and menstruating women should go out, with the menstruating women kept away from the prayer place of the people, so that they may witness the congregation of the Muslims and their supplication. No one narrated this hadith from al-Salt except Hashim; Ali is alone in transmitting it."
"3346","Jafar narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Amr ibn Shaqiq narrated to us, and I copied it from the original of his book, he said: Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, from Shubah, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdillah ibn Masud, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed Zuhr as five (rakahs), so it was said: O Messenger of Allah, has the prayer been increased? He said: And what is that? They said: You prayed five. He then prostrated two prostrations. No one narrated this hadith from Shubah except Yazid ibn Zuray; al-Hasan ibn Amr ibn Shaqiq is alone in transmitting it."
"3347","Jafar ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Abu Jafar al-Nufayli narrated to us, he said: Miskin ibn Bukayr narrated to us, from al-Awzai, from Ismail ibn Ubaydillah, from Yazid ibn al-Asamm, from Maymunah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted ruqyah for every poisonous bite/sting. No one narrated this hadith from al-Awzai except Miskin."
"3348","Jafar narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Amr ibn Shaqiq (narrated), he said: Jafar ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Salih ibn Rustum al-Khazzaz, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Aishah who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, (about) {As for those in whose hearts is deviation}? He said: Those who argue about it; when you see them, they are the ones Allah referred to, so beware of them. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Amir except Jafar."
"3349","Jafar narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi al-Sari al-Asqalani narrated to us, he said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in a dream, and I said: O Messenger of Allah, seek forgiveness for me, but he remained silent toward me. So I said: O Messenger of Allah, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir, that you were never asked for anything and said: No. So he smiled at me and said: O Allah, forgive him."
"3350","Jafar narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Abdillah al-Harawi narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Ulayyah narrated to us, he said: Umar Kisra narrated to us, from Said ibn Abi Burdah, from his father, from Abu Musa who said: Indeed two safeguards came down from heaven; as for one of them, it has passed, and it is the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); and as for the other, it is seeking forgiveness. Umar Kisra did not narrate any hadith with a chain except this one, and no one narrated it except Ibn Ulayyah."
"3351","Jafar narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Sahl al-Hannat narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Hamid al-Himmani narrated to us, he said: al-Haytham ibn Ulayyah al-Basri narrated to us, from al-Azraq ibn Qays who said: I saw Ibn Umar leaning (on his hands) when standing up in prayer, so I said: What is this? He said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) doing it. No one narrated this hadith from al-Azraq except al-Haytham; al-Himmani is alone in transmitting it."
"3352","Jafar narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi Dawud al-Anbari narrated to us, he said: Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, from Abu Jafar al-Razi, from al-Rabi ibn Anas, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever abandons prayer deliberately has openly disbelieved. No one narrated it from Abu Jafar al-Razi except Hashim ibn al-Qasim; Muhammad ibn Abi Dawud is alone in transmitting it."
"3353","Jafar narrated to us, he said: al-Walid ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Musarrih al-Harrani narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Ata narrated to us, from Maslamah ibn Abdillah al-Juhani, from his uncle Abu Mashjaah ibn Ribi, from Abu al-Darda who said: Increase of lifespan was mentioned before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No soul is delayed when its term comes; rather, increase of lifespan is righteous offspring that Allah grants the servant, who supplicate for him after him, so their supplication reaches him in his grave; that is the increase of lifespan."
"3354","Jafar ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi narrated to us, he said: Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Lului narrated to us, he said: al-Qasim ibn al-Hakam al-Urani narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Ubayd narrated to us, from Ali ibn Rabiah, from Ali who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by people among whom was a man wearing perfume/cream (mutakhalliq), and he greeted them but turned away from the man. The man said to him: O Messenger of Allah, you greeted them but turned away from me? He said: Between your eyes there is redness. No one narrated it from Ali ibn Rabiah except Said ibn Ubayd, nor from Said except al-Qasim; Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Lului is alone in transmitting it."
"3355","Jafar narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Bahr al-Hujaymi narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Salim narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Abdillah ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Abdillah ibn al-Zubayr who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever recites the Quran openly or by looking (at the mushaf) is given a tree in Paradise; if a crow hatched (its chick) under one of its leaves, then that chick grew up and took flight, old age would overtake it before it crossed that leaf. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Jurayj except Said ibn Salim; Muhammad ibn Bahr is alone in transmitting it."
"3356","Jafar narrated to us, he said: Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahim ibn Zayd al-Ammi narrated to us, from his father, from al-Hasan, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever walks to fulfill the need of his Muslim brother, Allah writes for him seventy good deeds for every step he takes. No one narrated this hadith from al-Hasan except Zayd, nor from Zayd except his son; Muhammad ibn Bahr is alone in transmitting it."
"3357","Jafar narrated to us, he said: Safwan ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Numayr al-Yahsibi narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Said al-Khudri, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no prayer after Asr until the sun sets, and no prayer after Fajr until the sun rises."
"3358","Jafar narrated to us, he said: Qutaybah ibn Said narrated to us, he said: Rushdin ibn Sad narrated to us, from Uqayl and Qurrah and Yunus, from Ibn Shihab, from Urwah, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he wanted to sleep, would blow into his palms and seek refuge in them with the Muawwidhat, then wipe them over his face. No one narrated this hadith from Qurrah except Rushdin."
"3359","Jafar narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Hakim al-Samarqandi narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Muhammad al-Warraq narrated to us, he said: Hallam ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: Salim ibn Rabiah narrated to us, from Hudhayfah ibn al-Yaman who said: A Muslim man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have bought a slave; what shall I do with him? He said: He is your brother in Islam; do not burden him with work beyond what he can bear, feed him from your food, clothe him from your clothing, and if you dislike him then sell him. No one narrated this hadith from Hallam except Said, and it is not narrated from Hudhayfah except with this chain."
"3360","Jafar narrated to us, he said: Ali narrated to us, he said: Hashim ibn Makhlad narrated to us, from Shibl ibn Abbad al-Makki, from Sulayman al-Ahwal, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas who said: I used to pour the ablution water for the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was at my aunt Maymunah's house; when he came out he said: Who placed my ablution water for me? She said: Your nephew, O Messenger of Allah, Ibn Abbas. So he said: O Allah, give him understanding in the religion and teach him interpretation. No one narrated this hadith from Sulayman except Shibl."
"3361","Jafar ibn Muhammad ibn al-Layth al-Ziyadi narrated to us, he said: Ghassan ibn Malik al-Sulami narrated to us, he said: Sallam Abu al-Mundhir narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from al-Hasan, from Abdillah ibn Mughaffal, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade khadhf (throwing pebbles). No one narrated it from Yunus except Sallam."
"3362","Jafar ibn Muhammad ibn Majid narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Bakr al-Balisi narrated to us, he said: Urwah ibn Marwan al-Raqqi narrated to us, he said: Mutamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj ibn Artah, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, mighty and majestic, says: I take revenge from those I hate through those I hate, then I shall consign all to the Fire. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn al-Munkadir except al-Hajjaj, nor from al-Hajjaj except Mutamir; Urwah ibn Marwan is alone in transmitting it."
"3363","Jafar narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Hasan ibn Shaqiq narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn al-Ashath, the companion of Fudayl ibn Iyad, narrated to us, he said: Fudayl ibn Iyad narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Hassan, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn al-Husayn who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever devotes himself to Allah, Allah suffices him every burden and provides for him from where he does not expect; and whoever devotes himself to the world, Allah entrusts him to it."
"3364","Jafar narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn Marwan ibn Shuja al-Harrani narrated to us, at al-Raqqah, he said: al-Khadir ibn Muhammad ibn Shuja narrated to us, he said: Afif ibn Salim narrated to us, from Umarah ibn Zadham, from Thabit, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The truest speech is that at which one sneezes. No one narrated this hadith from Thabit except Umarah; al-Khadir is alone in transmitting it."
"3365","Jafar narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Ala ibn Hammad al-Narsi narrated to us, he said: Bishr ibn Mansur narrated to us, from Umar ibn Nabhan, from Abu Shaddad, from Jabir ibn Abdillah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three things: whoever brings them along with faith shall enter through whichever gate of Paradise he wishes, and shall be married to as many houris as he wishes: whoever repays a hidden debt, forgives his killer, and recites ten times after every obligatory prayer: {Say: He is Allah, the One}. Abu Bakr said: Or (even) one of them, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Or (even) one of them. This hadith is not narrated except with this chain; Bishr ibn Mansur is alone in transmitting it."
"3366","Jafar ibn Humayd ibn Abd al-Karim ibn Farrukh ibn Dayzaj ibn Bilal ibn Sad al-Ansari al-Dimashqi narrated to us, he said: My maternal grandfather Umar ibn Aban ibn Mufaddal al-Madani narrated to me, he said: Anas ibn Malik showed me the ablution: he took a small vessel, placed it on his left, poured onto his right hand and washed it three times, then moved the vessel to his right hand and performed ablution three times three times, wiped his head three times, took fresh water for his earholes and wiped them. I said to him: You already wiped your ear. He said: Boy, they are part of the head, not part of the face. Then he said: Boy, did you see and understand, or shall I repeat for you? I said: It suffices me, and I understood. He said: This is how I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) perform ablution. Umar ibn Aban narrated nothing from Anas except this hadith."
"3367","Jafar ibn Sulayman ibn Hajib al-Antaki narrated to us, he said: Abu Salih al-Farra narrated to us, he said: Abu Ishaq al-Fazari narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, from al-Hasan al-Basri, from Anas ibn Malik who said: Umm Salamah said: O Messenger of Allah, shall I go out with you to battle? He said: O Umm Salamah, jihad has not been prescribed for women. She said: Shall I treat the wounded, tend the camels and give water? He said: Yes, then. No one narrated it from al-Hasan except Abd al-Rahman, nor from Abd al-Rahman except Abu Ishaq; Abu Salih is alone in transmitting it."
"3368","Jafar ibn Muhammad ibn Bariq al-Baghdadi narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Muhammad al-Jarmi narrated to us, he said: Abu Tumaylah Yahya ibn Wadih narrated to us, he said: Abu Hamzah al-Sukkari narrated to us, from Jabir al-Jufi, from Amir al-Shabi, from Masruq, from Abdillah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever lies about me, let him take his seat in the Fire. No one narrated this hadith from al-Shabi except Jabir, nor from Jabir except Abu Hamzah."
"3369","And with the same chain, from Jabir, from Atiyyah al-Awfi, from Abu Said al-Khudri who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The poor among the Emigrants shall enter Paradise five hundred years before their rich."
"3370","And with the same chain, from Abu Said al-Khudri who said: I was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey while he rode his mount, and it shied. I said: O Messenger of Allah, what is wrong with your mount that it shied? He said: It heard the voice of a man being punished in his grave, so it shied because of that."
"3371","And with the same chain, from Jabir, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), in a battle he fought, ordered that the bells be cut off."
"3372","And with the same chain, from Jabir, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Sabit, from Umm Salamah who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was in a state of major impurity, he would not eat until he performed ablution as for prayer."
"3373","And with the same chain, Jabir narrated to us, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: On the Day of Resurrection there shall be brought wrongs of people against one another and their dues like mountains, and Allah shall keep settling them until nothing remains of them. No one narrated these hadiths from Jabir except Abu Hamzah, except the hadith of Abu Hazim, for Shayban al-Nahwi shared in narrating it."
"3374","Jafar ibn Ahmad al-Shami al-Kufi narrated to us, he said: Abu Kurayb narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn Makhlad narrated to us, he said: Nafi ibn Abi Nuaym narrated to us, he said: Nafi narrated to us, from Ibn Umar, from Zayd ibn Thabit, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted the owner of an ariyyah (a palm tree given for its fruit) to sell it by its estimated measure. No one narrated it from Nafi ibn Abi Nuaym except Khalid ibn Makhlad; Abu Kurayb is alone in transmitting it."
"3375","And with the same chain, Abu Kurayb narrated to us, he said: Ubayd ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Sabbah ibn Yahya al-Madani narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: When a man sneezes and says: Praise be to Allah, the angels say: Lord of the worlds; and when he says: Lord of the worlds, the angels say: May Allah have mercy on you. No one raised it from Ata ibn al-Saib except Sabbah ibn Yahya."
"3376","And with the same chain, Abu Kurayb narrated to us, he said: Uthman ibn Said narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Yaman narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn al-Zibriqan narrated to us, from Salih ibn Hayyan, from Ibn Buraydah, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Every newborn is pledged for his aqeeqah. No one narrated it from Salih, from Ibrahim, except Yahya, nor from Yahya except Uthman; Abu Kurayb is alone in transmitting it."
"3377","Jafar narrated to us, he said: Jafar ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Asadi narrated to us, he said: Isa ibn Rashid narrated to us, from Ibn Shubrumah, from Anas ibn Malik, that he was asked: Where did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray when he entered the House? He said: Between the two pillars."
"3378","Jafar ibn Bujayr al-Attar al-Baghdadi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Affan Abu Bakr narrated to us, he said: Hajjaj ibn Muhammad al-Awar narrated to us, from Shubah, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdillah ibn Masud who said: The Messenger of Allah used to pray at night until his feet swelled, so it was said: O Messenger of Allah, has Allah not forgiven you what preceded of your sin and what followed? He said: Shall I not be a grateful servant. No one narrated this hadith from Shubah except Hajjaj; Abd al-Rahman is alone in transmitting it."
"3379","Jafar al-Attar narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Ibrahim al-Tarjumaani narrated to us, he said: Abdillah ibn Muhammad al-Talhi narrated to us, from Khalid ibn al-Walid al-Makhzumi, from al-Zuhri, from Anas ibn Malik who said: While the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was traveling, a woman came with her son and said: O Messenger of Allah, does this one have Hajj? He said: Yes, and you have reward. She said: What is his reward when he stands at Arafah? He said: There is written for his parents, for every person who stood at the standing place, good deeds equal to the number of hairs on their heads. This hadith was not narrated from al-Zuhri except with this chain; al-Tarjumaani is alone in transmitting it."
"3380","Jafar ibn Bujayr narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Bakkar ibn al-Rayyan narrated to us, he said: Hafs ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Layth ibn Abi Sulaym, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever performs Hajj and visits my grave after my death is like one who visited me in my life. No one narrated this hadith from Layth except Hafs."
"3381","Jafar ibn Muhammad al-Naysaburi al-Araj narrated to us, he said: Idris ibn Yunus al-Harrani narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Umar ibn Saj narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Wahb narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Abi Ablah, from Khalid ibn Madan, from Abu al-Darda who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever serves as a link for his Muslim brother to a person of authority to convey good or bring joy, Allah shall raise him to the highest ranks of Paradise. No one narrated this hadith from Ibrahim except Sulayman, nor from Sulayman except Yahya; Idris ibn Yunus is alone in transmitting it."
"3382","Jafar ibn Muhammad ibn Sawwar al-Naysaburi narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Hafs narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj ibn al-Hajjaj, from Abbad ibn Mansur, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah accepts charities and accepts none of them except what is pure, and accepts it with His right hand, then nurtures it for its owner as one of you raises his foal and young camel, until a morsel becomes like Uhud. No one narrated this hadith from al-Hajjaj except Ibrahim."
"3383","Jafar ibn al-Sabbah al-Bazzaz al-Asbahani narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Hammad al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Yala al-Aslami narrated to us, from Ali ibn al-Hazawwar, from Abu Dawud, from Imran ibn Husayn, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was at a funeral and saw people walking without cloaks, so he said: Is this done in my presence? I intended to supplicate against you a supplication that you would walk in other than your forms. He said: After that no one was seen walking without a cloak. This hadith is not narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except with this chain."
"3384","Jafar ibn Muhammad ibn Malik al-Fazari al-Kufi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Marwan al-Qattan al-Kufi narrated to us, he said: Abdillah ibn al-Zubayr al-Asadi narrated to us, from Ziyad ibn al-Mundhir, from Habib ibn Yasar, from Zadham, from Ali who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah says: Might is My waist-wrapper and pride is My cloak; whoever disputes with Me over them I shall punish him. It is not narrated from Ali except with this chain, and Habib is not known to have narrated from Zadham any hadith other than this."
"3385","Jafar ibn Ahmad ibn Sinan al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Abdillah Abu Talhah al-Khuzai narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Ishaq al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Wuhayb narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from his father, from Abdillah ibn Amr who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever lies about me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire. No one narrated this hadith from Ata except Wuhayb, nor from Wuhayb except Ahmad; Abu Talhah is alone in transmitting it."
"3386","Jafar narrated to us, he said: al-Qasim ibn Isa al-Tai narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Madani narrated to us, from Muawiyah ibn Yahya, from al-Zuhri, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood only for the funeral that passed by him because it was the funeral of a Jew, so he stood for it. No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except Muawiyah, nor from Muawiyah except Muhammad, who is Wasiti; al-Qasim ibn Isa is alone in transmitting it."
"3387","Jafar ibn Ahmad ibn Sinan narrated to us, he said: al-Qasim ibn Isa al-Tai narrated to us, he said: Talhah ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted trousers for the sick person who finds no waist-wrapper, and leather socks for one who finds no sandals. No one narrated this hadith from Qatadah except Talhah."
"3388","Jafar narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn Waki ibn al-Jarrah narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud al-Hafari narrated to us, he said: Muti al-Ghazzal narrated to us, from al-Shabi, from al-Bara ibn Azib who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: My Basin is between Aylah and Sanaa; it has two spouts, one of gold and the other of silver; its vessels are as many as the stars of the sky, whiter than milk, sweeter than honey, and its scent more pleasant than musk; whoever drinks from it shall never thirst. No one narrated this hadith from Muti except Abu Dawud; Sufyan is alone in transmitting it."
"3389","Jafar narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Sudran narrated to us, he said: Anbasah ibn Salim, the keeper of the tablets, narrated to us, he said: Ubaydillah ibn Abi Bakr narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, that he saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wearing a black turban. No one narrated this hadith from Ubaydillah except Anbasah; Muhammad ibn Sudran is alone in transmitting it."
"3390","Jafar narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Hamid ibn Bayan narrated to us, he said: Ishaq al-Azraq narrated to us, from Sharik, from Mughirah, from al-Shabi, from Jabir ibn Abdillah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None of you shall come to his family at night unexpectedly. No one narrated this hadith from Mughirah except Sharik; Ishaq is alone in transmitting it."
"3391","Jafar narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Yazid ibn al-Rawwas narrated to us, he said: Salamah ibn Alqamah narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir who said: We arrived with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while we were loudly calling out the Hajj, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered us to make it Umrah and to exit ihram, so we exited ihram. No one narrated this hadith from Dawud except Salamah; Muhammad is alone in transmitting it."
"3392","Jafar narrated to us, he said: al-Qasim ibn Dinar narrated to us, he said: Ubaydillah ibn Musa narrated to us, from Abu Israil al-Mulai, from Aban ibn Taghlib, from Jafar ibn Iyas, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to us while we were discussing truffles, so he said: Truffles are from manna, and their water is a cure for the eye. No one narrated this hadith from Aban except Abu Israil; Ubaydillah is alone in transmitting it."
"3393","Jafar ibn al-Fadl ibn al-Yaman al-Makhzumi al-Muaddib narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Shaybah al-Hizami narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Yaqub al-Zamai narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, that Abu Hazim informed him that Nafi, the freed slave of Ibn Umar, informed him that he heard Ibn Umar saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no traitor but he shall have a banner on the Day of Resurrection by which he is known. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Hazim except Abd al-Rahman, nor from Abd al-Rahman except Musa, nor from Musa except Ibn Fudayk; Abd al-Rahman is alone in transmitting it."
"3394","Jafar ibn Muhammad al-Kharaki al-Basri narrated to us, he said: Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn al-Jad narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The damage caused by a beast is without liability, and he ruled that a fifth is due on buried treasure. No one narrated this hadith from Qatadah except Hammad and Abu Maryam Abd al-Ghaffar ibn al-Qasim."
"3395","Jafar ibn Madan al-Ahwazi narrated to us, he said: Zayd ibn al-Harish narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi narrated to us, from Abd al-Wahhab ibn Mujahid, from his father, from Muawiyah ibn Abi Sufyan who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not rush toward something thinking that if you rush to it you will attain it, and do not hold back from something thinking that if you hold back from it it will be averted from you, if Allah has decreed it for you. This hadith is narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) only by Muawiyah, and is not narrated from Muawiyah except with this chain; Abd al-Wahhab is alone in transmitting it."
"3396","Jafar narrated to us, he said: Zayd narrated to us, he said: Uthman ibn al-Haytham narrated to us, he said: Awf narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Abdillah ibn Mughaffal who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The worst thieves among people are those who steal their prayer. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, how does he steal his prayer? He said: He does not complete its bowing nor its prostration; and the most miserly among people is one who is miserly with greeting. No one narrated this hadith from Abdillah except al-Hasan, nor from al-Hasan except Awf, nor from Awf except Uthman; Zayd is alone in transmitting it."
"3397","Jafar ibn Ahmad ibn Yahmazd al-Tustari narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Ashath Ahmad ibn al-Miqdam al-Ijli narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr al-Hanafi narrated to us: Ghalib ibn Ubaydillah al-Jazari said: I heard Said ibn al-Musayyib narrate from Abu Hurayrah who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of Khaybar, and he said of a man with him: This one is among the people of the Fire. When fighting came, he fought fiercely until wounds weighed him down. They came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, the one you claimed is among the people of the Fire fought fiercely. He said: Yet he is upon that among the people of the Fire. When the wounds pained him, he took out an arrow from his quiver and killed himself with it. They came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, Allah has confirmed your word; the one you told us is among the people of the Fire took an arrow from his quiver and killed himself with it. So he ordered Bilal to announce among the people: None shall enter Paradise except a believer, and Allah supports this religion with the wicked man. Ghalib narrated nothing from Said, from Abu Hurayrah, except this; Abu Bakr is alone in transmitting it."
"3398","Jubayr ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Jafar ibn al-Fadl al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Zakariyya ibn Farrukh al-Tammar narrated to us, from Waki ibn al-Jarrah, from al-Amash, from Shaqiq ibn Salamah, from Abdillah ibn Masud who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Shall I not teach you the words that Musa (peace be upon him) spoke when he crossed the sea with the Children of Israel? We said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Say: O Allah, to You is praise, to You is complaint, You are the One whose help is sought, and there is no power nor strength except through Allah the Almighty. He said: I have not abandoned them since I heard them from Shaqiq; and Shaqiq said: I have not abandoned them since I heard them from Abdillah; and Abdillah said: I have not abandoned them since I heard them from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Al-Amash said: A visitor came to me in a dream and said: O Sulayman, add to these words: And we seek Your help against corruption within us, and we ask You for the rectitude of all our affairs. No one narrated this hadith from al-Amash except Waki, nor from Waki except Zakariyya; Jafar is alone in transmitting it, and it is not narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except with this chain."
"3399","Jubayr narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Mahan ibn Abi Hanifah narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from Abbad ibn Kathir, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Love your beloved moderately, for he may become hated to you someday; and hate the one you hate moderately, for he may become beloved to you someday. No one narrated this hadith from Abu al-Zinad except Abbad; Muhammad ibn Mahan is alone in transmitting it."
"3400","Jubayr ibn Harun al-Asbahani narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Muhammad al-Tanafisi narrated to us, he said: Waki narrated to us, from al-Hasan ibn Salih, from Alqamah ibn Marthad, from Sulayman ibn Buraydah, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he sent an expedition, would say: Fight in the name of Allah, in the cause of Allah; fight those who disbelieve in Allah; do not steal from the spoils, do not betray, and do not act cowardly."
"3401","Jabrun ibn Isa al-Maghribi al-Misri narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sulayman al-Jafari al-Maghribi narrated to us, he said: Abbad ibn Abd al-Samad Abu Mamar narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik who said: I heard Abu Bakr al-Siddiq saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever bathes on Friday, his sins and wrongs are forgiven; when he walks to Friday prayer, for every step there is the reward of twenty years deeds; and when he finishes the Friday prayer he is granted the reward of two hundred years deeds. It is not narrated from Abu Bakr except with this chain; Yahya ibn Sulayman is alone in transmitting it."
"3402","And with the same chain, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: When you seek a need and wish it to succeed, say: There is no god but Allah alone, without partner, the Most High, the Almighty; there is no god but Allah alone, without partner, the Forbearing, the Generous; in the name of Allah besides whom there is no god, the Living, the Forbearing; glory be to Allah, Lord of the Mighty Throne; and praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds. {As though on the day they see what they are promised they had remained only an hour of the day; a proclamation; shall any be destroyed except the defiantly disobedient people} {As though on the day they see it they had remained only an evening or a morning}. O Allah, I ask You for what necessitates Your mercy, for firm resolves of Your forgiveness, for gain from every good, and safety from every sin; O Allah, leave no sin of mine unforgiven, no worry unrelieved, no debt unpaid, and no need among the needs of this world and the Hereafter unfulfilled, by Your mercy, O Most Merciful of the merciful. This hadith is not narrated from Anas except with this chain; Yahya ibn Sulayman is alone in transmitting it."
"3403","Al-Hasan ibn Abd al-Ala al-Bawsi al-Sanani narrated to us: Abd al-Razzaq informed us: al-Thawri informed us, from Abu Ishaq al-Shaybani, from al-Hasan ibn Sad, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdillah, from his father who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey, and we passed a colony of ants that had been burned, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is not fitting for a human to punish with the punishment of Allah. No one narrated it from Sufyan except Abd al-Razzaq."
"3404","Al-Hasan ibn Abd al-Ala al-Bawsi narrated to us: Abd al-Razzaq informed us: Mamar informed us, from Qatadah, from al-Nadr ibn Anas, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah promised me to admit four hundred thousand of my nation into Paradise. Abu Bakr said to him: Increase for us, O Messenger of Allah. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: And like this, and he joined his palms. Umar said: Enough, O Abu Bakr. Abu Bakr said: Leave me, O Umar; what harm is it to you if He admits us all into Paradise. Umar said: If Allah wills, He admits His creation into Paradise with a single handful. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Umar has spoken the truth. Thus Mamar narrated it, from Qatadah, from al-Nadr ibn Anas, from Anas; and Muadh ibn Hisham narrated it, from his father, from Qatadah, from Abu Bakr ibn Anas, from Abu Bakr ibn Umayr, from his father."
"3405","Al-Hasan ibn Jarir al-Suri narrated to us: Ismail ibn Abi Uways narrated to us: My father narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Said, from Amrah, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by some Ansari women at their wedding singing; the narrator said - so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None knows what is in tomorrow except Allah. No one narrated it from Yahya ibn Said except Abu Uways."
"3406","Al-Hasan ibn Jarir narrated to us: Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Dimashqi narrated to us: Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Abdillah ibn al-Zubayr and Abdillah ibn Jafar, that they pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when they were seven years old; when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw them he smiled and extended his hand and pledged allegiance to them. No one narrated it from Hisham ibn Urwah except Ismail ibn Ayyash, nor from Ismail except Ibn Bint Shurahbil; and it is not narrated from Abdillah ibn al-Zubayr and Abdillah ibn Jafar except through this channel, nor from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except with this chain."
"3407","Al-Hasan ibn Jarir al-Suri narrated to us: Abu al-Jumahir narrated to us: Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Ubaydillah, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The pen is lifted from three: the sleeper until he wakes, the mentally unsound until he recovers, and the child until he understands, or reaches puberty. It is not narrated from Ibn Abbas except through this channel, and none narrated it except Abu al-Jumahir."
"3408","Al-Hasan ibn Jarir narrated to us: Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us: Abd al-Rahman ibn Bishr narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq: Muhammad ibn Talhah ibn Yazid ibn Rukanah narrated to me, from Ibrahim ibn Sad ibn Abi Waqqas, from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) alighted at al-Hijr, and the people drew water from its well, then he departed from it; when he set out he ordered the people not to drink from its water nor perform ablution with it, and whatever dough had been kneaded with its water was to be fed to animals; so the people did so. It is not narrated from Sad except with this chain; Ibn Bint Shurahbil is alone in transmitting it."
"3409","Al-Hasan ibn Jarir al-Suri narrated to us: Abu al-Jumahir narrated to us: Khulayd ibn Dalaj narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever separates from the Muslims by a handspan has cast off the bond of Islam from his neck; whoever dies with no imam over him, his death is a death of ignorance; and whoever dies under a blind banner supporting tribalism, his killing is (a death of) ignorance. No one narrated it from Qatadah except Khulayd ibn Dalaj, and it is not narrated from Ibn Abbas except through this channel."
"3410","Al-Hasan ibn Ghulayb al-Misri narrated to us: Mahdi ibn Jafar al-Ramli narrated to us: Abd al-Majid ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Rawwad narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Abdillah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Truffles are from manna, their water is a cure for the eye, and ajwah dates are from Paradise and are a cure for poison. He said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prescribed for sciatica the fatty tail of a ram. We heard it only from Ibn Ghulayb, and it is not narrated from Ibn Abbas except through this channel."
"3411","Al-Hasan ibn Ghulayb narrated to us: Yahya ibn Sulayman al-Jufi narrated to us: Abu Khalid al-Ahmar narrated to us: Uthman ibn al-Aswad narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever comes to Friday prayer, let him bathe. No one narrated it except Yahya al-Jufi."
"3412","Al-Hasan ibn Ghulayb narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Ufayr narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Razin, from Muhammad ibn Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Ayyub ibn Qatan, from Ubadah ibn Nusayy, from Ubayy ibn Umarah al-Ansari, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed in his house, so I said: O Messenger of Allah, shall I wipe over the leather socks? He said: Yes. I said: A day? He said: And two days. I said: And three, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Yes, and whatever seems fit to you. A group narrated it from Yahya ibn Ayyub but did not mention Ubadah ibn Nusayy; none mentioned him except Said ibn Ufayr."
"3413","Al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn Zawlaq al-Misri narrated to us: Yahya ibn Sulayman al-Jufi narrated to us: Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Abu Husayn, from Sad ibn Ubaydah, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Night prayer is two by two; when you fear dawn, pray one rakah as witr. No one narrated it except Yahya ibn Sulayman."
"3414","Al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn Zawlaq narrated to us: Amr ibn al-Rabi ibn Tariq narrated to us: al-Sari ibn Yahya narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When he sits between her four parts and the circumcision touches the circumcision, washing becomes obligatory. No one narrated this hadith from al-Sari ibn Yahya except Amr ibn al-Rabi ibn Tariq."
"3415","Al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn Zawlaq al-Misri narrated to us: Amr ibn al-Rabi ibn Tariq narrated to us: Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ajlan, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not prevent the female servants of Allah from the mosques of Allah, and let them go out unattractive (without perfume). No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Ajlan except Yahya ibn Ayyub; Amr ibn al-Rabi ibn Tariq is alone in transmitting it."
"3416","Al-Hasan ibn al-Mutawakkil al-Baghdadi narrated to us: Sulayman ibn Muhammad al-Mubaraki narrated to us: Abu Shihab narrated to us, from Shubah, from al-Hakam, from Abu al-Muwarri, from Ali who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Who will go to Madinah and leave no grave nor idol but break it, nor image but deface it? A man stood and said: I will, O Messenger of Allah; then he feared the people of Madinah and sat down. Ali said: So I went, then came and said: O Messenger of Allah, I left no grave in Madinah but leveled it, no idol but broke it, and no image but defaced it. He said: O Ali, do not be divisive, nor arrogant, nor a trader - except a trader in good. No one narrated it from Shubah except Abu Shihab."
"3417","Al-Hasan ibn al-Mutawakkil narrated to us: Said ibn Dawud al-Zubayri narrated to us: Malik ibn Anas narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, from Ubaydillah ibn Abdillah ibn Utbah, from Ibn Abbas, from Maymunah, that she asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about a mouse that fell into ghee, and he said: Take it and what is around it and discard it. None said: from Maymunah, except al-Zubayri."
"3418","Al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Mamari narrated to us: Dawud ibn Bilal al-Sadi narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Congregational prayer exceeds the prayer of the individual by twenty-five prayers. No one narrated it from Amr ibn Dinar except Hammad, nor from Hammad except Dawud ibn Bilal."
"3419","Al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Mamari narrated to us: Abd al-Ghaffar ibn Abdillah al-Mawsili narrated to us: Abu Shihab narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Abu Ishaq, from Asim ibn Damrah who said: Ali ibn Abi Talib was asked: Tell us about the daytime voluntary prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: You cannot bear it. They said: Tell us it yourself. He said: When the sun was here, at the time of Asr, he prayed two rakahs; then he waited until when the sun was here, at the time of Zuhr, he prayed four; then he prayed two rakahs after Zuhr. No one narrated it from Khalid except Abu Shihab, nor from Abu Shihab except Abd al-Ghaffar."
"3420","Al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Mamari narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Jabalah narrated to us: Umayyah ibn Khalid narrated to us: Qurrah ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Nafi who said: When Ibn Umar wanted to enter ihram he would come to Dhu al-Hulayfah and spend the night there; in the morning he mounted his camel, and when it stood upright he would declare talbiyah; and he claimed that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to do so. No one narrated it from Qurrah except Umayyah, nor narrated it except Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Jabalah; and Qurrah narrated nothing from Nafi with a chain except this."
"3421","Al-Hasan ibn al-Abbas al-Razi narrated to us: Sahl ibn Uthman narrated to us: Ubayd ibn Hassab al-Saydalani narrated to us, from al-Salt ibn Bahram, from Abd Khayr, from Ali who said: The best of this nation after its Prophet are Abu Bakr and Umar. No one narrated it from al-Salt ibn Bahram except Ubayd ibn Hassab, nor from Ubayd except Sahl ibn Uthman."
"3422","Al-Hasan ibn al-Abbas al-Razi narrated to us: Abd al-Mumin ibn Ali narrated to us: Abd al-Salam ibn Harb narrated to us, from Abu Khalid al-Dalani, from Asim, from Zirr, from Abdillah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) taught me Surah Ha-Mim; I went to the mosque and found a man from the people of the mosque. I said to him: Do you recite this surah? He said: Yes, and he recited another (reading) that I do not recite. I said: Who taught you? He said: The Messenger of Allah. I said: The Messenger of Allah taught me. Then I met another, and I said: Do you recite this surah? He said: Yes. I said: Recite; and he recited the reading of my companion. I said: Who taught you? He said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). I said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) taught me. So I went to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was sitting and said: This one differed with me in recitation. His face changed and he became angry, and he gestured to Ali, who was with him; the Messenger of Allah spoke, and Ali said: The Messenger of Allah commands that each of you recite what he learned; those before you were destroyed only by disagreement. No one narrated it from Abu Khalid al-Dalani except Abd al-Salam ibn Harb; al-Amash narrated it from Asim, and others than al-Amash narrated it."
"3423","Al-Hasan ibn al-Abbas narrated to us: Abdillah ibn Imran narrated to us: Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated to us: Shubah ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to us, from Asim, from Zirr, from Abdillah who said: We said: O Messenger of Allah, how will you recognize those of your nation whom you have not seen on the Day of Resurrection? He said: Radiant with white marks on forehead and limbs from the traces of purification. No one narrated it from Shubah except Abu Dawud, nor from Abu Dawud except Abdillah ibn Imran."
"3424","Al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn Yasir al-Baghdadi narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Umar al-Wukayi narrated to us: Waki narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Abd Khayr, from Ali who said: The best of this nation after its Prophet are Abu Bakr, then Umar, then a man - meaning himself. No one narrated it from al-Amash except Waki, nor from Waki except Ahmad ibn Umar."
"3425","Al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Hisham al-Shatawi narrated to us: Ali ibn al-Madini narrated to us: Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us: al-Hasan ibn Salih narrated to us, from his brother Ali ibn Salih, from Abu Ishaq, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abdillah ibn Salamah, from Ali - (ha). Ali said: And Ibn Adam narrated to us: Israil narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Ali who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: Shall I not teach you words which, if you say them, you shall be forgiven, though you are already forgiven? There is no god but Allah, the Forbearing, the Generous; there is no god but Allah, the Most High, the Almighty; glory be to Allah, Lord of the Mighty Throne; praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds. No one narrated it from al-Hasan ibn Salih except Yahya, nor from him except Ali ibn al-Madini."
"3426","Al-Hasan ibn Ulwayh al-Qattan narrated to us: Ismail ibn Isa al-Attar narrated to us: Ismail ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, from Sufyan and Misar, from Ziyad ibn Ilaqah, from Yazid ibn al-Harith, from Abu Musa who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The passing of my nation is by piercing (in battle) and plague. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, this piercing we know; what is plague? He said: Stabs of your enemies from the jinn, and in each there is martyrdom. No one narrated it from Misar except Ismail ibn Zakariyya, nor from him except Ismail ibn Isa."
"3427","Al-Hasan ibn Ulwayh al-Qattan narrated to us: Ismail ibn Isa al-Attar narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Husayn narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Ayyash, from Jafar ibn al-Harith, from Abd al-Malik ibn Abd al-Aziz, from al-Qasim ibn Abi Bazzah, from Said ibn Jubayr who said: I said to Ibn Abbas: Does one who kills a believer deliberately have repentance? He said: No. I said: Then where is His saying: {And those who do not invoke another god with Allah, nor kill the soul Allah has forbidden except by right, nor commit adultery; whoever does that shall meet punishment; multiplied for him shall be the punishment on the Day of Resurrection, and he shall abide therein disgraced; except whoever repents, believes and does righteous work - for those, Allah shall replace their evils with good}? He said: This is a Makkan verse abrogated by a Madinan verse: {And whoever kills a believer deliberately, his recompense is Hell, abiding therein; Allah is angry with him, curses him, and has prepared for him a great punishment}. No one narrated this hadith from Jafar ibn al-Harith except Ismail ibn Ayyash; Muhammad ibn Husayn is alone in transmitting it."
"3428","Al-Hasan ibn Ulwayh al-Qattan narrated to us: Ubayd ibn Jannad al-Halabi narrated to us: Ubaydillah ibn Umar narrated to us, from Abd al-Karim, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had cupping done, and the cupper complained to him until he wept, so he sent to his masters to lighten his tax. No one narrated it from Abd al-Karim except Abdillah, nor from Ubaydillah except Ubayd ibn Jannad."
"3429","Al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Fasawi narrated to us: al-Fayd ibn Wathiq al-Thaqafi narrated to us: Ishaq ibn Ibrahim, the seller of clarified butter, narrated to us: al-Amash narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Wahb, from Umar ibn al-Khattab who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best generation is the generation I am in, then the second, then the third, then the fourth; Allah pays them no regard. It is not narrated from al-Amash except through this channel."
"3430","Al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn Dallawayh al-Baghdadi narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Thabit al-Jahdari narrated to us: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Muhammad ibn Ali and Mujammi, from Abu Umamah ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf, from Muawiyah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he heard the caller saying: I bear witness there is no god but Allah, would say: And I, and I; and when he said: And I bear witness Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, he would say: And I, and I. No one narrated this hadith from Sufyan, from Amr, except Ahmad ibn Thabit al-Jahdari."
"3431","Al-Hasan ibn Sulayman al-Darimi Abu Mashar narrated to us: Abu al-Rabi al-Zahrani narrated to us: Hafs ibn Abi Dawud narrated to us, from al-Haytham ibn Habib al-Sayrafi, from Atiyyah, from Abu Said who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The people of the highest ranks shall be seen by those below them as you see the brilliant star on the horizon of the sky; and Abu Bakr and Umar are among them, and blessed. No one narrated this hadith from al-Haytham ibn Habib al-Sayrafi except Hafs ibn Abi Dawud; Abu al-Rabi al-Zahrani is alone in transmitting it."
"3432","Al-Hasan ibn Ulayl al-Anazi narrated to us: Ali ibn al-Hasan ibn Salim al-Azdi narrated to us: al-Ashjai narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Abu Qilabah, from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked: Which part of the night is most likely to have supplication answered? He said: The last depth of the night. No one narrated this hadith from Sufyan except al-Ashjai."
"3433","Al-Hasan ibn Hubash al-Himmani narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Hamid al-Attar narrated to us: Sayf ibn Umayrah narrated to us, from Aban ibn Taghlib, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Bara who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded me: When you take your bed, say: O Allah, I submit myself to You, turn my face to You, entrust my affair to You, and lean my back on You, in fear and hope of You; there is no escape nor refuge from You except to You; I believe in Your Book which You sent down, and Your Prophet whom You sent; if you die that night you die upon the natural disposition, and if you wake you attain good. No one narrated it from Aban except Sayf ibn Umayrah."
"3434","Al-Hasan ibn Hubash al-Himmani narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Hamid al-Attar narrated to us: Sayf ibn Umayrah narrated to us, from Aban ibn Taghlib, from Simak ibn Harb, from Shahr ibn Hawshab who said: We were with Umm Salamah asking her about the letters of the Quran, when a man said: O Mother of the Believers, I speak to myself things which, if I uttered them, would nullify my reward, and if I were exposed for them my neck would be struck. She said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) being asked about the like of what you asked, and he said: None meets such speech except a believer. No one narrated it from Aban except Sayf."
"3435","And with the same chain, from Aban ibn Taghlib: Abu Ishaq narrated to me, from al-Harith, from Ali, that he was asked about the station of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of Badr. He said: The bravest of us on the day of Badr was the one who aligned himself with the knee of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). No one narrated it from Aban except Sayf."
"3436","Al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Nasr al-Nahhas Abu Said narrated to us: Qurrah ibn al-Ala ibn Murrah al-Sadi narrated to us: Abu Yunus al-Khassaf narrated to us: Dawud ibn Abi Hind narrated to us, that he performed Hajj and came to Said ibn Jubayr; Said ibn Jubayr said: Abu Hurayrah narrated to me that he saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) drinking from this well standing, gesturing with his hand toward Zamzam. No one narrated this hadith from Dawud ibn Abi Hind except Abu Yunus al-Khassaf, nor from Abu Yunus except Qurrah ibn al-Ala; al-Hasan ibn Muhammad al-Nahhas is alone in transmitting it."
"3437","Al-Hasan ibn Ibrahim ibn Muttarih al-Khawlani al-Misri narrated to us: Yazid ibn Said al-Sabbahi narrated to us: Malik ibn Anas narrated to us, from Said ibn Abi Said al-Maqburi, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said on one of the Fridays: Assembly of Muslims, this is a day Allah has made a festival for you, so bathe, and use the tooth-stick. No one narrated it from Malik except Yazid ibn Said and Man ibn Isa."
"3438","Al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn Shahriyar narrated to us: Zurayq ibn al-Ward al-Raqqi narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn Harasah narrated to us: Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If man knew what comes to him after death, he would not eat a morsel nor drink a drink except weeping and beating his chest. No one narrated it from Sufyan except Ibrahim ibn Harasah."
"3439","Al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Nahhas al-Kufi narrated to us: al-Haytham ibn Jannad al-Juhani narrated to us: Amr ibn Muhammad al-Anqari narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us, from Jabir, from Abu Nadr, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave me the kunyah. No one narrated it from Sufyan except al-Anqari."
"3440","Al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Nahhas narrated to us: Abbad ibn Yaqub al-Asadi narrated to us: Abu Ayyub al-Anmati, freed slave of Ibn Kuhayl, narrated to us, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Jariyah ibn Yazid ibn Jariyah al-Ansari, from his father who said: I was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and when he did not remember a man's name he would say: O Abdallah. It is not narrated from the Messenger of Allah except through this channel."
"3441","Al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn Salamah al-Dahhan narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn Yusuf al-Sayrafi narrated to us: Yahya ibn Yaman narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Ubaydillah ibn Umar, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah combined Hajj and Umrah and performed one circumambulation for both. No one narrated it from Sufyan except Yahya ibn Yaman."
"3442","Al-Hasan ibn Ahmad ibn Fahd al-Narsi narrated to us: Abdillah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated to us: Ubaydah ibn al-Aswad narrated to us, from Said ibn Abi Arubah, from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cut (the hand) for a shield worth five dirhams. None raised it from Said except Ubaydah."
"3443","Al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Musab al-Ushnani al-Kufi narrated to us: Abbad ibn Yaqub narrated to us: Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Masudi narrated to us, from Kathir al-Nawwa, from Atiyyah, from Abu Said who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I leave among you the two weighty things, one greater than the other: the Book of Allah, a rope extended from heaven to earth, and my kin, my household; and they shall not separate until they come to me at the Basin. No one narrated it from Kathir al-Nawwa except Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Masudi."
"3444","Al-Hasan ibn Sahl al-Mujawwiz al-Basri narrated to us: Abu Asim narrated to us, from Mansur ibn Dinar, from Hammad, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas who said: Wine itself was forbidden, and intoxication from every drink."
"3445","Al-Hasan ibn Sahl narrated to us: Abu Asim narrated to us, from Uthman ibn Sad, from Anas who said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) alighted at a place, he would not depart until he prayed two rakahs, or a prayer with which he bade farewell to the place."
"3446","Al-Hasan ibn Sahl narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to us: Abu Raja narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Zayd ibn Wahb, that Umar asked about the Magians, so Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf said: I bear witness that the Messenger of Allah said: The Magians are a group of the People of the Book, so treat them as you treat the People of the Book. No one narrated it from al-Amash except Abu Raja, who is Rawh ibn al-Musayyib."
"3447","Al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn al-Ashath al-Bazzaz al-Misri narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Sallam al-Ifriqi narrated to us: My father narrated to us: Uthman ibn Miqsam al-Barri narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Said, from Sulayman ibn Yasar who said: Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz wrote that Aishah informed him that prayer in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was two rakahs, then it was increased for the resident prayer, while the traveler's prayer was kept as it is. It is not narrated from Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz except through this channel; Hammad ibn Zayd and others narrated it from Yahya ibn Said, from Urwah."
"3448","Al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn al-Hajjaj Himsah narrated to us: Abdillah ibn Muawiyah al-Jumahi narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us: Ayyub narrated to us, from Yazid al-Rishk, from Muadhah, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would wake in major impurity not from a wet dream, then wash and fast. Ayyub narrated nothing from Yazid except this, and heard it only from this shaykh."
"3449","Al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn al-Hajjaj Himsah narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ubayd ibn Hassab narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Isa al-Sadi narrated to us, from Thawr ibn Yazid, from al-Mutim ibn al-Miqdam who said: I saw Muhammad ibn Maslamah standing on a roof looking at the sister of al-Dahhak ibn Qays, so I said: Do you do this while you are a companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When Allah casts into a man's heart the proposal of a woman, there is no harm in looking at her appearance. No one narrated it from Thawr ibn Yazid except Muhammad ibn Isa al-Sadi, nor from al-Mutim except Thawr ibn Yazid; and in our view he is not the Syrian."
"3450","Al-Hasan ibn Harun ibn Sulayman al-Asbahani narrated to us: Ali ibn al-Madini narrated to us: Ziyad ibn al-Rabi narrated to us: Asim ibn Bahdalah narrated to us, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, from Safwan ibn Assal who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever goes out from his house seeking knowledge, the angels spread their wings for him in pleasure at what he does. And I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Allah has opened a door toward the west, seventy years wide, and shall not close it until the sun rises from it. I said: Tell me more, may Allah have mercy on you. He said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey when a loud-voiced Bedouin came and said: O Muhammad, stop, I ask you; O Muhammad, stop, I ask you. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) answered him in like voice: Here, here. He said: O Messenger of Allah, may my father and mother be ransom for you, a man loves people and recognizes their merit but does not do deeds like theirs? He said: On the Day of Resurrection he is with those he loved. I said: Tell me about wiping over the leather socks. He said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a campaign, and he ordered a caller who called: Do not remove the socks for three (days) except from major impurity, but (you may keep them) for stool and urine. No one narrated it from Ziyad ibn al-Rabi except Ali ibn al-Madini, Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna, and al-Hasan ibn Khalid al-Harrani."
"3451","Al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Sarakhsi narrated to us: Hamdan ibn Dhi al-Nun al-Lakhmi narrated to us: Shaddad ibn Hakim narrated to us: Zufar ibn al-Hudhayl narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Said, from al-Zuhri, from Abdillah and al-Hasan, sons of Muhammad ibn al-Hanafiyyah, from their father, from Ali who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade temporary marriage with women on the day of Khaybar."
"3452","Al-Hasan ibn Mihran al-Saffar al-Mawsili narrated to us: Ghassan ibn al-Rabi narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Hisham and Ayyub, from Habib ibn al-Shahid, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Amr ibn Wahb, from al-Mughirah ibn Shubah who said: I poured for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): he washed his hands, rinsed his mouth and nose, washed his face and forearms, wiped his forelock and over the turban and the leather socks. No one narrated it from Habib ibn al-Shahid except Hammad ibn Zayd."
"3453","Al-Hasan ibn Ahmad ibn Fil al-Antaki narrated to us: Ishaq ibn Musa al-Ansari narrated to us: Man narrated to us, from Malik, from Abdillah ibn Idris al-Awdi, from Shubah, from Sad ibn Ibrahim, from his father who said: Umar ibn al-Khattab sent for Ibn Masud, Abu Masud al-Ansari and Abu al-Darda and said: What is this hadith you narrate so much from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? So he detained them in Madinah until he was martyred. None narrated it except Ishaq ibn Musa al-Ansari."
"3454","Al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn Nasr al-Tusi narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Mawsili narrated to us: Amr ibn Abi Salamah al-Tinnisi narrated to us: Sadaqah ibn Abdillah narrated to us, from al-Asbagh, meaning Ibn Zayd al-Warraq, from Bahz ibn Hakim, from his father, from his grandfather, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Secret charity extinguishes the anger of the Lord, blessed and exalted. No one narrated this hadith from Bahz ibn Hakim except al-Asbagh ibn Zayd al-Warraq, nor from al-Asbagh except Sadaqah; Amr ibn Abi Salamah is alone in transmitting it."
"3455","Al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Sarraj the judge narrated to us: al-Fadl ibn Yaqub al-Jazari narrated to us: Makhlad ibn Yazid narrated to us: Rawh ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, from Asim al-Ahwal, from Abdillah ibn Sarjis who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a man praying the two rakahs of Fajr while they prayed the dawn prayer, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Which of the two did you make your prayer? No one narrated this hadith from Rawh ibn al-Qasim except Makhlad ibn Yazid; al-Fadl ibn Yaqub is alone in transmitting it; and this Makhlad ibn Yazid is Basran, not the Harranian."
"3456","Al-Hasan ibn al-Muthanna ibn Muadh al-Anbari narrated to us: Abu Hudhayfah narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked: What is the due of camels? He said: To slaughter its fat one, lend its stallion, and milk it on its watering day. No one narrated this hadith from Sufyan except Abu Hudhayfah and al-Ashjai."
"3457","Al-Hasan ibn Muadh al-Anbari narrated to us: Arim Abu al-Numan narrated to us: al-Saq ibn Hazn narrated to us: Qatadah narrated to us, from Zahdam al-Jarmi who said: Ibn Abbas addressed us and said: Were it not that people sought (revenge for) the blood of Uthman, they would have been stoned from heaven."
"3458","Al-Hasan ibn Ahmad ibn Bakkar al-Allaf al-Basri narrated to us: Abu al-Rabi al-Zahrani narrated to us: Jarir ibn Abd al-Hamid narrated to us, from Raqabah ibn Masqalah who said: I saw the Lord of Might in a dream, and He said: By My might and majesty, I shall honor his resting place - meaning Sulayman al-Taymi."
"3459","Al-Hasan ibn Ahmad ibn Bakkar al-Allaf narrated to us: I heard Abu al-Rabi al-Zahrani saying: I heard Abdillah ibn al-Mubarak saying:"
"3460","Al-Hasan ibn Ahmad ibn Habib al-Kirmani al-Tarsusi narrated to us: Abu al-Rabi al-Zahrani narrated to us: Ammar ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Sufyan al-Thawri, from Dawud Abu al-Jahhaf, from Atiyyah al-Awfi, from Abu Said al-Khudri, regarding His saying: {Allah only wishes to remove impurity from you, O people of the House}: He said: It was revealed concerning five: the Messenger of Allah, Ali, Fatimah, al-Hasan and al-Husayn. No one narrated this hadith from Sufyan al-Thawri except Ammar ibn Muhammad, nor from Ammar ibn Muhammad except Abu al-Rabi al-Zahrani and Sulayman al-Shadhakuni."
"3461","Al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn Shahriyar al-Misri narrated to us: Ali ibn Maymun al-Raqqi narrated to us: Ata ibn Muslim al-Khaffaf al-Halabi narrated to us, from Ismail al-Kufi, from Asim al-Ahwal, from Abu Uthman al-Nahdi, from Abdillah ibn Masud who said: A man trailing his cloak or garment passed by him, so he called him: O Abdallah, lift your garment, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever drags his clothes in arrogance, Allah shall not look at him regarding lawful or unlawful. Ismail al-Kufi is in my view Ismail ibn Abi Khalid; no one narrated it from Ismail except Ata ibn Muslim."
"3462","Al-Hasan ibn Muslim ibn al-Tayyib al-Sanani narrated to us: Abd al-Hamid ibn Subayh al-Sanani narrated to us: Yunus ibn Arqam narrated to us, from Harun ibn Sad, from Mundhir al-Thawri, from Muhammad ibn al-Hanafiyyah who said: I said to my father: Who are the best people after the Messenger of Allah? He said: Abu Bakr. I said: Then who? He said: Then Umar. No one narrated this hadith from Harun ibn Sad except Yunus ibn Arqam; Abd al-Hamid is alone in transmitting it."
"3463","Al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn Khalaf al-Darrab narrated to us: Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Abdillah narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir who said: A man's wound was brought before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: Treat it, and he gave a year respite. No one narrated this hadith from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah except Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Dhimari; Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman is alone in transmitting it."
"3464","Al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn Khalaf al-Darrab al-Dimashqi narrated to us: Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Dhimari narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir who said: A man who had stabbed another in the thigh with a horn was brought before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The one stabbed in the thigh said: Give me retaliation, O Messenger of Allah. The Messenger of Allah said: Treat it, and wait with it until we see what it becomes. The man said: Give me retaliation, O Messenger of Allah; he said the like to him. The man said: Give me retaliation, O Messenger of Allah; so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave him retaliation. Then the leg of the one who sought retaliation withered, while the one retaliated against healed, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) annulled its blood-money. No one narrated this hadith from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah except Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Dhimari; Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman is alone in transmitting it."
"3465","Al-Hasan ibn Hammad ibn Fudalah al-Sayrafi al-Basri narrated to us: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ghiyath narrated to us: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj ibn Artah, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas: Fatimah bint Umays narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) assigned her neither lodging nor maintenance. No one narrated this hadith from Ata except al-Hajjaj ibn Artah, nor from al-Hajjaj except Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad and Abu Shihab al-Hannat."
"3466","Al-Hasan ibn Hammad narrated to us: Yahya ibn Habib ibn Arabi narrated to us: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj ibn Artah, from Ata, from Abu Hurayrah who said: He forbade the earnings of the cupper and the dowry of the prostitute. No one narrated this hadith from Hammad ibn Zayd except Yahya ibn Habib ibn Arabi."
"3467","Al-Husayn ibn al-Sumayda al-Antaki narrated to me, he said: Musa ibn Ayyub al-Nasibi narrated to us, he said: Abdillah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Misar, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) freed Safiyyah and made her freedom her dowry. No one narrated this hadith from Misar except Ibn al-Mubarak; Musa ibn Ayyub is alone in transmitting it."
"3468","Al-Husayn ibn al-Sumayda al-Antaki narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Ayyub al-Nasibi narrated to us, he said: Ata ibn Muslim al-Khaffaf narrated to us, from al-Amash who said: Salim ibn Abdillah ibn Umar was sitting with al-Hajjaj, who said to him: Stand and strike this one's neck. Salim took the sword, took the man and headed for the palace door. His father looked at him heading with the man and said: Do you think he will do it - he sent him back twice or three times. When he went out with him, Salim said to him: Did you pray Fajr? He said: Yes. He said: Then take whichever road you wish. Then he came and laid down the sword. Al-Hajjaj said to him: Did you strike his neck? He said: No. He said: Why? He said: I heard this father of mine saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever prays Fajr is under Allah's protection until evening. His father said to him: Shrewd; we named you Salim only that you be safe. No one narrated this hadith from al-Amash except Ata ibn Muslim; Musa ibn Ayyub is alone in transmitting it."
"3469","Al-Husayn ibn al-Sumayda narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Ayyub al-Nasibi narrated to us, he said: Abu Ishaq al-Fazari narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Shaqiq ibn Salamah, from Urwah, from Aishah who said: I and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to wash from a single vessel. No one narrated this hadith from al-Amash, from Shaqiq, from Urwah, except Abu Ishaq al-Fazari; Musa ibn Ayyub is alone in transmitting it."
"3470","Al-Husayn ibn Mansur al-Rummani al-Massisi narrated to us, he said: Dawud ibn Muadh narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Warith narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Juhadah, from Sulayman al-Amash, from Abu Wail, from Khabbab who said: We emigrated with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and our reward fell upon Allah; among us were those taken (in death) without consuming any of their reward, including Musab ibn Umayr, killed on the day of Uhud, for whom nothing was found except a striped cloth: when his head was covered his feet showed, and when his feet were covered his head showed. That was mentioned to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: Cover his head with it and place idhkhir (grass) over him; and among us are those whose fruit ripened and they harvest it. No one narrated it from Muhammad ibn Juhadah except Abd al-Warith, nor from Abd al-Warith except Dawud."
"3471","Al-Husayn ibn Mansur al-Rummani narrated to us, he said: al-Muafa ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: Hakim ibn Nafi narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Uqbah narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Washing is a sa and ablution is a mudd. No one narrated it from Musa ibn Uqbah except Hakim ibn Nafi; al-Muafa ibn Sulayman is alone in transmitting it."
"3472","Al-Husayn ibn Mansur al-Rummani narrated to us, he said: al-Muafa ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: Hakim ibn Nafi narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Uqbah narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would sometimes contend with some of his wives over a single vessel, washing together."
"3473","Al-Husayn ibn Mansur al-Rummani narrated to us, he said: al-Muafa ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: Hakim ibn Nafi narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Uqbah narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar who said: A dead person died and they passed with him by the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and invited him to pray over him. He said: Is there a debt upon your companion? They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah, two dinars. He said: Pray over your companion. A man among his relatives said: It is upon me, O Messenger of Allah. He said: It is upon you, and he is free of it? He said: Yes. So the Messenger of Allah prayed over him. He met him later and said: What did you do? He said: I have not finished. He said: Cool (relieve) your companion, then hasten its payment. Then he met him and he said: I have paid it, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Now you have cooled your companion. No one narrated these three hadiths from Musa ibn Uqbah except Hakim ibn Nafi."
"3474","Al-Husayn ibn Humayd al-Akki al-Misri narrated to us, he said: Hamid ibn Yahya al-Taymi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Umar ibn Said ibn Masruq, from al-Amash who said: I heard Said ibn Jubayr saying: Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami narrated to us, from Abu Musa al-Ashari, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: None is more patient toward harm than Allah; they claim a rival for Him while He provides for them and grants them health. No one narrated it from Sufyan except Hamid ibn Yahya and al-Humaydi."
"3475","Al-Husayn ibn Humayd al-Akki narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Hisham al-Sadusi narrated to us, he said: Bakr ibn Abdillah al-Laythi narrated to us, he said: Rawh ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, from Abdillah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Among the best of your garments are white ones, so clothe your living in them and shroud your dead in them; and among the best of your kohls is ithmid, for it clears sight and grows hair. No one narrated it from Rawh ibn al-Qasim except Bakr ibn Abdillah al-Laythi."
"3476","Al-Husayn ibn Muhammad al-Harrani Abu Arubah narrated to us, he said: Hashim ibn al-Harith al-Harrani narrated to us, he said: Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Abu Abd al-Rahim, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah, from Fulayh ibn Sulayman, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Abdillah ibn Abi Qatadah, from his father who said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The best a man leaves after his death are three: a righteous child who supplicates for him, ongoing charity whose reward reaches him, and knowledge acted upon after him. No one narrated it from Zayd ibn Aslam except Fulayh, nor from Fulayh except Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah, nor from Zayd except Abu Abd al-Rahim; none narrated it well-authenticated except Abu al-Muafa; and it is not narrated from Abu Qatadah except through this channel."
"3477","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, he said: Hamid ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, from Sad ibn Abi Waqqas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If the son of Adam had two valleys of wealth he would wish a third to them; nothing fills the belly of the son of Adam except dust; and Allah turns to whoever repents. No one narrated it from Sufyan except Hamid ibn Yahya, nor from Ismail except Sufyan; and it is not narrated from Sad except with this chain."
"3478","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, he said: al-Ala ibn Amr al-Hanafi narrated to us, he said: Abdillah ibn Idris al-Awdi narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah shall grasp the earth on the Day of Resurrection while the heavens are folded in His right hand, then shake them, then say: I am the King. No one narrated it from Abdillah ibn Idris except al-Ala ibn Amr."
"3479","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Sahl ibn Uthman narrated to us, he said: Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from al-Hajjaj ibn Artah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: There is no marriage except with a guardian. No one narrated it from Ibn al-Mubarak, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, except Sahl ibn Uthman, from al-Hajjaj ibn Artah, from Ikrimah; and people narrated it from Ibn al-Mubarak, from al-Hajjaj ibn Artah."
"3480","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Harmalah ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Ibn Wahb narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to me, from Wuhayb ibn Khalid, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Abu al-Aliyah, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say in the Quranic prostration at night: My face prostrated to the One who created it and fashioned its hearing and sight. No one narrated it from Hammad ibn Zayd except Ibn Wahb, nor from Ibn Wahb except Harmalah ibn Yahya."
"3481","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Bahr narrated to us, he said: Qatadah ibn al-Fudayl ibn Qatadah al-Rahawi narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu Hadir, from al-Wadin al-Thaqafi, from Salim, from his father, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The poor of my ummah will enter Paradise forty autumns before their rich. I said: O Messenger of Allah, describe them to us. He said: They are those whose clothes are dirty, whose heads are disheveled, those who are not given permission at gates, and who do not marry luxurious women; they give all that is due upon them and are not given all that is due to them. It is not narrated from Ibn Umar except through this chain, and none narrated it except Ali ibn Bahr."
"3482","Al-Husayn ibn Ahmad ibn Mansur ibn Sajjadah narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Dahir al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Abd al-Quddus narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Ishaq, from Hanash ibn al-Mu'tamir, he said: I saw Abu Dharr al-Ghifari holding the two doorposts of the Ka'bah, saying: whoever knows me has known me, and whoever does not know me, I am Abu Dharr al-Ghifari; I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The example of my household among you is like the example of the ship of Nuh among the people of Nuh; whoever boarded it was saved, and whoever stayed back from it perished, and like the gate of Hittah among the Children of Isra'il. None narrated it from al-A'mash except Abdullah ibn Abd al-Quddus."
"3483","Al-Husayn ibn Ahmad ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Umar al-Waki'i narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Sulayman narrated to us, from Abu Ali al-Kahili, he said: Abu Musa addressed us and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed us and said: O people, fear shirk, for it is more hidden than the creeping of an ant. Then whomever Allah willed said: And how do we guard against it, O Messenger of Allah, while it is more hidden than the creeping of an ant? He said: Say: O Allah, we seek refuge in You from associating anything with You while we know it, and we seek Your forgiveness for what we do not know. None narrated it from Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Sulayman except Ibn Numayr, and it is not narrated from Abu Musa except through this chain."
"3484","Al-Husayn ibn Ja'far al-Qattat al-Kufi narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Muhammad al-Talhi narrated to us, he said: Dawud ibn Ata al-Madani narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When Jibril comes with revelation, the first thing he casts upon me is: In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate. None narrated it from Musa ibn Uqbah except Dawud ibn Ata."
"3485","Al-Husayn ibn Ja'far al-Qattat narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Layla narrated to us, from Abu Bakr ibn Ubaydullah ibn Anas, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is put in charge of any affair of the Muslims and then cheats them, he is in the Fire. None narrated it from Abu Bakr ibn Ubaydullah except Abu Layla, and it is not narrated from Anas except through this chain."
"3486","Al-Husayn ibn Muhammad ibn Hatim al-Ijl narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ammar al-Mawsili narrated to us, he said: al-Qasim ibn Yazid narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Mansur, from Mujahid, from Ubayd ibn Umayr, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: All flies are in the Fire except bees. None narrated it from Sufyan except al-Qasim al-Jarmi, and none narrated it from him except Ibn Ammar."
"3487","Al-Husayn ibn Muhammad ibn Hatim al-Ijl narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Muhammad al-Adhrami narrated to us, he said: al-Qasim ibn Yazid al-Jarmi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Umar ibn al-Khattab, he said: It is from the Sunnah to stop at al-Abtah on the evening of nafr. None narrated it from Sufyan except al-Qasim al-Jarmi."
"3488","Al-Husayn ibn Muhammad ibn Hatim narrated to us, he said: Abu Mus'ab narrated to us, he said: al-Mughirah ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Sa'id ibn Abi Hind, from Harb ibn Qays, from Abdullah ibn Abi Salamah, from Irak ibn Malik, from Abu Hurayrah: that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade dubba, hantam and naqir. We do not know of Abdullah ibn Abi Salamah narrating from Irak ibn Malik other than this, and none narrated it from al-Mughirah except Abu Mus'ab."
"3489","Al-Husayn ibn Muhammad ibn Hatim narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ammar al-Mawsili narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Ayyub narrated to us, from Mu'adh ibn Uqbah, from Ziyad ibn Sa'd, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A sick camel is not to be brought to a healthy one. It is not narrated from Ziyad ibn Sa'd except with this chain."
"3490","Al-Husayn ibn Muhammad ibn Hatim narrated to us, he said: al-Husayn ibn Ali ibn Yazid al-Suda'i narrated to us, he said: my father narrated to me, he said: Hafs al-Ghadiri narrated to us, from Musa al-Saghir, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever says: there is no god but Allah, it will benefit him one day of his life, even after punishment befalls him. It is not narrated from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah except through this chain."
"3491","Al-Husayn ibn Abdullah al-Kharaqi al-Baghdadi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Mirdas al-Ansari narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Marwan al-Uqayli narrated to us, he said: Umarah ibn Abi Hafsah narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah ibn Mas'ud, from Ibn Abbas, from Maymunah bint al-Harith, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) woke up heavy-spirited, and evening came while he was likewise, and morning came while he was likewise, so I said: O Messenger of Allah, why do I see you heavy? He said: Jibril promised me he would come to me, and he never broke his promise to me. Then they looked, and there was a puppy under a couch of theirs, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered that puppy to be taken out, and ordered that place to be washed with water. Then Jibril came, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: You promised me you would come to me, and you never broke your promise to me? He said: Do you not know that we do not enter a house in which there is a dog or an image? Thus Umarah ibn Abi Hafsah narrated it, from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah, from Ibn Abbas. And the companions of al-Zuhri narrated it, among them Yunus ibn Yazid and Sufyan ibn Uyaynah and others, from al-Zuhri, from Ubayd ibn al-Sabbaq, from Ibn Abbas, from Maymunah. None narrated it from Umarah ibn Abi Hafsah except Muhammad ibn Marwan."
"3492","Al-Husayn ibn Abdullah al-Kharaqi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Mirdas narrated to us, he said: Mahbub ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Muslim, from Sayyar Abu al-Hakam, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about these two surahs? He said: It was said to me, so I said, so say as I said. It is not narrated from Ibn Mas'ud except through this chain. People only narrate from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b."
"3493","Al-Husayn ibn Ahmad al-Maliki narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Sahm al-Antaki narrated to us, he said: Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, from Mis'ar ibn Kidam, from Sa'd ibn Ibrahim, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by us while we were picking the fruit of arak. He said: Take to the black thereof, for I used to pick it while I herded sheep. They said: Did you herd, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Yes, and there is no prophet but that he herded it. None narrated it from Mis'ar except Isa ibn Yunus, and none narrated it from Isa except Ibn Sahm, and it is not narrated from Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf except with this chain."
"3494","Al-Husayn ibn Sahl ibn Hurayth al-Misri narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, he said: al-Rabi' ibn Badr al-Tamimi narrated to us, he said: al-Jurayri narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Concerning the pregnant woman who fears for herself, that she break her fast, and the nursing woman who fears for her child. None narrated it from al-Jurayri except al-Rabi' ibn Badr."
"3495","Al-Husayn ibn Idris al-Tustari narrated to us, he said: al-Abbas ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated to us, he said: Mu'adh ibn Hisham narrated to us, he said: my father narrated to me, from Qatadah, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas: that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The mukatab is compensated, in proportion to what has been freed of him, with the blood-money of a free man, and in proportion to what remains enslaved of him, with the blood-money of a slave."
"3496","Al-Husayn ibn Bihan al-Askari narrated to us, he said: Sahl ibn Uthman narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Asim al-Ahwal, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whose two precious ones I take away, and he is patient and seeks reward, I am not pleased with a reward for him less than Paradise. None narrated it from Asim except Abu al-Ahwas, and none narrated it from Abu al-Ahwas except Sahl."
"3497","Al-Husayn ibn Bihan al-Askari narrated to us, he said: Sahl ibn Uthman narrated to us, he said: Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, from Idris al-Awdi, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Swearing promotes the merchandise and wipes out the earning. None narrated it from Idris al-Awdi except Hafs, and none narrated it from Hafs except Sahl ibn Uthman."
"3498","Al-Husayn ibn Muhammad al-Khayyat al-Ramahurmuzi narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Rashid al-Adami narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Bilal narrated to us, he said: Imran al-Qattan narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, he said: Ibn Umar once led the prayer, then said to a man from the people: Step forward and lead, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When one of you is a rizz, let him perform ablution. None narrated it from Imran al-Qattan except Muhammad ibn Bilal."
"3499","Al-Husayn ibn Ahmad ibn Bistam al-Za'faranI narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Ibrahim, the companion of al-Harawi, narrated to us, he said: my father narrated to us, from Abu Ka'b, the silk merchant, from al-Jurayri, from Abu al-Salil, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent al-Ala ibn al-Hadrami to Bahrayn, I followed him and saw three qualities in him, I do not know which of them is most amazing: we reached the seashore, and he said: Name Allah and plunge in. He said: So we named Allah and plunged in, and crossed, and the water did not wet except the lower parts of our camels' boots. When we returned we were with him in a desert land with no water with us, so we complained to him; he prayed two rak'ahs then supplicated, and there appeared a cloud like a shield, then it let down its spouts, so we drank and drew water. Then he died and we buried him in the sand; when we had gone a short distance we said: a beast will come and eat him, so we returned and did not see him. None narrated this hadith from Abu Ka'b except Ibrahim, the companion of al-Harawi, and none narrated it from al-Jurayri except Abu Ka'b. The name of Abu al-Salil is Durayb ibn Nuqayr."
"3500","Al-Husayn ibn Ahmad ibn Bistam narrated to us, he said: Abu Hurayrah Muhammad ibn Firas al-Sayrafi narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Abi al-Wazir narrated to us, from Musa ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from his father, from Shaybah al-Hajabi, from his uncle, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three things make your brother's love sincere to you: you make room for him in the sitting, you call him by the names most beloved to him, and you visit him when he is ill. None narrated this hadith from Musa ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr except Ibrahim ibn Abi al-Wazir."
"3501","Al-Husayn ibn Taqi ibn Abi Taqi al-Himsi narrated to us, he said: my grandfather Abu Taqi Hisham ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, he said: Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, he said: Abu Salih al-Qurashi narrated to me, from Safwan ibn Sulaym, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Hakim ibn Umayr, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah does not create a morning but that no angel in heaven nor on earth knows what Allah does on that day; and the servant has his provision, and if the two heavy ones, jinn and men, gathered against him to turn away anything of that from him, they could not."
"3502","Al-Husayn ibn al-Kumayt narrated to us, he said: Ghassan ibn al-Rabi' narrated to us, he said: Ja'far ibn Maysarah al-Ashja'i narrated to us, from Hilal Abu Diya, from al-Rabi' ibn Khuthaym, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Every loan is charity. None narrated this hadith from al-Rabi' except Hilal Abu Diya, nor from Hilal except Ja'far ibn Maysarah; Ghassan ibn al-Rabi' is alone in it."
"3503","Al-Husayn ibn al-Kumayt al-Mawsili narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ziyad ibn Farwah narrated to us, he said: Abu Shihab al-Hannat narrated to us, from Awf al-A'rabi, from al-Minhal ibn Amr, from Zad han, from al-Bara ibn Azib, he said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the funeral of a man from the Ansar; we reached the grave and had not yet entered it, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sat and we sat around him as if birds were upon our heads. Then he mentioned the hadith in full. None narrated this hadith from Awf except Abu Shihab; Muhammad ibn Ziyad ibn Farwah is alone in it."
"3504","Those named Hasnun: Hasnun ibn Ahmad al-Misri narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated to us, he said: Usamah ibn Zayd informed me, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: People are like a hundred camels among which you hardly find a riding camel. He said: And the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: We do not know anything better than a hundred like him except the believing man."
"3505","Those named Habab: Habab ibn Salih al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Harb al-Nasha'i narrated to us, he said: Umayr ibn Imran al-Hanafi narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Allah Almighty revealed to me that I marry my two daughters to Uthman. None narrated this hadith from Ibn Jurayj except Umayr ibn Imran; Muhammad ibn Harb is alone in it."
"3506","Habab ibn Salih al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Harb al-Nasha'i narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Yahya ibn Ubaydullah al-Taymi narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Uthman is in Paradise. None narrated this hadith from Ibn Jurayj except Isma'il ibn Yahya al-Taymi."
"3507","Habab ibn Salih al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Harb al-Nasha'i narrated to us, he said: Nasr ibn Hammad Abu al-Harith al-Warraq narrated to us, from Rawh ibn Janah, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The sick is not to be visited except after three days. None narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except Rawh ibn Janah; Abu al-Harith al-Warraq is alone in it."
"3508","Those named Hubab: Hubab ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hubab al-Tustari narrated to us, he said: Uthman ibn Hafs al-Tumani narrated to us, he said: Sallam ibn Abi Khubzah narrated to us, he said: Dawud ibn Abi al-Qassaf narrated to me, he said: Sa'id ibn Jubayr narrated to me, he said: I was walking with Ibn Umar when he passed by people who had set up a bird as a target, shooting at it, so Ibn Umar said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed whoever does this. Dawud ibn Abi al-Qassaf did not musnad any hadith other than this, and he is a trustworthy Basran shaykh."
"3509","Hubab ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hubab al-Tustari narrated to us, he said: Uthman ibn Hafs al-Tumani narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Kathir Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Zayd ibn Jud'an narrated to us, from al-Muhajir, the freedman of the family of Ziyad, he said: While I was upon a donkey of mine, my feet almost touching the ground due to the smallness of the donkey, I came upon the bald head of the Commander of the Faithful, Ali ibn Abi Talib, gleaming in the moonlight. I said: O Commander of the Faithful, where are you headed? He said: For a need of mine. I said: Will you not ride? He said: Yes. So I moved to the rear of the donkey and said: Ride, O Commander of the Faithful. He said: I will not, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The owner of the animal is most entitled to the front of the animal, and the owner of the horse is most entitled to the front of the horse. None narrated this hadith from Ali ibn Zayd except Yahya ibn Kathir, and al-Muhajir, freedman of the family of Ziyad, did not narrate from Ali any hadith other than this."
"3510","Those named Hajib: Hajib ibn Arkin al-Farghani narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Mufaddal narrated to us, he said: Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, he said: al-Mas'udi narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Ayman ibn Khuraym ibn Fatik, from his father, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What a good young man Khuraym is, if only he shortened his hair and raised his lower garment. So Khuraym said: My hair shall not pass my ears, nor my lower garment my heels. None narrated this hadith from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr except al-Mas'udi; Yunus ibn Bukayr is alone in it."
"3511","Hajib ibn Arkin al-Farghani narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Shu'ayb al-Kaysani narrated to us, he said: al-Khasib ibn Nasih narrated to us, he said: Hammad al-Fustat narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Hasan say, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: My close friend (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) advised me with three, which I will not abandon until I lay my right side down: that I not sleep except upon witr, that I fast three days in every month, and the Duha prayer. None narrated this hadith from Hammad al-Fustat except al-Khasib ibn Nasih, and he is a Basran shaykh who settled in Egypt."
"3512","Those named Hamalah: Hamalah ibn Muhammad al-Ghazzi narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Amr al-Ghazzi narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Abi Salamah al-Tinnisi narrated to us, he said: Zuhayr narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade that a woman be married upon her paternal aunt or her maternal aunt. None narrated this hadith from Musa ibn Uqbah except Zuhayr ibn Muhammad; Amr ibn Abi Salamah is alone in it."
"3513","Those named Humayd: Humayd ibn Ahmad ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Makhlad al-Wasiti al-Bazzaz narrated to us, he said: Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated to us, he said: Aghlab ibn Tamim narrated to us, from Jisr Abu Ja'far, from Ghalib al-Qattan, from al-Hasan, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever recites Ya-Sin in a day and night, seeking the Face of Allah, he is forgiven. None narrated this hadith from Ghalib al-Qattan except Aghlab ibn Tamim."
"3514","Those named Hamad: Hamad ibn Muhammad ibn Hamad Abu Nasr the scribe narrated to us, he said: Kurdus ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Mu'alla ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Fudayl ibn Marzuq, from Atiyyah al-Awfi, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, he said: Al-Abbas, uncle of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), was among those who guarded him; when this verse was revealed: O Messenger, convey what was sent down to you from your Lord, and if you do not, then you have not conveyed His message, and Allah will protect you from people, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) abandoned the guard. None narrated this hadith from Fudayl ibn Marzuq except Mu'alla ibn Abd al-Rahman, and it is not narrated from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri except with this chain."
"3515","Those named Hudhaqi: Hudhaqi ibn Humayd ibn al-Mustanir ibn Hudhaqi ibn Amir ibn Iyad ibn Mukharraq al-Ammi al-Lakhmi narrated to us, he said: my father Humayd ibn al-Mustanir narrated to me, from his maternal uncle, the brother of his mother, Khalid ibn Musa, he said: my father narrated to me, from his grandfather, from Ziyadah ibn Jahwar, he said: A letter from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to me, in it: In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate; from Muhammad, Messenger of Allah, to Ziyadah ibn Jahwar: peace be upon you; I praise Allah to you, there is no god but He. To proceed: I remind you of Allah and the Last Day. To proceed: every religion people profess shall be laid down except Islam, so know that."
"3516","Those named Hamzah: Hamzah ibn Muhammad the scribe al-Baghdadi narrated to us, he said: Nu'aym ibn Hammad al-Marwazi narrated to us, he said: Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, from Bahir ibn Sa'd, from Khalid ibn Ma'dan, from Jubayr ibn Nufayr, from Abu Tha'labah al-Khushani, he said: We campaigned with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and seized domestic donkeys, slaughtered and cooked them; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was informed, so he ordered a caller, who called among the people: The meat of domestic donkeys is not lawful; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade it. And they found onions and garlic in its gardens and ate thereof, and the people were hungry; they went in the evening, and the smell of the mosque was onions and garlic. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever eats this foul tree, let him not approach us in our mosque."
"3517","Hamzah ibn Dawud ibn Sulayman ibn al-Hakam ibn al-Hajjaj ibn Yusuf al-Thaqafi al-Ubulli narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Malik ibn Isa al-Ubulli narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Ash'ath al-Huddani narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A promise is a debt. None narrated this hadith from al-A'mash except Abdullah ibn Muhammad al-Huddani, and none narrated it from him except Sa'id ibn Malik, and it is not narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except with this chain."
"3518","Hamzah ibn Dawud al-Thaqafi al-Ubulli narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Malik ibn Isa al-Ubulli narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Ash'ath al-Huddani narrated to us, he said: al-A'mash narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad and Alqamah, from Ali ibn Abi Talib and Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, they said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A promise is a debt. Ali added in his hadith: Woe to whoever promises then breaks it, saying it three times. None narrated this hadith from al-A'mash except Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Ash'ath; Sa'id ibn Malik is alone in it."
"3519","Hamzah ibn Dawud al-Thaqafi narrated to us, he said: Ja'far ibn al-Nadr al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Asim narrated to us, from Sa'id al-Jurayri, from Abu Nadrah, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O people of Madinah, remember the Day of Salvation, saying it three times. They said: O Messenger of Allah, what is the Day of Salvation? He said: The Dajjal will come until he descends at Dhubab, and there will remain in Madinah no disbelieving man nor disbelieving woman, no polytheist man nor polytheist woman, no hypocrite man nor hypocrite woman, except they will go out to him; on that day the believers will be purified, so that is the Day of Salvation."
"3520","Those named Hajjaj: Hajjaj ibn Imran al-Sadusi, scribe of Bakkar the judge, narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Shadhakuni narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Umar al-Waqidi narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Abi Yahya informed me, from Sa'id ibn Abi Hind, from Dhakwan, freedman of A'ishah, from A'ishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had two garments he wore on his Friday; when he returned, we folded them up likewise. This hadith is not narrated from A'ishah except with this chain; al-Waqidi is alone in it."
"3521","Hajjaj ibn Imran al-Sadusi narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Minqari narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Umar al-Waqidi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Hamid ibn Ja'far informed me, from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Habban, from Yusuf ibn Abdullah ibn Salam, from his father, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, are we better or those who come after us? He said: If one of them spent the like of Uhud in gold, he would not reach the mudd of one of you nor half of it. This hadith is not narrated from Abdullah ibn Salam except with this chain; al-Waqidi is alone in it."
"3522","Hajjaj ibn Imran al-Sadusi narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Minqari narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Rashid narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Thabit ibn Thawban, from his father, from Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from his father, from his grandfather: that Busrah bint Safwan asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about a woman who puts her hand into her private part? He said: Ablution is upon her. None narrated this hadith from Ibn Thawban except Yahya ibn Rashid; Sulayman ibn Dawud is alone in it."
"3523","Those named Hafs: Hafs ibn Umar ibn al-Sabbah al-Raqqi narrated to us, he said: Abu Hudhayfah Musa ibn Mas'ud narrated to us, he said: Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, from Jarir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The fastest land to ruin is its left, then its right. None narrated this hadith connected except Abu Hudhayfah."
"3524","Hafs ibn Umar ibn al-Sabbah al-Raqqi narrated to us, he said: Qabisah ibn Uqbah narrated to us, he said: Isra'il narrated to us, from Hilal ibn Miqlas al-Sayrafi, from Abu Bishr, from Abu Wa'il, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever eats wholesome food, acts upon the Sunnah, and people are safe from his harms, will enter Paradise. They said: O Messenger of Allah, this is much among your ummah? He said: And it will be in generations after me. This hadith is not narrated from Abu Wa'il, from Abu Sa'id, except with this chain; Isra'il is alone in it."
"3525","Hafs ibn Umar ibn al-Sabbah narrated to us, he said: Fayd ibn al-Fadl al-Bajali narrated to us, he said: Mis'ar ibn Kidam narrated to us, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Abu Sadiq, from Rabi'ah ibn Najid, from Ali, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The imams are from Quraysh; their righteous are rulers of their righteous, and their wicked are rulers of their wicked, and each has a right, so give every possessor of right his right. And if an Abyssinian mutilated slave is appointed over you, listen to him and obey, unless one of you is given choice between his Islam and striking his neck; if given choice between his Islam and striking his neck, let him extend his neck, may his mother be bereaved of him, for there is neither world nor Hereafter after the loss of his Islam. None narrated this hadith from Mis'ar except Fayd ibn al-Fadl."
"3526","Hafs ibn Umar ibn al-Sabbah al-Raqqi narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Raja narrated to us, he said: Isra'il informed us, from al-Miqdam ibn Shurayh, from his father, from Urwah al-Bariqi, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Good is tied in the forelocks of horses until the Day of Resurrection. None narrated this hadith from al-Miqdam ibn Shurayh except Isra'il."
"3527","Hafs ibn Umar narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Raja narrated to us, he said: Za'idah informed us, from Bayan, from al-Sha'bi, from Masruq, from A'ishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave us choice, so we chose him, and it was not a divorce. None narrated this hadith from Bayan except Za'idah."
"3528","Hafs ibn Umar narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Raja narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Shu'ayb informed us, from Mansur, from al-Sha'bi, from Abu Burdah ibn Niyar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah Almighty detains the debtor for his creditor as severely as anything is detained upon anything, and he says: O Lord, how do I give him when You have gathered me barefoot naked, from where? So Allah Almighty says: I shall give them from your good deeds what you gave them, so it is cast upon the good deeds of the people; if there are any, otherwise I shall take from the evils of the people and cast them upon your evils."
"3529","Hafs ibn Umar narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Raja narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Abi Za'idah informed us, he said: Abdullah ibn Abi al-Safar narrated to us, from al-Sha'bi, from Urwah ibn al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, from his father, he said: We were on a journey, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: Do you have water with you? I said: Yes. He dismounted from his mount, then walked until he was hidden from me; when he came back I met him with the water vessel, so he performed ablution, washed his hands and washed his face. He wore a tight-sleeved Syrian cloak, so he brought his hand out from under the cloak and washed his forearms, and wiped his head. Then I bent toward his boots to remove them, and he said: Leave them, for I entered them while they were pure. So he wiped over his boots. None narrated this hadith from Abdullah ibn Abi al-Safar except Umar ibn Abi Za'idah; Abdullah ibn Raja is alone in it."
"3530","Hafs ibn Umar narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Raja narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Salamah ibn Abi al-Husam informed us, he said: Salih ibn Kaysan narrated to us, from Isa ibn Mas'ud ibn al-Hakam al-Zuraqi, from his grandmother Habibah: that she was with her mother, Bint al-Ajma, in the days of Hajj at Mina, when Budayl ibn Warqa al-Khuza'i came to them upon the mount of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and called out: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) says: Whoever was fasting, let him break his fast, for they are days of eating and drinking. This hadith is not narrated from Budayl ibn Warqa except with this chain; Abdullah ibn Raja is alone in it."
"3531","Hafs ibn Umar narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Raja narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Salamah informed us, he said: Rabi'ah ibn Abi Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from al-Qasim, from A'ishah, she said: There entered upon us on the Day of Sacrifice portions of cattle, so we said: What is this? They said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sacrificed cattle on behalf of his wives. None narrated this hadith from Rabi'ah except Sa'id ibn Salamah; Abdullah ibn Raja is alone in it."
"3532","Hafs ibn Umar narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Raja narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Salamah informed us, he said: Abu Bakr ibn Umar ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah ibn Umar narrated to me, from Ibrahim ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Rabi'ah: that he heard Abu Khunays al-Ghifari say: I went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the Tihamah campaign, until when we were at Usfan his companions came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, hunger has exhausted us, so permit us regarding the mounts to eat them. He said: Yes. Umar was informed of that, so he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Prophet of Allah, what have you done? You ordered the people to eat the mounts, then upon what will they ride? He said: What do you think, O son of al-Khattab? He said: I think you command them and you have the best opinion that they gather the surplus of their provisions in a garment, then you supplicate Allah for them, for Allah will answer you. So he ordered them, and they gathered the surplus of their provisions in a garment, then he supplicated Allah for them, then said: Bring your vessels. Every man among them filled his vessel. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted departure; when they departed it rained as Allah willed, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) dismounted and they dismounted with him, and they and the beasts drank from the water. Then he addressed them, and three men came; two sat with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and the other went away. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Shall I not inform you about the three men? As for one, he was shy, so Allah was shy of him; as for the other, he came repentant, so Allah accepted his repentance; as for the other, he turned away, so Allah turned away from him. This hadith is not narrated from Abu Khunays except with this chain. Abdullah ibn Raja is alone in it."
"3533","Hafs ibn Umar ibn al-Sabbah narrated to us, he said: Abu Hudhayfah Musa ibn Mas'ud al-Nahdi informed us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Ata, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is asked about knowledge and conceals it will be bridled with a bridle of fire on the Day of Resurrection. None narrated this hadith from Simak except Ibrahim ibn Tahman."
"3534","Hafs ibn Umar narrated to us, he said: Sa'd ibn Hafs al-Kufi narrated to us, he said: al-Minhal ibn Khalifah narrated to us, from Salamah ibn Tammam, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: We did not rejoice over anything after Islam as we rejoiced over a hadith the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrated to us. He said: The believer is rewarded for guiding to the path, for expressing in his tongue on behalf of the non-Arab, and for removing harm from the road, until he is rewarded for merchandise in his garment which he seeks with his hand and misses, so his heart throbs for it, then it is returned to him, and its reward is written for him. None narrated this hadith from Thabit except Salamah ibn Tammam al-Shaqari Abu Abdullah; al-Minhal ibn Khalifah is alone in it."
"3535","Hafs ibn Umar ibn al-Sabbah narrated to us, he said: Abu Ghassan Malik ibn Isma'il narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Salam ibn Harb narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abd al-Rahman Abu Khalid al-Dalani, from Abd al-Malik ibn Maysarah, from Zayd ibn Wahb, from Hudhayfah, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, is there evil after this good? He said: Yes, evil and tribulation. I said: Is there good after this evil? He said: Yes, a truce upon smoke, and a community upon filth therein. I said: Is there evil after this good? He said: Yes, a deaf blind tribulation, and callers calling to the Fire; to die, O Hudhayfah, biting upon a trunk is better than responding to any of them. None narrated this hadith from Abd al-Malik ibn Maysarah except Abu Khalid al-Dalani; Abd al-Salam ibn Harb is alone in it."
"3536","Those named Hatim: Hatim ibn Muhammad ibn Humayd Abu Adi al-Baghdadi narrated to us, he said: Yusuf ibn Musa al-Qattan narrated to us, he said: Asim ibn Yusuf al-Yarbu'i narrated to us, he said: Su'ayr ibn al-Khums narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a piece of gold, the first charity that came to him from a mine, and he said: What is this? They said: Charity from a mine of ours. He said: There will be mines, and in them will be the worst of Allah Almighty's creation. None narrated this hadith from Su'ayr except Asim ibn Yusuf."
"3537","Those named Huwayt: Huwayt ibn Ahmad ibn Hakim al-Dimashqi narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Nafi' narrated to us, from Jarir ibn Hazim, from al-Hasan, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever comes to Friday, let him bathe."
"3538","Those named Habbush: Habbush ibn Rizqullah al-Misri narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, he said: Yusuf ibn Abi Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir narrated to us, from Jabir ibn Abdullah: that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have wealth and dependents, and my father has wealth and dependents, and he wants to take my wealth to his wealth. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You and your wealth belong to your father. None narrated this hadith from Yusuf ibn Abi Ishaq except Isa ibn Yunus."
"3539","Habbush ibn Rizqullah narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: Salamah ibn al-Ayyar narrated to us, he said: Malik ibn Anas narrated to us, from al-Awza'i, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from A'ishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah loves gentleness in all matters. None narrated this hadith from Salamah except Abdullah ibn Yusuf."
"3540","Habbush ibn Rizqullah narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: Rushdayn ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Yazid, from Ibn Shihab, from Qabisah ibn Dhu'ayb, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Black banners will come out from Khurasan, nothing will repel them until they are set up at Iliya. None narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except Yunus; Rushdayn is alone in it."
"3541","Habbush ibn Rizqullah narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: Rushdayn ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Qurrah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Ibn Shihab, from Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im, from his father, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The severer of kinship will not enter Paradise. None narrated this hadith from Qurrah except Rushdayn."
"3542","Habbush ibn Rizqullah narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: Rushdayn ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Amr ibn al-Harith, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever is pleased to have his provision expanded for him and his lifespan extended for him, let him join his kinship. None narrated this hadith from Abu al-Zubayr except Amr ibn al-Harith; Rushdayn is alone in it."
"3543","Those named Hamid: Hamid ibn Sa'dan ibn Yazid al-Baghdadi narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: Anbasah ibn Khalid narrated to us, he said: Yunus informed me, from Ibn Shihab, he said: Abdullah ibn Urwah claimed that Abu Hurayrah said: I heard Sahl ibn Abi Hathmah say: I saw Bakr, the two sons of Mughaffalah, that companion of ours, while I was a boy, and I drew near him until he kicked me. Meaning: the judgment of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) concerning qasamah. None narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except Yunus, nor from Yunus except Anbasah ibn Khalid; Ahmad ibn Salih is alone in it."
"3544","Those named Hakim: Hakim ibn Yahya al-Mattuni narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn Rashid al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Ja'far al-Madini narrated to us, he said: Sa'd ibn Amr ibn Sulaym al-Zuraqi informed me, from his father, from Abu Qatadah ibn Rib'i, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would pray while carrying Umamah bint Abi al-As ibn al-Rabi', daughter of Zaynab daughter of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); when he bowed he put her down, and when he stood he carried her, until he finished his prayer."
"3545","Those named al-Hakam: al-Hakam ibn Ma'bad al-Khuza'i al-Asbahani narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi Umar al-Adani narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Majid ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Rawwad narrated to us, he said: Balhat ibn Abbad narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, he said: We complained to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the heat of the ground, and he did not relieve our complaint, and said: Increase in saying: there is no might nor power except with Allah, for it repels ninety-nine doors of harm, the least of which is worry. None narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir except Balhat, nor from Balhat except Abd al-Majid; Muhammad ibn Abi Umar is alone in it, and it is not narrated from Jabir except with this chain, and Balhat did not musnad any hadith other than this."
"3546","Those named Hamdan: Hamdan ibn Ibrahim al-Amiri al-Kufi narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn al-Hasan ibn Furat al-Qazzaz narrated to us, he said: Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Mas'udi narrated to us, from Kathir al-Nawwa and Abu Maryam al-Ansari, from Atiyyah, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: I am leaving among you the two weighty things: the Book of Allah, and my progeny, my household; they will not separate until they come to me at the Hawd. None narrated this hadith from Kathir al-Nawwa except Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Mas'udi."
"3547","Hamdan ibn Ibrahim al-Amiri narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn al-Hasan ibn Furat al-Qazzaz narrated to us, he said: Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Mas'udi narrated to us, he said: al-Harith ibn Hasirah narrated to us, from Abu Sadiq, from Rabi'ah ibn Najid, from Ali, he said: Those possessed of knowledge from the family of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and A'ishah bint Abi Bakr know so ask her that the companions of al-Aswad Dhu al-Thudayyah are cursed upon the tongue of the unlettered Prophet, and he who fabricates has failed."
"3548","Chapter of Kha, those named Khalaf: Khalaf ibn Amr al-Ukbari narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Attaf ibn Khalid al-Makhzumi narrated to us, he said: Siddiq ibn Musa narrated to me, from Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) arrived at Madinah, and his mount knelt with him between the house of Ja'far ibn Muhammad ibn Ali and the house of al-Hasan ibn Zayd. People came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, the lodging. Then his mount rose with him and he said: Leave her, for she is commanded. Then she went out with him until she brought him to the place of the minbar, and knelt with him; then she shifted, and people there had a trellis they sprinkled and maintained and cooled themselves in, until the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) dismounted from his mount and took shelter in the shade and alighted therein. Abu Ayyub came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, my house is the nearest of houses to you, so move your baggage to me. He said: Yes. So he took his mount to the house. Then another man came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, alight with me. He said: A man is with his baggage wherever it is. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stayed in the trellis twelve nights until he built the mosque. This hadith is not narrated from Ibn al-Zubayr except with this chain; Sa'id ibn Mansur is alone in it."
"3549","Khalaf ibn Amr al-Ukbari narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Shaybah, from the offspring of Ka'b ibn Malik, narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Kulayb, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The imam is a guarantor, so whatever he does, do. This hadith is not narrated from Jabir ibn Abdullah except with this chain; al-Humaydi is alone in it."
"3550","Khalaf ibn Amr al-Ukbari narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Mu'awiyah al-Naysaburi narrated to us, he said: Layth ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Abu al-Khayr, from Uqbah ibn Amir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever a man becomes Muslim at his hands, Paradise is due for him. None narrated this hadith from al-Layth except Muhammad ibn Mu'awiyah, and it is not narrated from Uqbah ibn Amir except with this chain."
"3551","Khalaf ibn Amr al-Ukbari narrated to us, he said: al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Salamah ibn Sisan al-Makki the tailor narrated to us, he said: Bishr ibn Ubayd narrated to me and he was an old shaykh he said: We were with Tawus at the Maqam when we heard a clamor; Tawus said: What is this? He said: People whom Ibn Hisham seized in a cause and shackled. Then I heard Tawus narrate from Ibn Abbas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is none who introduces an innovation in this ummah but that he will not die until that befalls him. Bishr ibn Ubayd said: I saw Ibn Hisham when he was deposed, and the workers of al-Walid ibn Abd al-Malik came and shackled him. This hadith is not narrated from Ibn Abbas except with this chain; al-Humaydi is alone in it."
"3552","Khalaf ibn Amr al-Ukbari narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Sulayman al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Azhar ibn Sinan narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Wasi' narrated to us, he said: I said to Bilal ibn Abi Burdah: Your father narrated to me from your grandfather: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: In Hell there is a valley, and in the valley a well called Habhab; it is binding upon Allah to house in it every stubborn tyrant. None narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Wasi' except Azhar ibn Sinan, and it is not narrated from Abu Musa except with this chain."
"3553","Khalaf ibn Amr al-Ukbari narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abbad al-Makki narrated to us, he said: Hatim ibn Isma'il narrated to us, from Bashir ibn al-Muhajir, from Abdullah ibn Buraydah, from his father, he said: The chief of the Copts gifted to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) two sisters, slave girls, and a mule. As for the mule, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to ride it; as for one of the two girls, he took her as concubine, and she bore Ibrahim; as for the other, he gave her to Hassan ibn Thabit al-Ansari. None narrated this hadith from Bashir ibn al-Muhajir except Hatim ibn Isma'il."
"3554","Khalaf ibn Amr al-Ukbari narrated to us, he said: Muslim ibn Abi Muslim al-Jarmi narrated to us, he said: Makhlad ibn al-Husayn narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Hassan, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked at a man gesturing with two fingers and said: Make it one, make it one. None narrated this hadith from Hisham ibn Hassan except Makhlad ibn al-Husayn; Muslim al-Jarmi is alone in it."
"3555","Khalaf ibn Amr al-Ukbari narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abdullah Abu Bakr al-Zuhayri narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Asim al-Kilabi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah and Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, they said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave Khadijah glad tidings of a house in Paradise of hollow pearl, in which is neither noise nor toil. None in this hadith said from al-A'mash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Sa'id, except Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad, and none narrated it from Abd al-Wahid except Amr ibn Asim; Abu Bakr al-Zuhayri is alone in it. And Isa ibn Yunus narrated it, from al-A'mash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah alone."
"3556","Khalaf ibn Amr al-Ukbari narrated to us, he said: al-Mu'afa ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn A'yan narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Ayyub, from Ibn Jurayj, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) bought from a Bedouin I think he said: from Banu Amir ibn Sa'sa'ah a load of khabat or a load of wheat; when the sale became binding he said to him: Choose. The Bedouin said: If I see like today, by your life, from whom are you? He said: From Quraysh. None narrated this hadith from Ibn Jurayj except Yahya ibn Ayyub; Musa ibn A'yan is alone in it."
"3557","Khalaf ibn al-Hasan al-Wasiti al-Mustamli narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Harb al-Nasha'i narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Yazid al-Wasiti narrated to us, from Mis'ar ibn Kidam, from Ibrahim al-Hajari, he said: I prayed with Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa over the funeral of a daughter of his, and he made four takbirs over her. Then he said: Thus I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) do. None narrated this hadith from Mis'ar except Muhammad ibn Yazid al-Wasiti; Muhammad ibn Harb al-Nasha'i is alone in it."
"3558","Khalaf ibn al-Hasan al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Khalaf al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Ishaq al-Azraq narrated to us, from Awf al-A'rabi, from Muhammad ibn al-Hanafiyyah, he said: I said to my father: O father, who is the best of people after the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Abu Bakr, then Umar. None narrated this hadith from Awf except Ishaq al-Azraq; al-Hasan ibn Khalaf is alone in it."
"3559","Khalaf ibn al-Hasan al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Shami narrated to us, he said: Suwayd ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, from al-Awza'i, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abdullah ibn Abi Qatadah, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The ruin of my ummah is in three: the Qadariyyah, partisanship, and narrating without verification."
"3560","Khalaf ibn Ubaydullah ibn Salm al-Dabbi al-Basri narrated to us, he said: Nasr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Ghalib ibn Qurran al-Hudhali narrated to us, he said: Abu Na'amah al-Adawi Amr ibn Isa narrated to us, he said: Hafsah bint Sirin narrated to me, from Umm al-Ra'ih bint Sulay', from Salman ibn Amir al-Dabbi, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): that he used to say: Charity of a kinsman upon his kin is charity and joining. None narrated this hadith from Abu Na'amah except Ghalib ibn Qurran; Nasr ibn Ali is alone in it."
"3561","Khalaf ibn Ubaydullah al-Dabbi narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Ali al-Sayrafi narrated to us, he said: Mu'adh ibn Hani al-Bahrani narrated to us, he said: Hammam narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Umm Muhammad, from A'ishah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not sleep by night nor day then wake except he used the siwak before performing ablution. None narrated this hadith from Ali ibn Zayd except Hammam, and it is not narrated from A'ishah except with this chain."
"3562","Khalaf ibn Ubaydullah al-Dabbi narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn al-Wadi ibn Nasr ibn al-Wadi al-Basri narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Abd al-Malik al-Rummani narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Walid al-Dabbi narrated to us, from Abu Bakr al-Hudhali, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The mu'adhdhins and those saying talbiyah will come out of their graves, the mu'adhdhin calling adhan and the mulabbi saying talbiyah. None narrated this hadith from Abu al-Zubayr except Abu Bakr al-Hudhali, nor from Abu Bakr except Abu al-Walid al-Dabbi and he is al-Abbas ibn Bakkar and it is not narrated from Jabir except with this chain."
"3563","Khalaf ibn Ubaydullah al-Dabbi narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn Yusuf al-Samti narrated to us, he said: my father narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Ishaq ibn Yahya, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no shighar. They said: What is shighar, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Marrying a woman for a woman, with no dowry between them. This hadith is not narrated from Ubayy ibn Ka'b except with this chain; Yusuf ibn Khalid al-Samti is alone in it."
"3564","Khalaf ibn Ubaydullah al-Dabbi narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn Yusuf al-Samti narrated to us, he said: my father narrated to us, from Abu Sufyan al-Sa'di, he said: I heard Abu Nadrah narrate from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, he said: It was said: O Messenger of Allah, do we pray witr after the dawn call? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Pray witr before the call. He said: The call of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was after the rising of dawn. They said: Do we pray witr after the call? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Pray witr before the call. They said a third time: Do we pray witr after the call? He said: Pray witr after the call. So he permitted them. None narrated this hadith from Abu Sufyan al-Sa'di except Yusuf ibn Khalid al-Samti; his son is alone in it from him."
"3565","Khalaf ibn Ubaydullah al-Dabbi narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn Yusuf al-Samti narrated to us, he said: my father narrated to us, from Abu Sufyan al-Sa'di, he said: I heard al-Hasan, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) advised me with ten rak'ahs which I do not abandon: two rak'ahs before dawn, two before noon, two after noon, two after sunset, and two after night prayer. None narrated this hadith from Abu Sufyan al-Sa'di except Yusuf ibn Khalid; his son is alone in it from him."
"3566","Those named Khadir: Khadir ibn Muhammad ibn al-Marzuban al-Jawhari al-Baghdadi narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Qattan narrated to us, he said: Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, he said: Malik ibn Mighwal narrated to us, from al-Hakam ibn Utaybah, from Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham, from A'ishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would go out to the dawn prayer with his head dripping from ghusl, then he would wake fasting."
"3567","Khadir ibn Muhammad ibn al-Marzuban narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Budayl narrated to us, he said: Mufaddal ibn Salih narrated to us, from Asim, from Zirr, from Safwan ibn Assal, he said: A Bedouin came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, a man loves a people but has not yet joined them? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man is with whom he loves."
"3568","Those named Khalid: Khalid ibn al-Nadr Abu Yazid al-Qurashi al-Basri narrated to us, he said: Nasr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Juwayriyah narrated to me, from Abdullah ibn Nahar, he said: Umm Sa'd narrated to me, she said: I entered upon A'ishah and said: O Mother of the Believers, a woman gives something from her husband's house as charity; is it hers or her husband's? She said: It is between them both; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrated it to me. This hadith is not narrated from A'ishah except with this chain; Nasr ibn Ali is alone in it."
"3569","Khalid ibn al-Nadr al-Qurashi narrated to us, he said: Nasr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Salamah ibn Harb ibn Ziyad al-Kilabi narrated to us, he said: Abu Mudrik narrated to me, he said: Anas narrated to me, he said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the mosque; when the sun rose the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out and I followed him. He said: Come with us to enter upon Fatimah bint Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So he entered upon her, and she was sleeping lying down. He said: O Fatimah, what makes you sleep at this hour? She said: I have been feverish since last night. He said: Where is the supplication I taught you? She said: I forgot it. He said: Say: O Living, O Sustainer, by Your mercy I seek help; set right for me all my affair, and do not entrust me to anyone of people nor to myself for the blink of an eye. This hadith is not narrated from Anas except with this chain; Nasr ibn Ali is alone in it."
"3570","Those named Khayr: Khayr ibn Arafah al-Tujibi al-Misri narrated to us, he said: Urwah ibn Marwan al-Raqqi narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Asim al-Ahwal, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: My intercession is for the people of major sins of my ummah. None narrated this hadith from Asim except Ibn al-Mubarak; Urwah ibn Marwan is alone in it."
"3571","Khayr ibn Arafah narrated to us, he said: Urwah ibn Marwan al-Raqqi narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Layth ibn Abi Sulaym, from Talhah ibn Musarrif, from Masruq, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Abusing a Muslim is wickedness, and fighting him is disbelief. None narrated this hadith from Talhah ibn Musarrif except Layth, nor from Layth except Isma'il ibn Ayyash; Urwah ibn Marwan al-Raqqi is alone in it."
"3572","Khayr ibn Arafah narrated to us, he said: Urwah ibn Marwan narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abd al-Karim al-Jazari, from Ata, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is not in the seven heavens a place of a foot nor a span nor a palm except in it is an angel standing, or an angel bowing, or an angel prostrating; when the Day of Resurrection comes they all say: Glory be to You, we did not worship You as You deserve to be worshipped, except that we did not associate anything with You. None narrated this hadith from Ata except Abd al-Karim, nor from Abd al-Karim except Ubaydullah ibn Amr."
"3573","Khayr ibn Arafah narrated to us, he said: Haywah ibn Shurayh al-Himsi narrated to us, he said: Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, from al-Zubaydi, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to give two salams. None narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except al-Zubaydi."
"3574","Khayr ibn Arafah narrated to us, he said: Urwah ibn Marwan al-Raqqi narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I am Ahmad, and I am Muhammad, and I am al-Hashir at whose feet people will be gathered, and I am al-Mahi by whom Allah effaces disbelief; when the Day of Resurrection comes, the banner of praise will be with me, and I will be the imam of the messengers and the holder of their intercession. None narrated this hadith from Jabir ibn Abdullah except Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, nor from Ibn Aqil except Ubaydullah ibn Amr, and al-Qasim, from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil."
"3575","Khayr ibn Arafah narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Abd al-Hakam narrated to us, he said: al-Layth ibn Sa'd informed us, from Khalid ibn Yazid, from Sa'id ibn Abi Hilal, from Sumayy, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: An accepted Hajj has no reward except Paradise, and two Umrahs expiate what is between them. None narrated this hadith from Sa'id ibn Abi Hilal except Khalid ibn Yazid, nor from Khalid except al-Layth."
"3576","Khayr ibn Arafah narrated to us, he said: Haywah ibn Shurayh al-Himsi narrated to us, he said: Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, from Ibn Thawban, from his father, from Makhul, from Waqqas ibn Rabi'ah, from al-Mustawrid ibn Shaddad, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever eats a meal at the expense of a Muslim man, Allah will feed him the like thereof from Hell; whoever is clothed a garment at the expense of a Muslim man, Allah will clothe him the like thereof from Hell; and whoever stands with a Muslim man in a station of repute, Allah will make him stand in a station of show and repute on the Day of Resurrection. None narrated this hadith from Ibn Thawban except Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid."
"3577","Khayr ibn Arafah narrated to us, he said: Hani ibn al-Mutawakkil al-Iskandarani narrated to us, he said: Abu Rabi'ah Sulayman ibn Rabi'ah narrated to us, from Abu Hazim, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: All matters, their good and evil, are from Allah. And he said: Qadar is the system of tawhid; whoever declares Allah one and believes in qadar has held to the firmest handhold, and whoever does not believe in qadar has broken tawhid. And he said: A denier of qadar will not enter Paradise. None narrated this hadith from Abu Hazim except Sulayman ibn Rabi'ah; Hani ibn al-Mutawakkil is alone in it."
"3578","Those named Khattab: Khattab ibn Sa'd al-Dimashqi narrated to us, he said: Mu'ammal ibn Ihab al-Ramli narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn al-Walid al-Adani narrated to us, he said: Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Shimr ibn Atiyyah, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Umm al-Darda, from Abu al-Darda, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever fasts a day in the path of Allah, Allah will place between him and the Fire a trench as between heaven and earth. None narrated this hadith from Sufyan except Abdullah ibn al-Walid al-Adani."
"3579","Chapter of Dal, those named Dawud: Dawud ibn Muhammad ibn Salih Abu al-Fawaris al-Marwarrudhi narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj al-Sami narrated to us, he said: Sallam ibn Abi Muti' narrated to us, from Jabir al-Ju'fi, from al-Sha'bi, from Yahya ibn al-Jazzar, from A'ishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever washes a dead person and fulfills the trust therein, meaning: conceals what occurs at that, will be of his sins as the day his mother bore him. She said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let him be attended by whoever is most knowledgeable; if there is none who knows, then a man whom you see possessing piety and trustworthiness. This hadith is not narrated from A'ishah except with this chain; Sallam ibn Abi Muti' is alone in it."
"3580","Dawud ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Khazzaz narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Abbad Abu Muhammad al-Zimmani narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Abi Arubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: All of you are shepherds and all of you are responsible; the ruler is a shepherd responsible for his flock, a man is a shepherd responsible for his wife and what his right hand possesses, a woman is a shepherdess over her husband's right, responsible for her house and children, and the slave is a shepherd over his master's right, responsible for his wealth. All of you are shepherds and all of you are responsible, so prepare an answer for those questions. He said: O Messenger of Allah, what is its answer? He said: Deeds of righteousness. None narrated this hadith from Qatadah except Sa'id; Isma'il ibn Abbad is alone in it."
"3581","Dawud ibn al-Sarh al-Ramli narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Hisham ibn Yahya ibn Yahya al-Ghassani narrated to us, he said: my father Hisham ibn Yahya narrated to me, from Urwah ibn Ruwaym, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from A'ishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is a link for his Muslim brother to one in authority, in conveying good or easing hardship, Allah will help him cross the Sirat on the Day of Resurrection when feet slip. None narrated this hadith from Hisham ibn Urwah except Urwah ibn Ruwaym al-Lakhmi; Hisham ibn Yahya al-Ghassani is alone in it, and none narrated it from him except his son Ibrahim."
"3582","Those named Dulayl: Dulayl ibn Ibrahim ibn Dulayl al-Asbahani narrated to us, he said: Ziyad ibn Ayyub Dalawayh narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Asim narrated to us, he said: Ibn Tawus narrated to us, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Not permitted in sacrificial camels and cattle: the one-eyed, the emaciated, the mangy, nor one whose udders are cut off."
"3583","Dulayl ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Isa Abu Abdullah al-Muqri narrated to us, he said: Thabit ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad al-Muharibi narrated to us, from Harb ibn Surayj, from Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ali, from Muhammad ibn al-Hanafiyyah, from Ali, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah has imposed upon the rich Muslims in their wealth what suffices their poor; the poor will not be strained except when they hunger and go naked due to what their rich do. Verily Allah will call them to account on the Day of Resurrection with a severe reckoning, and punish them with a grievous punishment."
"3584","Chapter of Dhal, those named Dhakir: Dhakir ibn Shaybah al-Asqalani narrated to us, he said: Rawwad ibn al-Jarrah narrated to us, from Abu al-Zu'ayzi'ah and Sa'id ibn Abd al-Aziz, from Makhul, from Urwah, from A'ishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would often say to me: O A'ishah, what have your verses done? I would say: Which of my verses do you mean, for they are many, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Concerning thanks. I said: Yes, by my father and mother; the poet said: his union. He said: Then he says: Yes, O A'ishah, when Allah gathers creation on the Day of Resurrection, He will say to a servant of His to whom a servant of His did a favor: Did you thank him? He will say: O Lord, I knew that was from You, so I thanked You for it. He will say: You did not thank Me, since you did not thank him through whose hands I brought it about. This hadith is not narrated from Makhul except through this chain; Rawwad ibn al-Jarrah is alone in it."
"3585","Chapter of Ra, those named Rawh: Rawh ibn al-Faraj Abu al-Zinba' al-Misri narrated to us, he said: Zuhayr ibn Abbad al-Ru'asi narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Ata narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever buys a musarrat sheep has the option; if he wishes he returns it with a sa' of dates. None narrated this hadith from al-A'mash except Yazid ibn Ata, nor from Yazid except Zuhayr ibn Abbad; Abu al-Zinba' is alone in it."
"3586","Rawh ibn al-Faraj Abu al-Zinba' narrated to us, he said: Yusuf ibn Adi narrated to us, he said: Asbat ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Mutarrif ibn Tarif, from Atiyyah al-Awfi, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever does not thank people has not thanked Allah Almighty. None narrated this hadith from Mutarrif except Asbat; Yusuf ibn Adi is alone in it."
"3587","Rawh ibn al-Faraj Abu al-Zinba' narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sulayman al-Ju'fi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, he said: Bayan narrated to us, from Abu Amr al-Shaybani, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked: Which deeds are best? He said: Prayer at its time, then dutifulness to parents, then jihad in the path of Allah. None narrated this hadith from Bayan except Muhammad ibn Fudayl, nor from Muhammad ibn Fudayl except Yahya al-Ju'fi."
"3588","Rawh ibn al-Faraj Abu al-Zinba' narrated to us, he said: Yusuf ibn Adi narrated to us, he said: al-Qasim ibn Malik al-Muzani narrated to us, from Asim al-Ahwal, from Anas ibn Malik: that Abu Taybah cupped the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he gave him his wage; had it been unlawful he would not have given it to him."
"3589","Rawh ibn al-Faraj Abu al-Zinba' narrated to us, he said: Yusuf ibn Adi narrated to us, he said: Ma'mar ibn Sulayman al-Jazari narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Hibban, from Mis'ar ibn Kidam, from Muhammad ibn Ziyad, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Does not one of you fear, when he raises his head before the imam, that Allah will turn his head into the head of a donkey? None narrated this hadith from Mis'ar except Zayd ibn Hibban, nor from Zayd ibn Hibban except Ma'mar ibn Sulayman; Yusuf ibn Adi is alone in it."
"3590","Rawh ibn al-Faraj Abu al-Zinba' narrated to us, he said: Yusuf ibn Adi narrated to us, he said: al-Qasim ibn Malik al-Muzani narrated to us, from Ash'ath ibn Sawwar, from al-Sha'bi, from Shurayh, he said: Umar ibn al-Khattab said: Do not be excessive in women's dowries, for had it been an honor in this world and the Hereafter, the most deserving of it among you and the first to it would have been Muhammad, Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and his household; he did not marry any of his wives nor marry any of his daughters for more than twelve uqiyyahs. None narrated this hadith from Shurayh except al-Sha'bi, nor from al-Sha'bi except Ash'ath ibn Sawwar, nor from Ash'ath except al-Qasim ibn Malik; Yusuf ibn Adi is alone in it."
"3591","Rawh ibn al-Faraj Abu al-Zinba' narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to me, he said: Umarah ibn Ghaziyyah narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Yuhannas, freedman of al-Zubayr, from Abu Hurayrah: that the Messenger (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When my ummah walks with swagger, and Persia and Rome serve them, some of them will be set over others. None narrated this hadith from Umarah ibn Ghaziyyah except Ibn Lahi'ah."
"3592","Rawh ibn al-Faraj Abu al-Zinba' narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us, he said: Ya'qub ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Zuhri narrated to me, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Abdullah ibn Umar, he said: Among the supplication of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the removal of Your blessing, the change of Your protection, the suddenness of Your vengeance, and all Your wrath. None narrated this hadith from Ibn Umar except Abdullah ibn Dinar, nor from Abdullah ibn Dinar except Musa ibn Uqbah; Ya'qub ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Zuhri is alone in it."
"3593","Rawh ibn al-Faraj Abu al-Zinba' narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us, he said: al-Layth ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): that he said: O Allah, whoever wrongs the people of Madinah and frightens them, frighten him, and upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels and all people; neither sarf nor adl will be accepted from him. None narrated this hadith from Musa ibn Uqbah except Hisham ibn Urwah; al-Layth ibn Sa'd is alone in it."
"3594","Rawh ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, he said: Yusuf ibn Adi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman al-Razi narrated to us, from Asim al-Ahwal, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a man placing his foot on the side of a sheep while sharpening his blade, and it was looking at him with its eyes. He said: Was this not before this? Do you want to kill it twice? None connected this hadith from Asim, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, except Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman; Yusuf ibn Adi is alone in it."
"3595","Rawh ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sulayman al-Ju'fi narrated to us, he said: my uncle Amr ibn Uthman narrated to us, he said: Abu Muslim, guide of al-A'mash, narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you cooks a pot, let him increase its broth, then give his neighbor thereof. None narrated this hadith from al-A'mash except Abu Muslim."
"3596","Rawh ibn al-Faraj Abu al-Zinba' narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sulayman al-Ju'fi narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Bashir al-Hamdani narrated to us, he said: Mujalid ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Wabarah ibn Abd al-Rahman: that he heard Ibn Umar say: A daughter of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fell ill, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Uthman: Stay with her, for she must have me or you, and you are most entitled. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left him behind with her; when Allah gave victory to him, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent giving him glad tidings that Allah had completed their number with you. None narrated this hadith from Wabarah except Mujalid, nor from Mujalid except Ahmad ibn Bashir; Yahya al-Ju'fi is alone in it."
"3597","Rawh ibn al-Farakh Abu Hatim al-Baghdadi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Zanbur narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Jabir narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, from al-Mustawrid ibn Shaddad, he said: al-Miqdad said: When we emigrated to Madinah, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) divided us ten by ten, and I was in the ten that were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). We had a sheep whose milk we drank among us; one night it was late for us, though we had set aside his share for him. I got up to it while hungry and drank it. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came, and I had not yet slept; he came to the vessel in which we put the milk and found nothing in it. I said: O Messenger of Allah, shall I not slaughter it for you? He said: No. None narrated this hadith from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid except Muhammad ibn Jabir; Muhammad ibn Zanbur is alone in it."
"3598","Those named Raja: Raja ibn Ahmad ibn Zayd al-Baghdadi narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Mani' narrated to us, he said: Yusuf ibn Atiyyah al-Saffar narrated to us, he said: Sulayman al-Taymi narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever leads a blind man forty cubits will have as the freeing of a slave."
"3599","Raja ibn Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Ahmad al-Dawraqi narrated to us, he said: Talq ibn Ghannam narrated to us, he said: Sharik and Qays narrated to us, from Abu Husayn, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Render the trust to whoever entrusted you, and do not betray whoever betrays you. None narrated this hadith from Abu Husayn except Sharik and Qays; Talq is alone in it."
"3600","Chapter of Za, those named Zakariyya: Zakariyya ibn Hamdawayh al-Baghdadi narrated to us, he said: Affan ibn Muslim narrated to us, he said: Hammam ibn Yahya narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you eats, let him lick his three fingers, for he does not know in which of them is blessing. None narrated this hadith from Qatadah except Hammam ibn Yahya; Affan is alone in it."
